local _, ns = ...

-- pagetext: English -> Danish. Entries already in ns.Exact (hand-made) are kept.
local names = {
    ["\"After the climax of the war and the Great Sundering of Kalimdor, the new reality of a world bereft of the sustaining magic on which our people depended quickly became apparent. The ruling house of Eldre'Thalas--House Tortheldrin--rapidly set plans in motion to ensure stability and continuity of our way of life. However, the methods they intended to employ left many deeply concerned.\""] = "„Efter krigens klimaks og Kalimdors Store Sønderrivelse blev den nye virkelighed i en verden berøvet den opretholdende magi, vores folk var afhængige af, hurtigt tydelig. Eldre'Thalas' regerende hus – Hus Tortelrin – satte hurtigt planer i gang for at sikre stabilitet og kontinuitet i vores levevis. Men de metoder, de havde tænkt sig at anvende, bekymrede mange dybt.“",
    ["\"I will continue to serve our people here on Zephras, and I will devote much of my time to furthering our relationship with the wind spirits to whom we owe so much. The elemental spirits are wondrous and wise, and we still have so much to learn from one another.\r\n\r\nI am devoted to seeing the shen'dorei persevere in this beautiful and strange realm--and to seeing that we do so freely, justly, and unshackled by tyranny.\""] = "„Jeg vil fortsat tjene vores folk her på Vindras, og jeg vil bruge en stor del af min tid på at fremme vores forhold til vindånderne, som vi skylder så meget. Elementarånderne er vidunderlige og kloge, og vi har stadig så meget at lære af hinanden.\r\n\r\nJeg er hengiven til at se shen'dorei holde ud i dette smukke og underlige rige – og til at se, at vi gør det frit, retfærdigt og ubundet af tyranni.“",
    ["\"In the days immediately following the turmoil at the Well of Eternity, there was much unrest in Eldre'Thalas. The demonic forces that poured from the Well nearly overwhelmed the beleaguered elvish kingdoms, ravaging the land and killing indiscriminately. If not for the intervention of the demigod Goldrinn and the sacrifice of countless kaldorei heroes, the kingdom of Eldre'Thalas would surely have been overrun and destroyed.\""] = "„I dagene umiddelbart efter uroen ved Evighedens Brønd var der stor uro i Eldre'Thalas. De dæmoniske kræfter, der strømmede ud af Brønden, overmandede næsten de hårdt pressede elverkongeriger, hærgede landet og dræbte uden skelen. Hvis ikke det havde været for halvguden Goldrinns indgriben og ofret fra utallige kaldorei-helte, ville kongeriget Eldre'Thalas uden tvivl være blevet overløbet og ødelagt.“",
    ["\"In the end, the worst of the destruction was narrowly avoided due to the rebels' intervention, but the price was steep. The battle claimed many lives on all sides, but the rebels suffered the greatest losses. \r\n\r\nThe Shal'nan himself was the only one to survive the final confrontation within Tortheldrin's sanctum. Those closest to the Shal'nan have widely documented that whatever injury he suffered in that last battle left him forever changed. In the centuries since those dark days, the Shal'nan has never spoken of what occurred, and he becomes withdrawn and wistful when asked.\""] = "„Til sidst blev det værste af ødelæggelsen lige akkurat undgået takket være oprørernes indgriben, men prisen var høj. Slaget kostede mange liv på begge sider, men oprørerne led de største tab. \r\n\r\nShal'nan selv var den eneste, der overlevede det afgørende opgør inde i Tortelrins helligdom. Dem, der stod Shal'nan nærmest, har i vid udstrækning dokumenteret, at den skade, han led i det sidste slag, forandrede ham for evigt. I århundrederne siden de mørke dage har Shal'nan aldrig talt om, hvad der skete, og han bliver indesluttet og vemodig, når man spørger ham.“",
    ["\"In the immediate aftermath of the battle, Tortheldrin's forces were scattered and disorganized. Most were occupied with securing the city once more, and this distraction allowed the remaining rebels to escape and regroup. With nowhere else to go, the Shal'nan marched what was left of his exhausted forces west, toward the coast.\""] = "„Umiddelbart efter slaget var Tortelrins styrker spredt og desorganiserede. De fleste var optaget af igen at sikre byen, og denne afledning gav de resterende oprørere mulighed for at slippe væk og samle sig igen. Uden andre steder at tage hen marcherede Shal'nan det, der var tilbage af hans udmattede styrker, mod vest, hen mod kysten.“",
    ["\"It's well documented since our ascent to Skywall that our people have adopted more lithe, slender forms, but this occurred over the course of many millennia. In contrast, the first recorded case of the Sky-Touched Blessing--which causes shen'dorei children to be born with vivid cerulean skin--was noted fewer than five generations ago.\r\n\r\nWithin a single generation of its first appearance, one child in twenty born among the Skyborne bore this curious alteration. Two generations later, that rate had doubled.\""] = "„Det er velkendt, siden vi steg op til Himmelmuren, at vores folk har antaget mere smidige, slanke former, men dette skete over mange årtusinder. Til gengæld blev det første dokumenterede tilfælde af den Himmelberørte Velsignelse – som får shen'dorei-børn til at fødes med livlig himmelblå hud – noteret for færre end fem generationer siden.\r\n\r\nInden for en enkelt generation efter dens første optræden bar et barn ud af tyve født blandt de Himmelbårne denne nysgerrige forandring. To generationer senere var andelen fordoblet.“",
    ["\"Much of the flora and fauna of the Skyborne Isles has been shaped by the elemental forces that reign here in the realm of Skywall. Many creatures once bound to the earth now bear avian traits such as beaks, talons, and feathers. Others have gained the power of flight, though such transformations remain less common than other outward changes.\r\n\r\nAmong the shen'dorei, the elemental plane's influence upon the body has been gradual and subtle. Yet in recent generations its effects have grown increasingly dramatic. Consider, for instance, the phenomenon now commonly called the \"Sky-Touched Blessing.\"\""] = "„Meget af floraen og faunaen på De Himmelbårne Øer er formet af de elementare kræfter, der hersker her i riget Himmelmuren. Mange væsener, der engang var bundet til jorden, har nu fugleagtige træk som næb, klør og fjer. Andre har fået flyveevnen, selvom sådanne forvandlinger er mindre almindelige end andre ydre ændringer.\r\n\r\nBlandt shen'dorei har det elementare planets indflydelse på kroppen været gradvis og subtil. Men i de seneste generationer er dens virkninger vokset støt mere dramatiske. Tag for eksempel fænomenet, der nu almindeligvis kaldes ‚Himmelberørt Velsignelse‘.“",
    ["\"Of late, the magisters of the High Order have grown increasingly wary of the wind spirits' motives, insisting that all powers and perils native to this realm must be better understood. Even if such dangers lie far from us now, the magisters maintain that such knowledge will better prepare us to face whatever may yet come.\""] = "„For nylig er magistrene i Den Høje Orden blevet stadig mere på vagt over for vindåndernes motiver og insisterer på, at alle kræfter og farer, der er hjemmehørende i dette rige, må forstås bedre. Selvom sådanne farer ligger langt fra os nu, mener magistrene, at en sådan viden bedre vil forberede os på at møde det, der måtte komme.“",
    ["\"On the eve of the planned summoning ritual, the Shal'nan and his forces struck. Seeing this as their final opportunity to thwart Prince Tortheldrin's reckless plan, they made a daring raid on the Prince's sanctum, intent on stopping the ritual.\r\n\r\nJust as the Shal'nan and the rebels feared, the poorly considered spell spiraled out of control and threatened to destroy the entire city center. \r\n\r\nAs the battle raged, wild magics tore through the streets, opening portals to the Nether itself and manifesting malevolent arcane monstrosities that preyed mercilessly upon the defenseless citizens of Eldre'Thalas.\""] = "„Aftenen før den planlagte kaldelsesritual slog Shal'nan og hans styrker til. De så dette som deres sidste chance for at forpurre Prins Tortelrins letsindige plan, og de foretog et dristigt angreb på Prinsens helligdom med det formål at standse ritualet.\r\n\r\nPræcis som Shal'nan og oprørerne havde frygtet, spiralede den dårligt gennemtænkte besværgelse ud af kontrol og truede med at ødelægge hele bykernen. \r\n\r\nMens slaget rasede, flængede vilde magier gennem gaderne, åbnede portaler til selveste Nether og manifesterede ondsindede arkane monstrositeter, der nådesløst jagtede de forsvarsløse borgere i Eldre'Thalas.“",
    ["\"Prince Tortheldrin grew frustrated, fearing that delays and debate would lead to the further deterioration of his kingdom. \r\n\r\nAs a result, his response to this resistance was swift and brutal. Over the course of a single bloody night, a purge was carried out that saw the complete destruction of dozens of noble houses. All who publicly opposed Tortheldrin were abruptly silenced, and entire lineages were destroyed overnight.\""] = "„Prins Tortelrin blev frustreret, da han frygtede, at forsinkelser og debatter ville føre til yderligere forfald i hans kongerige. \r\n\r\nFølgelig var hans svar på denne modstand hurtigt og brutalt. I løbet af en enkelt blodig nat blev der gennemført en udrensning, der så den fuldstændige udslettelse af snesevis af adelshuse. Alle, der offentligt modsatte sig Tortelrin, blev brat tavsgjort, og hele slægter blev udslettet over natten.“",
    ["\"Thank you for everything you've sacrificed, everything you've built, and everything you've taught me about how to be a better person. You all represent the unshakable resolve of the shen'dorei people. We will thrive in this beautiful new world and reach new heights together.\""] = "„Tak for alt, I har ofret, alt, I har bygget, og alt, I har lært mig om, hvordan man bliver et bedre menneske. I repræsenterer alle den urokkelige beslutsomhed hos shen'dorei-folket. Vi vil trives i denne smukke nye verden og sammen nå nye højder.“",
    ["\"The Prince railed against the idea of an alternative path to combat his people's dependence on magic. He claimed that calls to embrace naturalistic magic were propaganda spread by illegitimate usurpers to Queen Azshara's vacant throne. \r\n\r\nHe and his supporters dismissed druidic magic as base and barbaric--utterly beneath the proud, ancient traditions of the highborne. Yet the practice of druidism began to take hold on the fringes of Eldre'Thalas society, and with it, the rebellion continued to grow.\""] = "„Prinsen fór ud mod tanken om en alternativ vej til at bekæmpe sit folks afhængighed af magi. Han hævdede, at opfordringerne til at omfavne naturnær magi var propaganda, spredt af illegitime usurpatorer til Dronning Azsyras ledige trone. \r\n\r\nHan og hans tilhængere afviste druidisk magi som simpel og barbarisk – fuldstændig under de stolte, gamle traditioner hos de højtfødte. Alligevel begyndte druidismen at slå rod i udkanten af Eldre'Thalas' samfund, og med den voksede oprøret stadig.“",
    ["\"The leader of the rebels was a mysterious figure known only as the 'Shal'nan' or, 'The Veiled One.' He wore a featureless golden mask intended to conceal his identity and protect those close to him. This man quickly became a symbol for ordinary citizens who would stand up against oppression, and the word Shal'nan became a battle cry synonymous with rebellion.\r\n\r\nThrough sabotage, coercion, and--according to some rumors--assassination, the rebels quickly became a thorn in the side of Prince Tortheldrin's efforts to construct his network of crystalline foci.\""] = "„Oprørernes leder var en mystisk skikkelse, kendt blot som ‚Shal'nan‘ eller ‚Den Tilslørede‘. Han bar en ansigtsløs gylden maske, beregnet til at skjule hans identitet og beskytte dem, der stod ham nær. Denne mand blev hurtigt et symbol for almindelige borgere, der ville rejse sig mod undertrykkelse, og ordet Shal'nan blev et kampråb, synonymt med oprør.\r\n\r\nGennem sabotage, tvang og – ifølge nogle rygter – attentater blev oprørerne hurtigt en torn i siden på Prins Tortelrins bestræbelser på at opbygge hans netværk af krystallinske fokusser.“",
    ["\"The message of resistance spread by the Shal'nan began to gain traction within Eldre'Thalas, due in no small part to the very public embarrassment the Prince suffered nearly daily at the hands of rebel operations.\r\n\r\nAwareness of an alternative, more naturalistic way of life also spread quickly in the kingdom at this time. This was heavily influenced by the example set by the Cenarion druids, who had taken control of the greater kaldorei empire in the northern part of the continent. There were even rumors that the rebels were secretly supported by covert agents sent by the new de facto leader of the night elves: the Archdruid Malfurion Stormrage.\""] = "„Budskabet om modstand, som Shal'nan spredte, begyndte at vinde indpas i Eldre'Thalas, i ikke ringe grad takket være den meget offentlige forlegenhed, Prinsen næsten dagligt led under i hænderne på oprørsoperationer.\r\n\r\nKendskabet til en alternativ, mere naturnær levevis spredte sig også hurtigt i riget på denne tid. Det var stærkt præget af det eksempel, Cenarion-druiderne satte, og som havde overtaget kontrollen over det større kaldorei-imperium i den nordlige del af kontinentet. Der var endda rygter om, at oprørerne i hemmelighed blev støttet af skjulte agenter sendt af den nye de facto-leder af natteelverne: Ærkedruiden Malfurion Stormrasen.“",
    ["\"The skyseer elders among the Windshapers, by contrast, place implicit trust in the wind spirits and regard any questioning of their designs as an affront to our benefactors. They hold that our patrons in Skywall have already sacrificed much to bring us here and sustain us. They assert that if any further knowledge was vital to our survival, they would surely reveal it in due course. This difference in belief has given rise to no small measure of tension between the two orders.\r\n\r\nWhatever the truth may be, it is plain that we are not alone in this realm, and that many mysteries yet remain beyond our present understanding.\""] = "„Himmelseer-ældsterne blandt Vindformerne derimod har ubetinget tillid til vindånderne og betragter enhver stillen spørgsmål ved deres planer som en fornærmelse mod vores velgørere. De mener, at vores beskyttere i Himmelmuren allerede har ofret meget for at bringe os hertil og opretholde os. De hævder, at hvis nogen yderligere viden var afgørende for vores overlevelse, ville de uden tvivl afsløre den til sin tid. Denne forskel i overbevisning har givet anledning til ikke så lidt spænding mellem de to ordener.\r\n\r\nUanset hvad sandheden end er, står det klart, at vi ikke er alene i dette rige, og at mange mysterier endnu ligger hinsides vores nuværende forståelse.“",
    ["\"The terror of such brazen suppression caused a shocked silence to fall over the people of Eldre'Thalas. All discourse around Prince Tortheldrin's plan abruptly ceased... for a time, at least. Unfortunately for the Prince, the harder tyrants squeeze their people, the brighter the flames of resistance burn.\r\n\r\nThere were those who resolved to ensure our people did not repeat Queen Azshara's mistakes. A group of scholars formerly of the order of the Shen'dralar met in secret and formed a pact. Swearing to stop the Prince by any means necessary, they began to plant the seeds of rebellion.\""] = "„Terroren fra en så fræk undertrykkelse fik en chokeret tavshed til at lægge sig over folket i Eldre'Thalas. Al diskussion om Prins Tortelrins plan ophørte brat... i hvert fald for en stund. Uheldigvis for Prinsen gælder det, at jo hårdere tyranner klemmer deres folk, desto klarere brænder modstandens flammer.\r\n\r\nDer var dem, der besluttede sig for at sikre, at vores folk ikke gentog Dronning Azsyras fejltagelser. En gruppe lærde, tidligere af Shendralar-ordenen, mødtes i hemmelighed og dannede en pagt. Med ed på at standse Prinsen med alle midler begyndte de at så oprørets frø.“",
    ["\"The young Prince Tortheldrin intended to build a network of crystalline foci and use them to siphon and shape a new font of power for our people to draw upon. The point of contention for many was that he intended to use the very power that nearly destroyed our world to accomplish this. He meant to siphon this power from a demon world within the Twisting Nether itself. \r\n\r\nMany rightly feared this could open a new door through which demonic entities might gain once again access to our world.\""] = "„Den unge Prins Tortelrin havde til hensigt at bygge et netværk af krystallinske fokusser og bruge dem til at udsuge og forme en ny kilde til kraft, som vores folk kunne øse af. Det springende punkt for mange var, at han agtede at bruge netop den kraft, der næsten ødelagde vores verden, for at nå dette. Han ville udsuge denne kraft fra en dæmonverden inde i selveste Tvistende Nether. \r\n\r\nMange frygtede med rette, at dette kunne åbne en ny dør, hvorigennem dæmoniske væsener igen kunne få adgang til vores verden.“",
    ["\"There were those who loudly opposed the Prince's plan to channel a font of demonic energy to power his network of crystalline foci. Many of the detractors were members of outspoken noble families who attempted to use their influence to turn public sentiment against House Tortheldrin and the Prince's plan.\""] = "„Der var dem, der højlydt modsatte sig Prinsens plan om at kanalisere en kilde til dæmonisk energi for at drive hans netværk af krystallinske fokusser. Mange af kritikerne var medlemmer af frimodige adelsfamilier, som forsøgte at bruge deres indflydelse til at vende den offentlige stemning mod Hus Tortelrin og Prinsens plan.“",
    ["\"Thus, I am abdicating my position as your leader and handing over governance of our Skyborne Isles to a carefully chosen council of provincial elders. After the transition period is over, you will have the opportunity to choose your own leaders, and your voices will determine the direction we take from here on. \r\n\r\nYou have demonstrated the ability to lead yourselves better than any king, queen, prince, or other individual sovereign ever could--and that fills me with profound pride.\""] = "„Derfor træder jeg tilbage fra min stilling som jeres leder og overdrager styret over vores Himmelbårne Øer til et omhyggeligt udvalgt råd af provinsældste. Når overgangsperioden er forbi, får I mulighed for at vælge jeres egne ledere, og jeres stemmer vil afgøre den retning, vi tager herfra. \r\n\r\nI har vist en evne til at lede jer selv bedre, end nogen konge, dronning, prins eller anden enevældig suveræn nogensinde kunne – og det fylder mig med dyb stolthed.“",
    ["\"Today, three in ten children born on the Skyborne Isles have the striking complexion of the Sky-Touched. In recent centuries, the acceleration of our physical alterations has increased, and many scholars believe that the last vestiges of our kaldorei heritage may vanish entirely within two to three more generations.\r\n\r\nThe cause of this transformation may never be fully understood. Yet it is plain that, in making our lives within the elemental plane, we as a people are being changed by it in turn. Skywall is a realm of wonders, but this serves as a sober reminder that we still know perilously little of what such a place may work upon those not born to it.\""] = "„I dag har tre ud af ti børn født på De Himmelbårne Øer den slående hudfarve hos de Himmelberørte. I de seneste århundreder er accelerationen af vores fysiske forandringer tiltaget, og mange lærde mener, at de sidste rester af vores kaldorei-arv kan forsvinde helt inden for to til tre generationer.\r\n\r\nÅrsagen til denne forvandling vil måske aldrig blive fuldt forstået. Men det er klart, at vi, når vi skaber vores liv i det elementare plan, selv bliver forandret af det som folk. Himmelmuren er et rige af vidundere, men dette tjener som en nøgtern påmindelse om, at vi stadig ved forfærdelig lidt om, hvad et sådant sted kan udrette på dem, der ikke er født dertil.“",
    ["\"Whatever the truth may be, our benefactors clearly have no wish to speak of Al'Akir or his servants, and they are quick to dismiss all rumors of the Windlord's presence as idle fancy, unworthy of serious heed. They assure us that we need not trouble ourselves with such matters here, safe upon our Skyborne Isles. While this offers solemn comfort to many, it also raises a troubling question: what, precisely, are the wind spirits concealing from us?\""] = "\"Uanset sandheden, så har vores velyndere tydeligvis ingen lyst til at tale om Al'Akir eller hans tjenere, og de er hurtige til at afvise alle rygter om Vindherrens tilstedeværelse som tomt fantasteri, ikke værd at tage alvorligt. De forsikrer os om, at vi ikke behøver bekymre os om sådanne sager her, trygt på vores Himmelbårne Øer. Selvom dette giver mange en højtidelig trøst, rejser det også et foruroligende spørgsmål: hvad i alverden skjuler vindånderne for os?\"",
    ["\"When the beleaguered rebel army arrived at the port city of Eldre'narr, the magisters in control of the city had already heard of Tortheldrin's mighty rage--and of his standing order to kill any rebel found on sight. In an act of miraculous mercy, the magisters made no move to hinder the rebels' progress, allowing them to commandeer a number of ships without resistance.\r\n\r\nThe Shal'nan understood that this act of mercy would likely expose many in Eldre'narr to Tortheldrin's wrath. Even so, he accepted this unexpected gift with grace and, with a heavy heart, sailed his people west into the unknown.\""] = "\"Da den belejrede oprørshær ankom til havnebyen Eldre'nar, havde magistrene, der styrede byen, allerede hørt om Tortelrins vældige raseri – og om hans faste ordre om at dræbe enhver oprører, der blev set. I en handling af mirakuløs barmhjertighed gjorde magistrene intet for at hindre oprørernes fremmarch og lod dem kapre en række skibe uden modstand.\r\n\r\nShal'nanen forstod, at denne barmhjertighedshandling sandsynligvis ville udsætte mange i Eldre'nar for Tortelrins vrede. Ikke desto mindre modtog han denne uventede gave med nåde og sejlede med tungt hjerte sit folk mod vest, ud i det ukendte.\"",
    ["\"Who is Al'Akir the Windlord? The priests of the radical Al'Aketh would have us believe him to be the true ruler of Skywall, the realm we now call home. In their telling, we are but interlopers here, and one day Al'Akir shall appear before us to reckon with our trespass into his dominion within the elemental plane.\r\n\r\nThough such claims may at first seem the ravings of the misguided or the mad, there may yet be some measure of truth in them. When asked of Al'Akir's nature, the wind spirits grow evasive and agitated. Indeed, even the mere speaking of the so-called \"Windlord's\" name appears to cause them profound unease, perhaps even fear.\""] = "\"Hvem er Al'Akir Vindherren? Præsterne i den radikale Al'Aketh vil have os til at tro, at han er den sande hersker over Himmelmuren, riget vi nu kalder hjem. I deres version er vi blot indtrængere her, og en dag skal Al'Akir dukke op foran os for at gøre regnskab for vores overtrædelse ind i hans herredømme på elementarplanet.\r\n\r\nSelvom sådanne påstande ved første øjekast kan virke som den vildfarnes eller galmandens vrøvl, kan der alligevel være et vist mål af sandhed i dem. Når man spørger til Al'Akirs natur, bliver vindånderne undvigende og oprevne. Ja, selv blot det at udtale det såkaldte \"Vindherrens\" navn synes at volde dem dyb uro, måske endda frygt.\"",
    ["\"With the founding of our new home here in the clouds, we embark on a new age of peace and prosperity for our people.\r\n\r\nYou have all endured so much to make it here. I have watched our people grow into a hardy, self-reliant society, which fills me with a pride I cannot hope to describe in full.\r\n\r\nThe greatest part of that pride, however, is that it has become clear to me that I no longer have any need to act as our singular ruler.\""] = "\"Med grundlæggelsen af vores nye hjem her i skyerne går vi ind i en ny æra af fred og velstand for vort folk.\r\n\r\nI har alle udholdt så meget for at komme hertil. Jeg har set vores folk vokse sig til et hårdført, selvhjulpent samfund, og det fylder mig med en stolthed, jeg ikke kan håbe på at beskrive fuldt ud.\r\n\r\nDen største del af denne stolthed er dog, at det er blevet tydeligt for mig, at jeg ikke længere har nogen grund til at optræde som vores eneste hersker.\"",
    ["$n, you've got a good sword arm and I've taken notice. \r\n\r\nThings are a fine mess here on Zephras Isle, no doubt about it. We need our fighting shen'dorei in top form if we are to survive what's to come. It's time for you to stop playing at being a proper warrior, and actually become one.\r\n\r\nFind me inside the base of the watchtower here in Thendal Village. I'll see to it you are properly trained.\r\n\r\n\r\n-Blademaster Ren, Warrior Trainer"] = "$n, du har en god sværdarm, og jeg har lagt mærke til det. \r\n\r\nTingene står i en pæn rodebutik her på Vindras-øen, ingen tvivl om det. Vi har brug for vores kæmpende shen'dorei i topform, hvis vi skal overleve det, der kommer. Det er på tide, at du holder op med at lege at være en ordentlig kriger og faktisk bliver en.\r\n\r\nFind mig inde i basen af udkigstårnet her i Thendal-landsbyen. Jeg skal nok sørge for, at du bliver ordentligt trænet.\r\n\r\n\r\n-Klingemester Ren, Krigertræner",
    [". . .Giles, the boy, seems a bit rambunctious and will be a challenge to educate.  However the elder daughter, Tilloa, seems exceptionally smart.  I couldn't help but to notice her captivating beauty as well.  She is on the cusp of womanhood now.  Supposedly the Lord has arranged her marriage for next year.  But I digress.  This week I will accompany the family to their summer cottage near the Eastvale Logging Camp in Elwynn, close to the Red Ridge Mountains.  I hope to write more while there."] = ". . .Gilles, drengen, virker lidt vild og bliver en udfordring at uddanne. Den ældste datter, Tilloa, virker dog usædvanlig klog. Jeg kunne heller ikke lade være med at bemærke hendes fortryllende skønhed. Hun står nu på randen af kvindelighed. Herren har angiveligt arrangeret hendes ægteskab til næste år. Men jeg kommer ud ad en sidevej. Denne uge vil jeg ledsage familien til deres sommerhus nær Østdal Tømmerlejr i Elvendal, tæt på Rødryg-bjergene. Jeg håber at kunne skrive mere, mens jeg er der.",
    ["<A crude rendition of the landscape, with a clear point of interest indicated.>\r\n\r\nMogodun- z kost a-hine\r\nta golg\r\ngar thon- kha z'ta gor weard-hald\r\n\r\n<The map is in too poor of condition to make out any other writing.>"] = "<Et groft billede af landskabet, med et tydeligt interessepunkt markeret.>\r\n\r\nMogodun- z kost a-hine\r\nta golg\r\ngar thon- kha z'ta gor weard-hald\r\n\r\n<Kortet er i for dårlig stand til at kunne tyde nogen anden skrift.>",
    ["<As you touch the glowing crystal a draft of wind stirs around you, carrying the faint hint of spoken words.>\r\n\r\nThe High Order has been watching you, $n and we see great promise in your abilities.\r\n\r\nThe Wind Spirits have left Zephras Isle, and now more than ever, promising mages like yourself are needed. If our people are to find the self-reliance to survive this crisis, we must use our knowledge of the arcane to uncover the secrets of this realm.\r\n\r\nSeek me out in Thendal Village, on the ground floor of the great tree. We will begin your training in earnest.\r\n\r\n-Dorii Brightwhisper, Mage Trainer"] = "<Idet du rører ved den glødende krystal, river et vindpust rundt om dig og bærer det svage ekko af talte ord.>\r\n\r\nDen Høje Orden har holdt øje med dig, $n, og vi ser stort potentiale i dine evner.\r\n\r\nVindånderne har forladt Vindras-øen, og nu mere end nogensinde er lovende magikere som dig nødvendige. Hvis vort folk skal finde selvhjulpenheden til at overleve denne krise, må vi bruge vores viden om det arkane til at afdække hemmelighederne i dette rige.\r\n\r\nSøg mig op i Thendal-landsbyen, i stueetagen i det store træ. Vi begynder din træning for alvor.\r\n\r\n-Dorii Lysviske, Magiker-træner",
    ["<HTML>\r\n<BODY>\r\n<BR/>\r\n<BR/>\r\n<P>\r\nIn memory of my dear mentor, Horatio M. Montgomery, M.D. Healer, Teacher, Friend.\r\n</P>\r\n<BR/>\r\n<H1 align=\"center\">\r\n50 BTFT - 25 ATFT\r\n</H1>\r\n<BR/>\r\n<P>\r\n\"The world is full of the sick and weary. It is our job, as healers, NAY, as men and women of medicine, to cleanse them ALL of the 'itis.'\" \r\n</P>\r\n<BR/>\r\n<P>\r\n- H.M.M., M.D., PhD, JD, Grandmaster Farmer, Dancer Extraordinaire, Friend to the Animals\r\n</P>\r\n<BR/>\r\n</BODY>\r\n</HTML>"] = "<HTML>\r\n<BODY>\r\n<BR/>\r\n<BR/>\r\n<P>\r\nTil minde om min kære mentor, Horatio M. Montgomeri, dr.med. Helbreder, Lærer, Ven.\r\n</P>\r\n<BR/>\r\n<H1 align=\"center\">\r\n50 FFT - 25 EFT\r\n</H1>\r\n<BR/>\r\n<P>\r\n\"Verden er fuld af syge og trætte. Det er vores opgave, som helbredere, NEJ, som mænd og kvinder af medicinen, at rense dem ALLE for 'itis.'\" \r\n</P>\r\n<BR/>\r\n<P>\r\n- H.M.M., dr.med., ph.d., cand.jur., Stormester-Bonde, Ekstraordinær Danser, Dyrenes Ven\r\n</P>\r\n<BR/>\r\n</BODY>\r\n</HTML>",
    ["<HTML>\r\n<BODY>\r\n<H1 align=\"center\">ALLIANCE MILITARY RANKS</H1><BR/>\r\n<P align=\"center\">OFFICERS</P><BR/>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Grand Marshal</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Field Marshal</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Marshal</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Commander</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Lieutenant Commander</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Knight-Champion</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Knight-Captain</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Knight-Lieutenant</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Knight</P><BR/>\r\n<P align=\"center\">ENLISTED</P><BR/>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Sergeant Major</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Master Sergeant</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Sergeant</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Corporal</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Private</P>\r\n</BODY>\r\n</HTML>"] = "<HTML>\r\n<BODY>\r\n<H1 align=\"center\">ALLIANCE-MILITÆRE GRADER</H1><BR/>\r\n<P align=\"center\">OFFICERERE</P><BR/>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Storemarskalen</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Feltmarskal</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Marskal</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Kommandør</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Løjtnantkommandør</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Ridder-Mester</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Ridderkaptajn</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Ridderløjtnant</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Ridder</P><BR/>\r\n<P align=\"center\">MANDSKAB</P><BR/>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Sergentmajor</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Hovedsergent</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Sergent</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Korporal</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Menig</P>\r\n</BODY>\r\n</HTML>",
    ["<HTML>\r\n<BODY>\r\n<H1 align=\"center\">HORDE MILITARY RANKS</H1><BR/>\r\n<P align=\"center\">OFFICERS</P><BR/>\r\n<P align=\"center\">High Warlord</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Warlord</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">General</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Lieutenant General</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Champion</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Centurion</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Legionnaire</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Blood Guard</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Stone Guard</P><BR/>\r\n<P align=\"center\">ENLISTED</P><BR/>\r\n<P align=\"center\">First Sergeant</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Senior Sergeant</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Sergeant</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Grunt</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Scout</P>\r\n</BODY>\r\n</HTML>"] = "<HTML>\r\n<BODY>\r\n<H1 align=\"center\">HORDE-MILITÆRE GRADER</H1><BR/>\r\n<P align=\"center\">OFFICERERE</P><BR/>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Højkrigsherre</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Krigsherre</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">General</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Generalløjtnant</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Mester</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Centurion</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Legionær</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Blodvagt</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Stenvagten</P><BR/>\r\n<P align=\"center\">MANDSKAB</P><BR/>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Førstesergent</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Seniorsergent</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Sergent</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Fodsoldat</P>\r\n<P align=\"center\">Spejder</P>\r\n</BODY>\r\n</HTML>",
    ["<HTML>\r\n<BODY>\r\n<IMG src=\"Interface\\Pictures\\11733_blackrock_256\"/>\r\n</BODY>\r\n</HTML>"] = "<HTML>\r\n<BODY>\r\n<IMG src=\"Interface\\Pictures\\11733_blackrock_256\"/>\r\n</BODY>\r\n</HTML>",
    ["<HTML>\r\n<BODY>\r\n<IMG src=\"Interface\\Pictures\\11733_blasted_256\"/>\r\n</BODY>\r\n</HTML>"] = "<HTML>\r\n<BODY>\r\n<IMG src=\"Interface\\Pictures\\11733_blasted_256\"/>\r\n</BODY>\r\n</HTML>",
    ["<HTML>\r\n<BODY>\r\n<IMG src=\"Interface\\Pictures\\11733_ungoro_256\"/>\r\n</BODY>\r\n</HTML>"] = "<HTML>\r\n<BODY>\r\n<IMG src=\"Interface\\Pictures\\11733_ungoro_256\"/>\r\n</BODY>\r\n</HTML>",
    ["<You thumb through more of the bound paper and land on a diagram spread across both pages.>\r\n\r\nWeapons System Modifications\r\n\r\nIce Turret - Operational\r\nFlame Thrower - Operational\r\nElectro Pulse - Operational\r\nRadiation Spray - Operational\r\nAuto Rifle - Operational\r\nLaser Cutting Beam - EXPERIMENTAL\r\nSonic Cannon - EXPERIMENTAL\r\nPhase Ray - CONCEPT ONLY\r\n\r\nPage 34                                      Page 35"] = "<Du bladrer igennem mere af det indbundne papir og lander på et diagram, der strækker sig over begge sider.>\r\n\r\nVåbensystemmodifikationer\r\n\r\nIs-tårn - Operationel\r\nFlammekaster - Operationel\r\nElektro-puls - Operationel\r\nStrålingssprøjt - Operationel\r\nAuto-gevær - Operationel\r\nLaserskærende Stråle - EKSPERIMENTEL\r\nSonisk Kanon - EKSPERIMENTEL\r\nFasestråle - KUN KONCEPT\r\n\r\nSide 34                                      Side 35",
    ["<You touch the small white crystal and you can hear faint sounds on the wind. This is an audio recording of some sort.>\r\n\r\n\"An excerpt from the Shal'nan's speech at the groundbreaking ceremony for the Shrine of the Four Winds, Zephras Isle.\""] = "<Du rører ved den lille hvide krystal, og du kan høre svage lyde i vinden. Dette er en slags lydoptagelse.>\r\n\r\n\"Et uddrag af Shal'nanens tale ved første spadestik for Helligdommen for de Fire Vinde, Vindras-øen.\"",
    ["<You touch the small white crystal and you can hear faint sounds on the wind. This is an audio recording of some sort.>\r\n\r\n\"On The Windlord.\""] = "<Du rører ved den lille hvide krystal, og du kan høre svage lyde i vinden. Dette er en slags lydoptagelse.>\r\n\r\n\"Om Vindherren.\"",
    ["<You touch the small white crystal and you can hear faint sounds on the wind. This is an audio recording of some sort.>\r\n\r\n\"The Rebellion in Eldre'Thalas, Part 1\""] = "<Du rører ved den lille hvide krystal, og du kan høre svage lyde i vinden. Dette er en slags lydoptagelse.>\r\n\r\n\"Oprøret i Eldre'Thalas, Del 1\"",
    ["<You touch the small white crystal and you can hear faint sounds on the wind. This is an audio recording of some sort.>\r\n\r\n\"The Rebellion in Eldre'Thalas, Part 2\""] = "<Du rører ved den lille hvide krystal, og du kan høre svage lyde i vinden. Dette er en slags lydoptagelse.>\r\n\r\n\"Oprøret i Eldre'Thalas, Del 2\"",
    ["<You touch the small white crystal and you can hear faint sounds on the wind. This is an audio recording of some sort.>\r\n\r\n\"The Rebellion in Eldre'Thalas, Part 3\""] = "<Du rører ved den lille hvide krystal, og du kan høre svage lyde i vinden. Dette er en slags lydoptagelse.>\r\n\r\n\"Oprøret i Eldre'Thalas, Del 3\"",
    ["<You touch the small white crystal and you can hear faint sounds on the wind. This is an audio recording of some sort.>\r\n\r\n\"The Rebellion in Eldre'Thalas, Part 4\""] = "<Du rører ved den lille hvide krystal, og du kan høre svage lyde i vinden. Dette er en slags lydoptagelse.>\r\n\r\n\"Oprøret i Eldre'Thalas, Del 4\"",
    ["<You touch the small white crystal and you can hear faint sounds on the wind. This is an audio recording of some sort.>\r\n\r\n\"The Sky-Touched Mystery\""] = "<Du rører ved den lille hvide krystal, og du kan høre svage lyde i vinden. Dette er en slags lydoptagelse.>\r\n\r\n\"Den Himmelberørte Gåde\"",
    ["Aegwynn would never know that she had done exactly as Sargeras had planned. She had inadvertently sealed the fate of the mortal world, for Sargeras, at the time of his corporeal death, had transferred his spirit into Aegwynn's weakened body. Unbeknownst to the young Guardian, Sargeras would remain cloaked within the darkest recesses of her soul for many long years."] = "Ægwynn ville aldrig få at vide, at hun havde gjort præcis, som Sargerås havde planlagt. Hun havde uforvarende beseglet den dødelige verdens skæbne, for Sargerås havde ved sin legemlige død overført sin ånd til Ægwynns svækkede krop. Uvidende om det for den unge Vogter ville Sargerås blive gemt i de mørkeste afkroge af hendes sjæl i mange lange år.",
    ["Aegwynn, a fiery human girl, won the approbation of the Order and was given the mantle of Guardianship. Aegwynn vigorously worked to hunt down and eradicate demons wherever she found them, but she often questioned the authority of the male-dominated Council of Tirisfal."] = "Ægwynn, en ildfuld menneskepige, vandt Ordenens bifald og fik overdraget Vogterens kappe. Ægwynn arbejdede ivrigt på at jage og udrydde dæmoner, hvor end hun fandt dem, men hun satte ofte spørgsmålstegn ved autoriteten i det mandsdominerede Tirisfal-råd.",
    ["After a few months the superstitious peasantry began to suspect that their sorcerous rulers were hiding something terrible from them. Rumors of revolution began to sweep through the streets of Dalaran as the paranoid citizenry questioned the motives and practices of the magicians they had once admired. The Magocrats, fearing that the peasants would revolt and that Strom would take action against them, turned to the only group they felt would understand their particular problem: the elves."] = "Efter et par måneder begyndte den overtroiske bondestand at mistænke, at deres tryllende herskere skjulte noget forfærdeligt for dem. Rygter om revolution begyndte at feje gennem Dalarns gader, da de paranoide borgere satte spørgsmålstegn ved motiverne og metoderne hos de magikere, de engang havde beundret. Magokraterne frygtede, at bønderne ville gøre oprør, og at Storm ville tage affære imod dem, og vendte sig derfor til den eneste gruppe, de mente ville forstå deres særlige problem: alferne.",
    ["After a few years the majority of the orcish Horde had crossed into Azeroth, and Gul'dan deemed that the time for the primary strike against humanity had come. The Horde launched its full might against the unsuspecting kingdom of Stormwind."] = "Et par år senere var det meste af den orkiske Horde krydset over til Azerot, og Gul'dæn vurderede, at tiden for det primære angreb på menneskeheden var kommet. Horden satte hele sin styrke ind mod det uvidende kongerige Stormvind.",
    ["After seeing this my head grew light, perhaps from my recent injury (though I did not believe I had lost that much blood) or perhaps because I had finally, after so much frustration, uncovered one of the bloodstone's properties.  I reached behind me for my work stool and sat down, pondering.  Thoughts and questions raced through my head, dizzying and threatening to topple me.  \r\n\r\nDoes bloodstone drink blood?  Does it crave blood?  Does it attract blood?"] = "Efter at have set dette blev mit hoved lyst, måske på grund af min nylige skade (selvom jeg ikke troede, jeg havde mistet så meget blod), eller måske fordi jeg endelig, efter så megen frustration, havde afdækket en af blodstenens egenskaber.  Jeg rakte bagud efter min arbejdsskammel og satte mig ned for at grunde.  Tanker og spørgsmål susede gennem mit hoved, svimlende og truende med at vælte mig.  \r\n\r\nDrikker blodsten blod?  Higer den efter blod?  Tiltrækker den blod?",
    ["After the exiled Frostwolves charged through the portal, only a few orc clans followed. These orcs quickly set up a base of operations within the Black Morass, a dark and swampy area far to the east of the kingdom of Stormwind. As the orcs began to branch out and explore the new lands, they came into immediate conflict with the human defenders of Stormwind."] = "Efter at de forviste Frostulvene var stormet gennem portalen, fulgte kun få orkklaner med. Disse orker etablerede hurtigt en operationsbase i Det Sorte Morads, et mørkt og sumpet område langt mod øst for kongeriget Stormvind. Da orkerne begyndte at brede sig ud og udforske de nye lande, kom de straks i konflikt med Stormvinds menneskelige forsvarere.",
    ["Aided by his lieutenants, Uther the Lightbringer, Admiral Daelin Proudmoore, and Turalyon, Lothar was able to convince Lordaeron's demi-human races of the impending threat as well. The Alliance succeeded in gaining the support of the stoic dwarves of Ironforge and a small number of high elves of Quel'Thalas."] = "Med hjælp fra sine løjtnanter, Uther Lysbringer, admiral Daelin Stoltmoor og Turalyon, lykkedes det også Lotar at overbevise Herrelandes halvmenneskelige racer om den forestående trussel. Alliancen fik støtte fra de stoiske dværge fra Jernsmede og et lille antal højalfer fra Quel'Thalas.",
    ["Aku'mai, Princess of the Deep, serves the Old Gods.  She dwells in Blackfathom Deeps, blessing its caves with her ancient wisdom.   Brought to the Deeps by older mortals, Aku'mai is a symbol of divinity.  She has but a sliver of the Old Gods' power and savagery, and yet hers is still beyond measure.\r\n\r\nAnd so she is worshipped.  And she is feared, and loved.\r\n\r\n\r\n--Lorgalis"] = "Aku'maj, Dybets Prinsesse, tjener De Gamle Guder.  Hun bor i Den Sorte Afgrund og velsigner dets huler med sin oldgamle visdom.   Bragt til dybet af ældre dødelige er Aku'maj et symbol på guddommelighed.  Hun har kun en skerv af De Gamle Guders kraft og vildskab, og dog er hendes stadig uden for al målestok.\r\n\r\nOg derfor bliver hun tilbedt.  Og hun frygtes og elskes.\r\n\r\n\r\n--Lorgalis",
    ["Although Medivh had been defeated, the Horde continued to dominate the defenders of Stormwind. As the Horde's victory drew nearer, Orgrim Doomhammer, one of the greatest orc chieftains, began to see the depraved corruption that had spread throughout the clans since their time in Draenor."] = "Selvom Medivér var blevet besejret, fortsatte Horden med at dominere Stormvinds forsvarere. Da Hordens sejr nærmede sig, begyndte Orgrim Dømmehammer, en af de største orkhøvdinge, at se den fordærvede korruption, der havde bredt sig gennem klanerne siden deres tid i Draenør.",
    ["Although my colleagues in Dalaran were cautious to study the bloodstones that Kegan and his followers brought with them, instead quarantining the four refugees and leaving the bloodstones on their persons, the sincerity of Kegan obliged me to study his bloodstone pendant."] = "Selvom mine kolleger i Dalarn var forsigtige med at studere de blodsten, som Kegøn og hans følgere bragte med sig, og i stedet isolerede de fire flygtninge og lod blodstenene blive på deres person, forpligtede Kegøns oprigtighed mig til at studere hans blodstensvedhæng.",
    ["Am I going mad? Today I severed the head of one of my most trusted patrollers in order to get a better look at their soul. As I peered down their severed breathing passage, it occurred to me: I had not eaten anything in days!"] = "Er jeg ved at blive gal? I dag huggede jeg hovedet af en af mine mest betroede patruljerere for at få et bedre kig på deres sjæl. Mens jeg kiggede ned ad deres afhuggede åndedrætsgang, gik det op for mig: Jeg havde ikke spist noget i flere dage!",
    ["Aman'Thul, the Highfather of the Pantheon, bestowed a portion of his cosmic power upon the massive bronze dragon, Nozdormu. The Highfather empowered Nozdormu to guard time itself and police the ever-spinning pathways of fate and destiny. The stoic, honorable Nozdormu became known as the Timeless One."] = "Aman'Tul, Højfaderen af Panteonet, skænkede en del af sin kosmiske kraft til den enorme bronzedrage Nosdormu. Højfaderen gav Nosdormu magt til at vogte selve tiden og holde øje med de evigt snurrende stier for skæbne og bestemmelse. Den stoiske, ærefulde Nosdormu blev kendt som Den Tidløse.",
    ["An enormous dark visage appeared in the sky above Northrend. Sargeras, the demon king and lord of the Burning Legion, appeared before Aegwynn and bristled with hellish energy. He informed the young Guardian that the time of Tirisfal was about to come to an end and that the world would soon bow before the onslaught of the Legion."] = "Et enormt mørkt ansigt viste sig på himlen over Nordrend. Sargerås, dæmonkongen og herren over Den Brændende Legion, viste sig for Ægwynn og sprudlede af helvedesk energi. Han informerede den unge Vogter om, at Tirisfals tid snart var forbi, og at verden snart ville bøje sig for Legionens angreb.",
    ["Archmage Khadgar of the Kirin Tor\r\n\r\nFormer apprentice of Medivh. Supreme Commander of the Alliance Expedition that marched into the orc homeworld of Draenor. Presumed deceased. \r\n\r\nNever did one so selflessly delve into the dark heart of magic and warfare. We wish you well, bold wanderer. Wherever you are. \r\n\r\n- Antonidas - Archmage of Dalaran"] = "Ærkemager Kadgar fra Kirin Tårn\r\n\r\nTidligere lærling hos Medivér. Øverstkommanderende for Alliance-ekspeditionen, der marcherede ind i orkernes hjemverden Draenør. Formodentlig død. \r\n\r\nAldrig har nogen så uselvisk dykket ned i magiens og krigens mørke hjerte. Vi ønsker dig alt det bedste, modige vandrer. Uanset hvor du er. \r\n\r\n- Antonidæs - Ærkemager af Dalarn",
    ["As I waited for the results of these tests, I spent my time speaking to Kegan.  Although I constantly pressed him for what he knew about bloodstones, he never told me more than what he said the day he gave me his pendant.  And he did not often speak of his time within the fold of what he called \"the Forsaken,\" which is the name he calls his clan of undead."] = "Mens jeg ventede på resultaterne af disse tests, tilbragte jeg min tid med at tale med Kegøn.  Selvom jeg konstant pressede ham om, hvad han vidste om blodsten, fortalte han mig aldrig mere, end hvad han sagde den dag, han gav mig sit vedhæng.  Og han talte ikke ofte om sin tid inden for det, han kaldte \"De Forladte\", som er navnet på hans klan af udøde.",
    ["As Kil'jaeden prepared the Horde for its invasion of Azeroth, Medivh continued to fight for his soul against Sargeras. King Llane, the noble monarch of Stormwind, grew wary of the darkness which seemed to taint the spirit of his former friend."] = "Mens Kil'Dagen forberedte Horden til sin invasion af Azerot, kæmpede Medivér videre for sin sjæl mod Sargerås. Kong Llane, Stormvinds adelige monark, blev mistroisk over for mørket, der så ud til at besmitte sin tidligere venners ånd.",
    ["As a final incentive, Sargeras promised to bestow great power upon Gul'dan if he agreed to lead the Horde to Azeroth. Through Medivh, Sargeras told the warlock that he could become a living god if he found the undersea tomb where the Guardian Aegwynn had placed Sargeras' crippled body nearly a thousand years before."] = "Som et sidste incitament lovede Sargerås at skænke Gul'dæn stor magt, hvis han gik med til at føre Horden til Azerot. Gennem Medivér fortalte Sargerås hekseriateren, at han kunne blive en levende gud, hvis han fandt den undersøiske gravkrypt, hvor Vogteren Ægwynn næsten tusind år tidligere havde lagt Sargerås' forkrøblede krop.",
    ["As doubt and despair overwhelmed Sargeras' senses, he lost all faith not only in his mission, but also in the Titans' vision of an ordered universe. Eventually he came to believe that the concept of order itself was folly, and that chaos and depravity were the only absolutes within the dark, lonely universe."] = "Da tvivl og fortvivlelse overvældede Sargerås' sanser, mistede han al tro, ikke kun på sin mission, men også på titanernes vision om et ordnet univers. Til sidst kom han til at tro, at selve begrebet orden var dårskab, og at kaos og fordærv var de eneste absolutter i det mørke, ensomme univers.",
    ["As her mastery over the cosmic power of Tirisfal grew, Aegwynn became aware of a number of powerful demons that stalked the icy northern continent of Northrend. Traveling to the distant north, Aegwynn tracked the demons into the mountains. There, she found that the demons were hunting one of the last surviving dragonflights and draining the ancient creatures of their innate magic."] = "Efterhånden som hendes beherskelse af Tirisfals kosmiske kraft voksede, blev Ægwynn opmærksom på en række mægtige dæmoner, der strejfede rundt på det iskolde nordlige kontinent Nordrend. Hun rejste mod det fjerne nord og fulgte dæmonerne op i bjergene. Der fandt hun ud af, at dæmonerne jagtede en af de sidste overlevende drageflyvninger og drænede de gamle væsener for deres medfødte magi.",
    ["As she confronted the enemy warriors, Modgud used her powers to strike fear into their hearts. Shadows moved at her command, and dark things crawled up from the depths of the earth to stalk the Wildhammers in their own halls. Eventually Modgud broke through the gates and laid siege to the fortress itself. The Wildhammers fought desperately, Khardros himself wading through the roiling masses to slay the sorceress queen."] = "Da hun stod over for fjendens krigere, brugte Modgud sine kræfter til at jage frygt ind i deres hjerter. Skygger rørte sig efter hendes befaling, og mørke ting kravlede op fra jordens dybder for at liste rundt efter Vildhamrene i deres egne haller. Til sidst brød Modgud gennem portene og lagde selve fæstningen under belejring. Vildhamrene kæmpede desperat, og Khardros selv vadede gennem de vrimlende masser for at slå trylledronningen ihjel.",
    ["As soon as the fighting stopped, they started moving massive crates of windstones to the top of the tower. The leader, some kind of priest, said something about a ritual.\r\n\r\nI'm writing this note just in case I don't make it back to Shen'dar to warn Aonda, but they are doing something here. Something bad."] = "Så snart kampene var slut, begyndte de at flytte enorme kasser med vindsten op til toppen af tårnet. Lederen, en slags præst, sagde noget om et ritual.\r\n\r\nJeg skriver dette notat for en sikkerheds skyld, hvis jeg ikke når tilbage til Shen'dar for at advare Aonda, men de gør noget her. Noget ondt.",
    ["As the Titans made their way across the primordial landscape, they encountered a number of hostile elemental beings. These elementals, who worshipped a race of unfathomably evil beings known only as the Old Gods, vowed to drive the Titans back and keep their world inviolate from the invaders' metallic touch."] = "Mens Titanerne bevægede sig hen over det urgamle landskab, stødte de på en række fjendtlige elementarvæsener. Disse elementarer, der tilbad en race af ufatteligt onde væsener kendt som De Gamle Guder, svor at drive Titanerne tilbage og holde deres verden ukrænket for angribernes metalliske berøring.",
    ["As the battle raged across the burning fields of Kalimdor, a terrible turn of events unfolded. The details of the event have been lost to time, but it is known that Neltharion, the Dragon Aspect of the Earth, went mad during a critical engagement against the Burning Legion. He began to split apart as flame and rage erupted from his dark hide. Renaming himself Deathwing, the burning dragon turned on his brethren and drove the five dragonflights from the field of battle."] = "Mens slaget rasede over Kalimdørs brændende marker, tog begivenhederne en forfærdelig drejning. Detaljerne om begivenheden er gået tabt med tiden, men det vides, at Neltharion, Jordens Drage-aspekt, blev vanvittig under et afgørende slag mod Brændende Legion. Han begyndte at splittes ad, mens flamme og raseri brød ud af hans mørke hud. Den brændende drage omdøbte sig selv til Dødsvinge, vendte sig mod sine brødre og drev de fem drageflyvninger væk fra slagmarken.",
    ["As the empire grew and expanded into new lands, the young magicians also spread out into the southlands. Wielding their mystical powers, the magicians protected their brethren from the wild creatures of the land and made it possible for new city-states to be constructed in the wilderness. Yet, as their powers grew, the magicians became ever more conceited and isolated from the rest of society."] = "Efterhånden som imperiet voksede og bredte sig ud i nye lande, spredte de unge magikere sig også ud i sydlandene. Med deres mystiske kræfter beskyttede magikerne deres brødre mod landets vilde væsener og gjorde det muligt at bygge nye bystater ude i ødemarken. Men efterhånden som deres kræfter voksede, blev magikerne stadig mere indbildske og isolerede sig fra resten af samfundet.",
    ["As the forces of Azeroth and the Horde clashed across the kingdom, internal conflicts began to take their toll on both armies. King Llane, who believed the bestial orcs to be incapable of conquering Azeroth, contemptuously held his position at his capital of Stormwind. However, Sir Lothar became convinced that the battle should be taken directly to the enemy, and he was forced to choose between his convictions and his loyalty to the king."] = "Mens Azerots og Hordens styrker stødte sammen over hele riget, begyndte interne stridigheder at tage deres tribut af begge hære. Kong Llane, der mente, at de dyriske orker var ude af stand til at erobre Azerot, holdt foragteligt sin position i hovedstaden Stormvind. Ridder Lotar blev dog overbevist om, at slaget måtte føres direkte ind i fjendens lejr, og han blev tvunget til at vælge mellem sine overbevisninger og sin loyalitet over for kongen.",
    ["As the generations passed, Guardians defended the masses of humanity from the invisible threat of the Burning Legion throughout the lands of Arathor and Quel'Thalas. Arathor grew and prospered while the use of magic spread throughout the empire. Meanwhile, the Guardians kept careful watch for signs of demonic activity."] = "Gennem generationerne forsvarede Vogterne menneskemasserne mod Brændende Legions usynlige trussel over hele Arators og Quel'Thalas' lande. Arator voksede og trivedes, mens brugen af magi bredte sig over hele imperiet. Imens holdt Vogterne nøje øje med tegn på dæmonisk aktivitet.",
    ["As the high elves fought for their lives against the trolls' fierce onslaught, the scattered, nomadic humans of Lordaeron fought to consolidate their own tribal lands. The tribes of early humanity raided each other's settlements with little heed for racial unification or honor."] = "Mens højalferne kæmpede for deres liv mod trollernes voldsomme angreb, kæmpede de spredte, nomadiske mennesker i Herrelande for at samle deres egne stammeområder. Stammerne fra den tidlige menneskehed overfaldt hinandens bosættelser med ringe hensyn til racemæssig enhed eller ære.",
    ["As the politics and rivalries of the seven human nations waxed and waned, the line of Guardians kept its constant vigil against chaos. There were many Guardians over the years, but only one ever held the magical powers of Tirisfal at any given time. One of the last Guardians of the age distinguished herself as a mighty warrior against the shadow."] = "Mens de syv menneskelige nationers politik og rivaliseringer svandt og tog til, holdt Vogternes række konstant vagt mod kaos. Der var mange Vogtere gennem årene, men kun én ad gangen besad nogensinde Tirisfals magiske kræfter. En af de sidste Vogtere i sin tidsalder udmærkede sig som en mægtig kriger mod skyggen.",
    ["As the titanic battle raged around Azshara's capital city, the delusional queen waited in anticipation for Sargeras' arrival. The lord of the Legion was preparing to pass through the Well of Eternity and enter the ravaged world. As his impossibly huge shadow drew ever closer to the Well's surface, Azshara gathered the most powerful of her Highborne followers. Only by linking their magics together in one focused spell would they be able to create a gateway large enough for Sargeras to enter."] = "Mens det titaniske slag rasede omkring Azsyras hovedstad, ventede den vrangforestillede dronning i spænding på Sargerås' ankomst. Legionens herre var ved at passere Evighedens Brønd og træde ind i den hærgede verden. Efterhånden som hans umuligt store skygge kom tættere og tættere på brøndens overflade, samlede Azsyra de mest mægtige af sine højfødte følgere. Kun ved at forbinde deres magi i én fokuseret besværgelse kunne de skabe en port stor nok til, at Sargerås kunne træde igennem.",
    ["As the troll armies broke and attempted to flee, Thoradin's armies ran them down and slaughtered every last one of their soldiers. The trolls would never fully recover from their defeat, and history would never see the trolls rise as one nation again. Assured that Quel'Thalas was saved from destruction, the elves made a pledge of loyalty and friendship to the nation of Arathor and to the bloodline of its king, Thoradin. Humans and elves would nurture peaceful relations for ages to come."] = "Da trollehærene brød sammen og forsøgte at flygte, jagede Torradins hære dem ned og slagtede hver eneste af deres soldater. Trollerne ville aldrig komme helt over nederlaget, og historien ville aldrig se trollerne rejse sig som én nation igen. Efter at være blevet forsikret om, at Quel'Thalas var reddet fra undergang, svor alferne troskab og venskab til Arators nation og til kongens, Torradins, blodslinje. Mennesker og alfer ville pleje fredelige relationer i tidsaldre fremover.",
    ["As twilight fell on the final day of their labors, the Titans named the continent Kalimdor: \"land of eternal starlight\"."] = "Da tusmørket faldt på den sidste dag af deres slid, navngav Titanerne kontinentet Kalimdør: \"Det evige stjernelysets land\".",
    ["Aside from their shadowy origins, it is clear that the night elves came to power soon after their discovery of the Well of Eternity. Despite the trolls' attempts to keep them from expanding their territories, the night elves built up a mighty empire that expanded rapidly across primordial Kalimdor. Wielding fierce magics never before imagined by the superstitious trolls, the night elves had little trouble doing what the evil aqir could never do: topple the two greatest empires in the world."] = "Bortset fra deres skyggefulde oprindelse står det klart, at nattealferne kom til magten kort efter, at de opdagede Evighedens Brønd. Til trods for trollernes forsøg på at holde dem fra at udvide deres territorier, opbyggede nattealferne et mægtigt imperium, der hurtigt bredte sig over det urgamle Kalimdør. Ved at svinge vilde magier, som de overtroiske trolde aldrig havde forestillet sig, havde nattealferne ikke de store problemer med at gøre det, som de onde aqirer aldrig kunne: at vælte de to største imperier i verden.",
    ["At the continent's center, the Titans crafted a lake of scintillating energies. The lake, which they named the Well of Eternity, was to be the fount of life for the world. Its potent energies would nurture the bones of the world and empower life to take root in the land's rich soil. Over time, plants, trees, monsters, and creatures of every kind began to thrive on the primordial continent."] = "I kontinentets centrum skabte Titanerne en sø af funklende energier. Søen, som de døbte Evighedens Brønd, skulle blive verdens livskilde. Dens mægtige energier ville nære verdens knogler og give livet kraft til at slå rod i landets rige jord. Med tiden begyndte planter, træer, monstre og væsener af enhver slags at trives på det urgamle kontinent.",
    ["At the end of this terrible conflict -- known as the War of the Ancients -- the Well of Eternity imploded. The resulting shockwave shattered the greater landmass of Kalimdor. The center of the continent was blasted beneath the sea, leaving only a small group of broken, single continents."] = "Ved enden af denne forfærdelige konflikt -- kendt som De Ældgamles Krig -- imploderede Evighedens Brønd. Chokbølgen, der fulgte, knuste Kalimdørs store landmasse. Kontinentets centrum blev sprængt ned under havet, og tilbage blev kun en lille gruppe af brudte, enkeltstående kontinenter.",
    ["Backed by the Stormreaver and Twilight's Hammer clans, Gul'dan succeeded in raising the Tomb of Sargeras from the sea floor. However, when he opened the ancient, flooded vault, he found only crazed demons awaiting him."] = "Med støtte fra Stormrøver- og Tusmørkets Hammer-klanerne lykkedes det Gul'dæn at hæve Sargerås' Grav fra havbunden. Men da han åbnede det gamle, oversvømmede hvælv, fandt han kun rasende dæmoner, der ventede på ham.",
    ["Before the Age of Memory, the gentle Earthmother breathed upon the golden mists of dawn. Where the amber clouds came to rest, there were endless fields of flowing wheat and barley. This was the basin of her works - the great basket of life and hope."] = "Før Mindets Tidsalder åndede den milde Jordmoder på morgenens gyldne tåger. Der hvor de rav-farvede skyer faldt til ro, lå endeløse marker med bølgende hvede og byg. Dette var bassinet for hendes værk -- den store kurv af liv og håb.",
    ["Brother Neals,\r\n\r\nMy grapes are saved!  $N, the bearer of this manifest, braved my thug-infested vineyard and gathered the grapes that I could not.  Although the Defias still roam across the river, nearly my entire crop has been salvaged.\r\n\r\nYou may add a full load of grape bushels to your stores.\r\n\r\nMay the Light protect us,\r\n-Milly Osworth"] = "Broder Neals,\r\n\r\nMine druer er reddet! $N, bæreren af dette manifest, trodsede min banditplagede vingård og samlede de druer op, som jeg ikke selv kunne nå. Selvom Defias stadig strejfer rundt på den anden side af floden, er næsten hele min høst blevet reddet.\r\n\r\nDu må gerne lægge en hel læs drueskæpper til dine lagre.\r\n\r\nMåtte Let beskytte os,\r\n-Milly Osværd",
    ["But Kegan was very eager to speak on other subjects, particularly his time growing up in Lordaeron before its fall.  \r\n\r\nHe still holds much love for that lost kingdom, even though it is now ruined, and dead.\r\n\r\nMy growing fondness for Kegan gave me patience as I waited for my test results."] = "Men Kegøn var meget ivrig efter at tale om andre emner, især om sin tid som barn i Herrelande, før dens fald.  \r\n\r\nHan elsker stadig det tabte kongerige højt, selvom det nu er ødelagt og dødt.\r\n\r\nMin voksende hengivenhed for Kegøn gav mig tålmodighed, mens jeg ventede på mine testresultater.",
    ["But after weeks of no news my patience faltered, and upon further inquires to Dalaran I learned that the bloodstone never reached my colleagues.  My courier was somehow lost on the way, and the bloodstone pendant was lost with him!\r\n\r\nThis is grave news, for although Kegan and his followers still have bloodstone specimens with which we may experiment, I fear the pendant may fall into unsavory hands."] = "Men efter flere uger uden nyheder slap mit tålmod, og ved yderligere forespørgsler i Dalarn fandt jeg ud af, at blodstenen aldrig nåede mine kolleger. Min kurer var på en eller anden måde gået tabt undervejs, og blodstensvedhænget var gået tabt sammen med ham!\r\n\r\nDet er alvorlige nyheder, for selvom Kegøn og hans følgere stadig har blodstensprøver, som vi kan eksperimentere med, frygter jeg, at vedhænget kan havne i usle hænder.",
    ["But to answer those questions, more studies and experiments must be performed on the pendant, and I fear that the Lordamere Interment Camp cannot marshal the manpower nor the equipment for the task.  So I sent the bloodstone pendant with a courier to Dalaran with specific instructions on how to test it, so they may avoid my earlier frustrations."] = "Men for at besvare disse spørgsmål skal der udføres flere studier og eksperimenter på amuletten, og jeg frygter, at Lordamere-interneringslejren hverken kan mønstre mandskabet eller udstyret til opgaven.  Så jeg sendte blodstensamuletten med en budbringer til Dalarn med specifikke instrukser om, hvordan den skulle testes, så de kan undgå mine tidligere frustrationer.",
    ["But why do I mention this?  I do so to give credence to what I am about to write, for these words came from Kegan's lips and it is my hope that my colleagues will, upon reading this journal, know why I believe what he said:\r\n\r\n\"Remnants of the Old Gods still linger in the deep hollows of the world.  New forces seek to harness that ancient power, and those who succeed will have a terrible weapon against their enemies.\""] = "Men hvorfor nævner jeg dette?  Jeg gør det for at give troværdighed til det, jeg er ved at skrive, for disse ord kom fra Kegøns læber, og jeg håber, at mine kolleger, når de læser denne journal, vil forstå, hvorfor jeg tror på det, han sagde:\r\n\r\n\"Rester af De Gamle Guder ulmer stadig i verdens dybe hulrum.  Nye kræfter søger at tæmme den gamle magt, og de, der lykkes, vil få et frygteligt våben mod deres fjender.\"",
    ["By all accounts, the heroes were successful in destroying the portal and saving Azeroth - but whether or not they escaped the death throes of Draenor remains to be seen."] = "Efter alt at dømme lykkedes det heltene at ødelægge portalen og redde Azerot - men om de slap levende fra Draenørs dødskamp, må tiden vise.",
    ["By killing Medivh's body, Lothar and the young apprentice inadvertently banished the spirit of Sargeras to the abyss. As a consequence, the pure, virtuous spirit of Medivh was also allowed to live on... and wander the astral plane for many years to come."] = "Ved at dræbe Medivérs legeme forviste Lotar og den unge lærling uforvarende Sargerås' ånd til afgrunden. Som følge heraf fik Medivérs rene, dydige ånd også lov til at leve videre... og vandre rundt på det astrale plan i mange år frem.",
    ["By the time Sargeras' madness had consumed the last vestiges of his valiant spirit, he believed that the Titans themselves were responsible for creation's failure. Deciding, at last, to undo their works throughout the universe, he resolved to form an unstoppable army that would set the physical universe aflame."] = "Da Sargeras' galskab havde fortæret de sidste rester af hans tapre ånd, mente han, at Titanerne selv var skyld i skabelsens fiasko. Han besluttede sig endelig for at ophæve deres værker i hele universet og besluttede at danne en ustoppelig hær, der skulle sætte det fysiske univers i brand.",
    ["Calling themselves dwarves, the last of the earthen left the halls of Uldaman and ventured out into the waking world. Still lulled by the safety and wonders of the deep places, they founded a vast kingdom under the highest mountain in the land."] = "Kaldende sig selv for dværge forlod de sidste af de jordbårne Uldhulens haller og drog ud i den vågnende verden. Stadig vuggede af dybets tryghed og undere grundlagde de et enormt kongerige under landets højeste bjerg.",
    ["Cenarius, calling on the spirits of the enchanted forests, rallied an army of ancient tree-men and led them against the Legion in a daring ground assault. As the night elves' allies converged upon Azshara's temple and the Well of Eternity, all-out warfare erupted. Despite the strength of their newfound allies, Malfurion and his colleagues realized that the Legion could not be defeated by martial strength alone."] = "Cenarus, der kaldte på de fortryllede skoves ånder, samlede en hær af gamle træmænd og førte dem mod Legionen i et dristigt angreb på jorden. Da nattealfernes allierede samledes ved Azsyras tempel og Evighedens Brønd, brød fuldskala krig ud. På trods af styrken i deres nyfundne allierede gik det op for Malfurion og hans kolleger, at Legionen ikke kunne besejres med krigerisk styrke alene.",
    ["Cenarius, who dwelt within the sacred Moonglades of the distant Mount Hyjal, agreed to help the night elves by finding the ancient dragons and enlisting their aid. The dragons, led by the great red leviathan, Alexstrasza, agreed to send their mighty flights to engage the demons and their infernal masters."] = "Cenarus, der boede i de hellige Månelysninger ved det fjerne Hyjal-bjerg, indvilligede i at hjælpe nattealferne ved at finde de gamle drager og hverve deres støtte. Dragerne, ledet af det store røde havuhyre Aleksstrasa, indvilligede i at sende deres mægtige flyvninger for at engagere dæmonerne og deres helvedes herrer.",
    ["Choosing to follow his instincts, Lothar stormed Medivh's tower-fortress of Karazhan with the help of the wizard's young apprentice, Khadgar. Khadgar and Lothar succeeded in vanquishing the possessed Guardian, whom they confirmed to be the source of the conflict."] = "Lotar valgte at følge sit instinkt og stormede Medivérs tårnfæstning Karazhæn med hjælp fra troldmandens unge lærling, Kadgar. Kadgar og Lotar lykkedes med at nedkæmpe den besatte Vogter, som de bekræftede var kilden til konflikten.",
    ["Commander Primwell Skye\r\n\r\nCommander Skye's studies in military theory during her tenure as archivist bolstered Lordaeron's strategy during the Second War.  After serving as tactician on the Arathi front, she retired to a farmstead on the land she helped reclaim for humanity."] = "Kommandør Primvæl Skye\r\n\r\nKommandør Skyes studier i militærteori under hendes embedsperiode som arkivar styrkede Herrelandes strategi under Anden Krig.  Efter at have tjent som taktiker på Arathi-fronten trak hun sig tilbage til en gård på den jord, hun var med til at generobre for menneskeheden.",
    ["Confident that they could hold their own against the troll warbands or even the reclusive elves if need be, the Arathi warlords decided to construct a mighty fortress city in the southern regions of Lordaeron. The city-state, named Strom, became the capital of the Arathi nation, Arathor. As Arathor prospered, humans from all over the vast continent traveled south to the protection and safety of Strom."] = "Overbevist om at de kunne holde deres eget mod troldekrigerflokkene eller endda de tilbagetrukne alfer, hvis det blev nødvendigt, besluttede Arathi-krigsherrerne at bygge en mægtig fæstningsby i de sydlige egne af Herrelande. Bystaten, der blev kaldt Storm, blev hovedstaden i den arathiske nation, Arator. Efterhånden som Arator blomstrede, rejste mennesker fra hele det enorme kontinent sydpå til Storms beskyttelse og tryghed.",
    ["Consumed with the curse of this new bloodlust, the orcs sought to unleash their fury on any who stood before them. Sensing that the time had come, Gul'dan united the warring clans into a single unstoppable Horde."] = "Fortæret af forbandelsen fra denne nye blodtørst ville orkerne slippe deres raseri løs på enhver, der stod foran dem. Gul'dæn mærkede, at tiden var inde, og samlede de krigende klaner til én ustoppelig Horde.",
    ["Convinced that Ner'zhul was planning a new offensive against the Alliance, King Terenas of Lordaeron sent his armies into Draenor to end the orcish threat once and for all. Led by Khadgar and General Turalyon, the Alliance forces clashed with the orcs across the burning landscape. Even with the aid of the elven Ranger Alleria, the dwarf Kurdran and the veteran soldier Danath, Khadgar was unable to prevent Ner'zhul from opening his portals to other worlds."] = "Overbevist om at Ner'zhøl planlagde en ny offensiv mod Alliancen, sendte kong Terenæs af Herrelande sine hære ind i Draenør for at standse orkertruslen én gang for alle. Ledet af Kadgar og general Turalyon kolliderede Alliance-styrkerne med orkerne på tværs af det brændende landskab. Selv med hjælp fra alvespejderen Alleria, dværgen Kurdræn og veteransoldaten Danath kunne Kadgar ikke forhindre Ner'zhøl i at åbne sine portaler til andre verdener.",
    ["Deathwing's sudden betrayal was so destructive that the five dragonflights never truly recovered. Wounded and shocked, Alexstrasza and the other noble dragons were forced to abandon their mortal allies. Malfurion and his companions, now hopelessly outnumbered, barely survived the ensuing onslaught."] = "Dødsvinges pludselige forræderi var så ødelæggende, at de fem dragestammer aldrig rigtig kom sig. Såret og chokeret blev Aleksstrasa og de andre ædle drager tvunget til at forlade deres dødelige allierede. Malfurion og hans følgesvende, nu håbløst overtallige, overlevede knap nok det efterfølgende angreb.",
    ["Elf,\r\n\r\nAs a guest of the Horde, the Warchief has given you leave to travel freely throughout Horde territory.\r\n\r\nUse this guide to find your way around our lands."] = "Alf,\r\n\r\nSom gæst i Horden har Krigshøvdingen givet dig tilladelse til at rejse frit rundt i Hordens territorium.\r\n\r\nBrug denne vejledning til at finde rundt i vores lande.",
    ["Eonar also blessed Alexstrasza's younger sister, the lithe green dragon Ysera, with a portion of nature's influence. Ysera fell into an eternal trance, bound to the waking Dream of Creation. Known as the Dreamer, she would watch over the growing wilds of the world from her verdant realm, the Emerald Dream."] = "Ejonar velsignede også Aleksstrasas yngre søster, den slanke grønne drage Yserå, med en del af naturens indflydelse. Yserå faldt i en evig trance, bundet til Skabelsens vågnende Drøm. Kendt som Drømmeren ville hun vogte over verdens voksende vildnis fra sit frodige rige, Den Smaragdgrønne Drøm.",
    ["Eonar, the Titan patron of all life, gave a portion of her power to the red leviathan, Alexstrasza. Ever after, Alexstrasza would be known as the Life-Binder, and she would work to safeguard all living creatures within the world. Due to her supreme wisdom and limitless compassion for all living things, Alexstrasza was crowned the Dragonqueen and given dominion over her kind."] = "Ejonar, Titanen og beskytteren af alt liv, gav en del af sin kraft til det røde havuhyre Aleksstrasa. Fra da af blev Aleksstrasa kendt som Livbinderen, og hun ville arbejde for at beskytte alle levende væsener i verden. På grund af sin overlegne visdom og grænseløse medfølelse med alt levende blev Aleksstrasa kronet til Dragedronningen og fik herredømme over sin art.",
    ["Even Sargeras' titanic form became distorted from the corruption that plagued his once-noble heart. His eyes, hair, and beard erupted in fire, and his metallic bronze skin split open to reveal an endless furnace of blistering hate."] = "Selv Sargerås' titaniske skikkelse blev forvrænget af den korruption, der plagede hans engang så ædle hjerte. Hans øjne, hår og skæg blussede op i ild, og hans metalliske bronzehud revnede og afslørede en endeløs smedeovn af blærende had.",
    ["Eventually, the night elves were burned by the arcane fires they had sought to control. Their reckless use of magic had lured the demonic Burning Legion to the world. The demons crushed much of the night elves' civilization. Though there are no records to indicate that the Legion attacked either troll civilization, it is likely that battles took place across the breadth of the continent."] = "Til sidst blev nattealferne brændt af de arkane ild, de havde søgt at tæmme. Deres hensynsløse brug af magi havde lokket den dæmoniske Brændende Legion til verden. Dæmonerne knuste en stor del af nattealfernes civilisation. Selvom der ikke findes nogen optegnelser, der tyder på, at Legionen angreb nogen af trolde-civilisationerne, er det sandsynligt, at der fandt kampe sted over hele kontinentet.",
    ["Fern Crimsonleaf\r\nLead Intelligence Agent for the 2nd Division of the Brotherhood of the Horse\r\nFormer pupil of Ravenholdt\r\n\r\nInfiltrated and assassinated Horde leadership camped outside Farholde prior to the charge that broke the siege. The corpses of the fallen orcs and her dagger the only clues to her success. Whereabouts unknown. Presumed dead.\r\n\r\nA silent blade in the dark can be worth ten on the battlefield."] = "Fern Karmosinblad\r\nChef-efterretningsagent for Hestens Broderskabs 2. division\r\nTidligere elev fra Ravnehold\r\n\r\nInfiltrerede og myrdede Hordens ledelse, der havde lejret uden for Fjernholde før angrebet, der brød belejringen. Liggene af de faldne orker og hendes dolk er de eneste spor til hendes succes. Opholdssted ukendt. Formodet død.\r\n\r\nEt lydløst sværd i mørket kan være ti værd på slagmarken.",
    ["Find what the Alliance have dug up. We know what lies in these hills. With this, we will bring a worthy tribute to Rend.\r\n\r\nChieftain Nek'rosh"] = "Find det, Alliancen har gravet frem. Vi ved, hvad der ligger i disse bakker. Med dette vil vi bringe en værdig tribut til Flænse.\r\n\r\nHøvding Nekrosh",
    ["Fire rekindled within me, I then dove back into my experiments.  This time I made no assumptions, methodically performing every test at my disposal.  This increased my required efforts tremendously, but I would be more likely to make discoveries.  \r\n\r\nAnd, although my lab here is small and I have no subordinates to spare to aid, I did find one more intriguing quality of bloodstone..."] = "Ilden blussede op i mig igen, og jeg kastede mig tilbage over mine eksperimenter. Denne gang gjorde jeg ingen antagelser, men udførte metodisk hver eneste test, jeg havde til rådighed. Det øgede min indsats enormt, men så havde jeg større chance for at gøre opdagelser.  \r\n\r\nOg selvom mit laboratorium her er lille, og jeg ingen underordnede har til at hjælpe, fandt jeg dog én mere intrigerende egenskab ved blodstenen...",
    ["For a time the three factions kept a tenuous peace, but tensions erupted when High King Anvilmar passed away from old age. The three ruling clans went to war for control of Ironforge itself. The dwarf civil war raged under the earth for many years. Eventually the Bronzebeards, who had the largest standing army, banished the Dark Irons and Wildhammers from under the mountain."] = "I en tid holdt de tre fraktioner en skrøbelig fred, men spændingerne brød ud, da Overkonge Ambolmar døde af alderdom. De tre regerende klaner gik i krig om kontrollen over selve Jernsmede. Dværgenes borgerkrig rasede under jorden i mange år. Til sidst forviste Bronzeskæggene, som havde den største stående hær, Mørkjernsdværgene og Vildhamrene ud under bjerget.",
    ["For the first time in nearly three thousand years, the disparate nations of Arathor were once again united under a common banner. Appointed as Supreme Commander of the Alliance forces, Lord Lothar prepared his armies for the coming of the Horde."] = "For første gang i næsten tre tusinde år var Arators spredte nationer igen forenet under ét fælles banner. Herre Lotar, udnævnt til Den Højeste Kommandør for Alliancens styrker, forberedte sine hære til Hordens komme.",
    ["Found in the sweltering wastes of the Tanaris desert, this peculiar egg remains a mystery to modern ecologists. Dating tests suggest the egg could be up to a thousand years old. Though certain elements denote insectoid structure, its true origins cannot be discerned.  The species that lays such distinct eggs still remains to be discovered."] = "Fundet i de hedeslåede ørkener i Tanaris står dette besynderlige æg stadig som en gåde for moderne økologer. Dateringstest tyder på, at ægget kan være op til tusind år gammelt. Selvom visse elementer peger på insektlignende opbygning, kan dets sande oprindelse ikke afgøres.  Arten, der lægger så tydelige æg, er endnu ikke opdaget.",
    ["Gilneas and Alterac became strong supporters of Strom and developed mighty armies that explored the mountainous southern lands of Khaz Modan. It was during this period that humans first met the ancient race of dwarves and traveled to their cavernous subterranean city of Ironforge. The humans and dwarves shared many secrets of metal-smithing and engineering and discovered a common love for battle and storytelling."] = "Gilnæas og Alterac blev stærke støtter af Storm og udviklede mægtige hære, der udforskede de bjergrige sydlige lande i Khaz Mødan. Det var i denne periode, at menneskene første gang mødte dværgenes oldgamle race og rejste til deres hulende underjordiske by Jernsmede. Menneskene og dværgene delte mange hemmeligheder om metalsmedning og ingeniørkunst og opdagede en fælles kærlighed til kamp og historiefortælling.",
    ["Greetings $n,\r\n\r\nSince the elemental wind spirits vanished, Zephras has been on a deadly precipice. The birds, the beasts, and even the roots beneath our feet call to us for aid.\r\n\r\nSeek me out on the ground floor of the great tree here in Thendal Village. I will counsel and train you in the druidic arts.\r\n\r\n-Xyton Silverwind, Druid Trainer"] = "Hilsen $n,\r\n\r\nSiden de elementare vindånder forsvandt, har Vindras stået på en dødelig afgrund. Fuglene, bæsterne og selv rødderne under vores fødder kalder på vores hjælp.\r\n\r\nSøg mig op i stueetagen i det store træ her i Thendal-landsbyen. Jeg vil rådgive og træne dig i de druidiske kunster.\r\n\r\n-Xyton Sølvvind, Druidetræner",
    ["Greetings, $n,\r\n\r\nYou've shown great promise as a hunter, and I'd like to ensure that you receive proper guidance and training. \r\n\r\nThe rangers do a good job of keeping the wilds in check here in Thendal Grove, but beyond our borders... well, the same can't be said.\r\n\r\nCome find me near the center of the village as soon as you are able. The wilds are calling.\r\n\r\n-Tai'ree Farsight, Hunter Trainer"] = "Hilsen, $n,\r\n\r\nDu har vist et stort talent som jæger, og jeg vil gerne sikre, at du får ordentlig vejledning og træning. \r\n\r\nRangerne gør et godt stykke arbejde med at holde vildmarken i ave her i Thendal-lunden, men uden for vores grænser... ja, det samme kan ikke siges.\r\n\r\nKom og find mig nær landsbyens centrum, så snart du kan. Vildmarken kalder.\r\n\r\n-Tai'ree Langsyn, Jægertræner",
    ["Gul'dan agreed and decided that once the denizens of Azeroth were beaten, he would find the legendary tomb and claim his reward. Assured that the Horde would serve his purposes, Sargeras ordered the invasion to begin."] = "Gul'dæn gik med til det og besluttede, at når Azeroths indbyggere var besejret, ville han finde den legendariske grav og gøre krav på sin belønning. Sargerås, forsikret om at Horden ville tjene hans formål, befalede invasionen at begynde.",
    ["Here we honor the fallen\r\nBrave souls who paid the ultimate price\r\nThey gave their lives for our freedom\r\nWe stand in their shadows, forever grateful\r\nTheir sacrifice endures, their memory lives"] = "Her ærer vi de faldne\r\nModige sjæle, som betalte den ultimative pris\r\nDe gav deres liv for vores frihed\r\nVi står i deres skygge, evigt taknemmelige\r\nDeres offer varer ved, deres minde lever",
    ["His fellow Titans tried to persuade him of his error and calm his raging emotions, but he disregarded their more optimistic beliefs as self-serving delusions. Storming from their ranks forever, Sargeras set out to find his own place in the universe. Although the Pantheon was sorrowful at his departure, the Titans could never have predicted just how far their lost brother would go."] = "Hans medtitaner forsøgte at overbevise ham om sin fejl og berolige hans rasende følelser, men han afviste deres mere optimistiske overbevisninger som selvisk vrangforestilling. Han stormede for evigt ud af deres rækker, og Sargerås begav sig ud for at finde sin egen plads i universet. Selvom Panteonet var sorgfuldt over hans afrejse, kunne Titanerne aldrig have forudset, hvor langt deres fortabte bror ville gå.",
    ["His old comrade, Durotan, returned from exile and warned him yet again of Gul'dan's treachery. In speedy retribution, Gul'dan's assassins murdered Durotan and his family, leaving only his infant son alive. Unknown to Doomhammer was the fact that Durotan's infant son was found by the human officer, Aedelas Blackmoore, and taken as a slave. \r\n\r\nThat infant orc would one day rise to become the greatest leader his people would ever know."] = "Hans gamle kammerat, Dorotan, vendte tilbage fra eksilet og advarede ham nok en gang om Gul'dæns forræderi. Som en hurtig hævn myrdede Gul'dæns snigmordere Dorotan og hans familie og efterlod kun hans spæde søn i live. Hvad Dømmehammer ikke vidste, var, at Dorotans spæde søn blev fundet af den menneskelige officer Aedelas Sortmoor og taget som slave. \r\n\r\nDen spæde ork ville en dag stige op og blive den største leder, hans folk nogensinde ville kende.",
    ["However, during the final days of the Second War, as the Horde's victory over the Alliance seemed almost assured, a terrible feud erupted between the two most powerful orcs on Azeroth. As Doomhammer prepared his final assault against the Capital City of Lordaeron - an assault that would have crushed the last remnants of the Alliance - Gul'dan and his followers abandoned their posts and set out to sea."] = "Men under de sidste dage af Anden Krig, da Hordens sejr over Alliancen næsten virkede sikret, brød en forfærdelig fejde ud mellem de to mægtigste orker på Azeroth. Mens Dømmehammer forberedte sit sidste angreb mod Herrelandes Hovedstad - et angreb, der ville have knust Alliancens sidste rester - forlod Gul'dæn og hans tilhængere deres poster og drog ud på havet.",
    ["However, knowing that the various chieftains like Hellscream and Orgrim Doomhammer would vie for overall supremacy, Gul'dan set up a puppet warchief to rule over this new Horde. Blackhand the Destroyer, a particularly depraved and vicious orc warlord, was chosen to be Gul'dan's puppet. Under Blackhand's command, the Horde set out to test itself against the simple draenei."] = "Men Gul'dæn vidste, at de forskellige høvdinge som Helskrig og Orgrim Dømmehammer ville kæmpe om den samlede overhøjhed, og satte derfor en marionet-krigshøvding over til at herske over denne nye Horde. Sortehånd Ødelæggeren, en særligt fordærvet og ond orkekrigsherre, blev valgt til at være Gul'dæns marionet. Under Sortehånds kommando drog Horden ud for at teste sig selv mod de simple draenei.",
    ["I have sent another messenger to Dalaran, and hear that even now they are scouring for the pendant, in the ruins outside our protective sphere.\r\n\r\nI only hope we're not too late."] = "Jeg har sendt endnu en budbringer til Dalarn, og jeg hører, at de allerede nu gennemsøger ruinerne uden for vores beskyttende kuppel efter vedhænget.\r\n\r\nJeg håber blot, at vi ikke er for sent på den.",
    ["I hope my sigil finds you well, $c. I write to you because our people have need for those strong with the blade, the glaive, and all other weapons. So much has happened since our people have been reintroduced to the other races of Azeroth that we have an even greater need for protectors of all kinds.$B$BThis is where you come in. I would tell you more, but I feel it should be in person. Find me inside Aldrassil... on the lower levels.$B$B-Alyissia, Warrior Trainer"] = "Jeg håber, mit segl finder dig vel, $c. Jeg skriver til dig, fordi vores folk har brug for dem, der er stærke med klinge, glaive og alle andre våben. Så meget er sket, siden vores folk blev genindført til Azeroths andre racer, at vi har et endnu større behov for beskyttere af alle slags.$B$BDet er her, du kommer ind i billedet. Jeg ville fortælle dig mere, men jeg mener, det bør ske ansigt til ansigt. Find mig inde i Aldrasil... på de nederste etager.$B$B-Alyisia, Krigertræner",
    ["I started my tests with the assumption that bloodstone was a type of rock, like quartz or obsidian.  So I began a series of procedures to determine: what minerals were contained within bloodstone, what forces were applied to produce its color and hardness, and other properties common to rocks and ore.  But the bloodstone pendant, to my frustration, did not react to my procedures as would normal ore."] = "Jeg startede mine forsøg med den antagelse, at blodsten var en slags sten, ligesom kvarts eller obsidian.  Så jeg begyndte en række procedurer for at fastslå: hvilke mineraler der var indeholdt i blodsten, hvilke kræfter der var blevet påført for at skabe dens farve og hårdhed, og andre egenskaber fælles for sten og malm.  Men blodstensvedhænget reagerede til min frustration ikke på mine procedurer, sådan som almindelig malm ville have gjort.",
    ["If anyone finds this, please, do your best to stop them. There were only a few left at the tower when I scribbled this note and crawled away.\r\n\r\nAlso, try and get Raani's lucky feather from his body. He liked to tell tall tales about how he plucked it from some kind of firebird and I think he'd want to make sure that it made its way back home.\r\n\r\nIf you are also able to retrieve Arvensus Shadowsong's family signet from his body, please do so. High Elder Shadowsong is his uncle and he would want it to be returned to the family."] = "Hvis nogen finder dette, så gør dit bedste for at stoppe dem. Der var kun få tilbage ved tårnet, da jeg skrev denne seddel og krøb væk.\r\n\r\nPrøv også at få Rænis heldige fjer ud af hans lig. Han elskede at fortælle fantastiske historier om, hvordan han plukkede den fra en slags ildfugl, og jeg tror, han ville ønske at sikre, at den fandt vej hjem.\r\n\r\nHvis du også kan hente Skyggesang-familiens Signet fra Arvensus Skyggesangs lig, så gør det venligst. Højelder Skyggesang er hans onkel, og han ville ønske, at det blev returneret til familien.",
    ["Illidan, who had grown dependent on magic's empowering energies, struggled to keep control of his nearly overwhelming hunger to tap the Well's energies once again. However, with Tyrande's patient support, he was able to restrain himself and help his brother find the reclusive demigod, Cenarius."] = "Ilidan, som var blevet afhængig af magiens styrkende energier, kæmpede for at bevare kontrollen over sin næsten overvældende trang til igen at tappe Brøndens energier. Men med Tyrandes tålmodige støtte formåede han at tøjle sig selv og hjælpe sin bror med at finde den tilbagetrukne halvgud Cenarus.",
    ["In a last-ditch effort, Doomhammer and his lieutenants staged a daring charge from the Spire and clashed with Lothar's paladins in the center of the Burning Steppes. Doomhammer and Lothar squared off in a titanic battle that left both mighty combatants battered and drained. Though Doomhammer narrowly succeeded in vanquishing Lothar, the great hero's death did not have the effect the warchief had hoped for."] = "I et sidste desperat forsøg lod Dømmehammer og hans løjtnanter et dristigt angreb storme ud fra Spiret og stødte sammen med Lotars korsriddere midt i de Brændende Stepper. Dømmehammer og Lotar tog hinanden op i et titanisk slag, der efterlod begge mægtige krigere forslåede og drænede. Selvom Dømmehammer med nød og næppe fik overvundet Lotar, havde den store helts død ikke den effekt, krigshøvdingen havde håbet på.",
    ["In addition to blood, there are elemental forces fused within the stone.  Fire, water, thunder and rock are mixed with the blood (but again, the blood of what?), and although this mixture is outwardly inert, all these forces seem to rage inwardly against each other.  So many more questions were then raised about this amazing, and foreboding material."] = "Ud over blod er der elementarkræfter smeltet ind i stenen.  Ild, vand, torden og klippe er blandet op med blodet (men igen: blod af hvad?), og selvom denne blanding udadtil er inaktiv, synes alle disse kræfter at rase indvendigt mod hinanden.  Der opstod så mange flere spørgsmål om dette fantastiske og ildevarslende materiale.",
    ["In fact, it often acted in precisely the opposite fashion as expected!  It was almost as if the pendant was deliberately fouling my experiments.\r\n\r\nLike it was thinking, and alive.\r\n\r\nAngered but not discouraged, I switched from assuming the pendant was an inert piece of rock, to assuming it was a living thing.  \r\n\r\nBut again, I failed."] = "Faktisk opførte den sig ofte præcis modsat af det forventede!  Det var næsten, som om vedhænget bevidst ødelagde mine eksperimenter.\r\n\r\nSom om den tænkte og var levende.\r\n\r\nOpbragt, men ikke modløs, skiftede jeg fra at antage, at vedhænget var et inaktivt stykke sten, til at antage, at det var en levende ting.  \r\n\r\nMen igen mislykkedes jeg.",
    ["In his fury, Sargeras shattered the prisons of the eredar and the Nathrezim and set the loathsome demons free. These cunning creatures bowed before the dark Titan's vast rage and offered to serve him in whatever malicious ways they could. From the ranks of the powerful Eredar, Sargeras picked two champions to command his demonic army of destruction."] = "I sin vrede knuste Sargerås fængslerne for eredarerne og Nathrezimmerne og slap de forhadte dæmoner løs. Disse snedige væsener bøjede sig for den mørke Titans umådelige raseri og tilbød at tjene ham på de mest ondsindede måder, de kunne. Fra rækkerne af de mægtige eredarer udvalgte Sargerås to mestre til at anføre sin dæmoniske ødelæggelseshær.",
    ["In the ancient times, after the Titans departed Azeroth, their children, known as the earthen, continued to shape and guard the deep recesses of the world. The earthen were largely unconcerned with the affairs of the surface-dwelling races and longed only to plumb the dark depths of the earth."] = "I oldtiden, efter Titanerne havde forladt Azerot, fortsatte deres børn, kendt som jordfolket, med at forme og vogte verdens dybe afkroge. Jordfolket var stort set ligeglade med overfladeracernes anliggender og længtes kun efter at lodde jordens mørke dybder.",
    ["In time, the lords of Strom sought to move their estates to the lush northlands of Lordaeron and leave the arid lands of the south. The heirs of King Thoradin, the last descendants of the Arathi bloodline, argued that Strom should not be abandoned and thus incurred the displeasure of the greater citizenry, who were likewise eager to leave."] = "Med tiden ønskede Storms herrer at flytte deres godser til Herrelandes frodige nordlande og forlade de tørre lande i syd. Kong Torradins arvinger, de sidste efterkommere af Arathi-blodslinjen, hævdede, at Storm ikke burde forlades, og pådrog sig dermed den brede befolknings misbilligelse, som lige så ivrigt ville af sted.",
    ["Incensed by Durotan's death, Orgrim set out to free the Horde from demonic corruption and ultimately assumed the role of warchief of the Horde by killing Gul'dan's corrupt puppet, Blackhand. Under his decisive leadership the relentless Horde finally laid siege to Stormwind Keep."] = "Opbragt over Dorotans død satte Orgrim sig for at befri Horden fra dæmonisk korruption og overtog til sidst rollen som krigshøvding for Horden ved at dræbe Gul'dæns korrupte marionet, Sortehånd. Under hans afgørende lederskab belejrede den ubarmhjertige Horde til sidst Stormvinds Fæstning.",
    ["Ira Valor, Forest Stalker\r\n\r\nWhen Ira's father grew ill, she took it upon herself to gather food and supplies from the nearby forests. While resources were not in short supply, you were as likely to find food as you were to become it.\r\n\r\nOver the years, she adapted to the forests, preferring to spend her time within the dark woods rather than in Raven Hill. Travelers who got lost in the trees would tell stories of a shadow seemingly opening the way for them back to the road. There was no confirmations of who it was, but rumors spread quickly.\r\n\r\nIt's said that Ira is still in the woods offering a guiding hand to those who fall prey to the beasts within."] = "Ira Tapper, Skovsniger\r\n\r\nDa Iras far blev syg, tog hun på sig at samle mad og forsyninger fra de nærliggende skove. Selvom ressourcerne ikke var knappe, var man lige så sandsynligt at finde mad, som man var at blive den.\r\n\r\nGennem årene tilpassede hun sig skovene og foretrak at tilbringe sin tid i de mørke træer frem for på Ravnehøj. Rejsende, der var faret vild i træerne, fortalte historier om en skygge, der tilsyneladende åbnede vejen tilbage til landevejen for dem. Der var ingen bekræftelse på, hvem det var, men rygterne spredte sig hurtigt.\r\n\r\nDet siges, at Ira stadig er i skoven og tilbyder en hjælpende hånd til dem, der falder offer for bæsterne derinde.",
    ["It fell to Malfurion Stormrage to find help for his beleaguered people. Stormrage, whose own brother, Illidan, practiced the Highborne's magics, was incensed by the growing corruption amongst the upper class. Convincing Illidan to forsake his dangerous obsession, Malfurion set out to find Cenarius and muster a resistance force."] = "Det faldt til Malfurion Stormrasen at finde hjælp til sit plagede folk. Stormrasen, hvis egen bror, Ilidan, udøvede de Højfødtes magier, var opbragt over den voksende korruption blandt overklassen. Efter at have overtalt Ilidan til at opgive sin farlige besættelse, begav Malfurion sig ud for at finde Cenarus og samle en modstandsstyrke.",
    ["It is encouraging to hear that the new magic that our lord provided has performed above expectations. If the venom is as effective as you claim, it will be a powerful tool for us to use in the conflict to come. I told you that there was much to be learned from the undead littering our mountain. Don't worry, I won't hold your initial skepticism against you.\r\n\r\nFinish your business there and return to the summit with your samples. No need to cull the beasts. If they spread to neighboring areas, they will only sow chaos, confusion and fear. This will serve to further the Pact's goals, in the end.\r\n\r\nGood work. The Wild King will surely be pleased with what you have accomplished."] = "Det er opmuntrende at høre, at den nye magi, vores herre har skaffet, har overgået forventningerne. Hvis giften er så effektiv, som du hævder, bliver den et kraftfuldt redskab for os i konflikten, der kommer. Jeg sagde jo, at der er meget at lære af de udøde, der vrimler på vores bjerg. Bekymr dig ikke, jeg vil ikke holde din oprindelige skepsis imod dig.\r\n\r\nAfslut dine ærinder dér og vend tilbage til toppen med dine prøver. Der er ingen grund til at udrydde bæsterne. Hvis de spreder sig til nabolandene, vil de blot så kaos, forvirring og frygt. Det vil i sidste ende tjene Pagtens mål.\r\n\r\nGodt arbejde. Den Vilde Konge vil helt sikkert være tilfreds med det, du har udrettet.",
    ["It would appear that whatever it is that Klaven has locked away in the chest is having adverse effects upon the inhabitants of the tower. I suspect that the other guards may have similar weaknesses and perhaps, even Klaven himself has fallen victim to the fallout. \r\n\r\nAgent Amber Kearnen\r\nSI:7 Ground Level Operative, R8"] = "Det ser ud til, at det, Klaven har låst inde i kisten, har skadelige virkninger på tårnets indbyggere. Jeg mistænker, at de andre vagter kan have lignende svagheder, og måske er selv Klaven faldet offer for nedfaldet. \r\n\r\nAgent Rav Kjarnen\r\nSI:Syv Malet Niveau-agent, R8",
    ["Kegan Darkmar, leader of the small group of undead who came to us in search of asylum from their \"brethren,\" defies our common attitudes toward his kind.  His skin may be rotting and blood may have long stopped flowing through his veins, but he acts very nobly and seems to care more for his compatriots' safety than his own.\r\n\r\nIndeed, there is a humanity within him that, I confess, I sometimes see lacking in the humans around me."] = "Kegøn Mørkmar, leder af den lille flok udøde, der kom til os for at søge asyl fra deres \"brødre\", trodser vores almindelige holdninger over for hans slags.  Hans hud kan være ved at rådne, og blodet er måske for længst holdt op med at flyde i årene, men han opfører sig meget ædelt og synes at bekymre sig mere om sine kompagnoners sikkerhed end sin egen.\r\n\r\nFaktisk er der en menneskelighed i ham, som jeg indrømmer, jeg til tider ser mangle hos de mennesker omkring mig.",
    ["Khardros and his Wildhammer warriors traveled north through the barrier gates of Dun Algaz, and they founded their own kingdom within the distant peak of Grim Batol. There, the Wildhammers thrived and rebuilt their stores of treasure. Thaurissan and his Dark Irons did not fare as well. Humiliated and enraged by their defeat, they vowed revenge against Ironforge. Leading his people far to the south, Thaurissan founded a city (which he named after himself) within the beautiful Redridge Mountains."] = "Khardros og hans Vildhammer-krigere rejste nordpå gennem barriereportene i Algaz-bakken, og de grundlagde deres eget kongerige i den fjerne top Grimbatol. Dér trivedes Vildhamrene og genopbyggede deres skatkamre. Tårissan og hans Mørkjernsdværge klarede sig ikke lige så godt. Ydmyget og rasende over deres nederlag svor de hævn mod Jernsmede. Tårissan førte sit folk langt mod syd og grundlagde en by (som han opkaldte efter sig selv) inde i de smukke Rødryg-bjerge.",
    ["Khaz'goroth, the Titan shaper and forger of the world, bestowed some of his vast power upon the mighty black wyrm, Neltharion. The great-hearted Neltharion, known afterwards as the Earth-Warder, was given dominion over the earth and the deep places of the world. He embodied the strength of the world and served as Alexstrasza's greatest supporter."] = "Khaz'gorot, Titanen, der formede og smedede verden, skænkede noget af sin enorme kraft til den mægtige sorte wyrm, Neltharion. Den storhjertede Neltharion, som senere blev kendt som Jordvogteren, fik herredømmet over jorden og verdens dybe steder. Han legemliggjorde verdens styrke og var Aleksstrasas største tilhænger.",
    ["Kil'jaeden knew that the Horde was finally prepared. The orcs had become the Burning Legion's greatest weapon. The cunning demon shared his knowledge with his waiting master, and Sargeras agreed that the time of his revenge had finally come."] = "Kil'Dagen vidste, at Horden endelig var rustet. Orkerne var blevet den Brændende Legions største våben. Den snedige dæmon delte sin viden med sin ventende herre, og Sargerås erklærede sig enig i, at tiden for hans hævn endelig var kommet.",
    ["Kil'jaeden knew that the orc clans were almost ready, but he needed to be certain of their ultimate loyalty. In secret, he had the Shadow Council summon Mannoroth the Destructor, the living vessel of destruction and rage. Gul'dan called the clan chieftains together and convinced them that drinking Mannoroth's raging blood would make them utterly invincible."] = "Kil'Dagen vidste, at orkeklanerne næsten var klar, men han måtte være sikker på deres yderste loyalitet. I hemmelighed fik han Skyggerådet til at tilkalde Mannoroth Destruktoren, den levende beholder af ødelæggelse og raseri. Gul'dæn kaldte klanhøvdingene sammen og overbeviste dem om, at det at drikke Mannoroths rasende blod ville gøre dem fuldstændig uovervindelige.",
    ["Kil'jaeden the Deceiver was chosen to seek out the darkest races in the universe and recruit them into Sargeras' ranks. The second champion, Archimonde the Defiler, was chosen to lead Sargeras' vast armies into battle against any who might resist the Titan's will."] = "Kil'Dagen Bedrageren blev valgt til at opspore de mørkeste racer i universet og hverve dem til Sargerås' rækker. Den anden mester, Archimonde Skænderen, blev valgt til at lede Sargerås' enorme hære ud i kamp mod enhver, der måtte modsætte sig Titanens vilje.",
    ["Kil'jaeden's first move was to enslave the vampiric dreadlords under his terrible power. The dreadlords served as his personal agents throughout the universe, and they took pleasure in locating primitive races for their master to corrupt and bring into the fold. First amongst the dreadlords was Tichondrius the Darkener. Tichondrius served Kil'jaeden as the perfect soldier and agreed to bring Sargeras' burning will to all the dark corners of the universe."] = "Kil'Dagens første træk var at gøre de vampyriske frygtherrer til slaver under sin frygtelige magt. Frygtherrerne tjente ham som hans personlige agenter i hele universet, og de nød at finde primitive racer, som deres mester kunne korrumpere og føre ind i folden. Blandt frygtherrerne var Tichondrius Formørkeren den første. Tichondrius tjente Kil'Dagen som den perfekte soldat og lovede at bringe Sargerås' brændende vilje til alle universets mørke afkroge.",
    ["King Llane had severely underestimated the might of the Horde, and he watched helplessly as his kingdom fell to the green-skinned invaders. Ultimately King Llane was assassinated by one of the Shadow Council's finest killers: the half-orc, Garona."] = "Kong Lane havde alvorligt undervurderet Hordens styrke, og han så hjælpeløst til, mens hans kongerige faldt for de grønhudede invasorer. Til sidst blev Kong Lane myrdet af et af Skyggerådets dygtigste mordere: halvorken Garona.",
    ["King Llane shared his concerns with Anduin Lothar, the last descendent of the Arathi bloodline, whom he named his lieutenant-at-arms. Even so, neither man could have imagined that Medivh's slow descent into madness would bring about the horrors that were to come."] = "Kong Lane delte sine bekymringer med Anduin Lotar, den sidste efterkommer af Arathi-blodslinjen, som han udnævnte til sin våbenløjtnant. Alligevel kunne ingen af mændene have forestillet sig, at Medivérs langsomme glidning ud i vanvid ville føre til de rædsler, der skulle komme.",
    ["Lady Cassandra Valor, Loving mother and wife\r\n\r\nNot much is known about Cassandra other than her love for her family. She nurtured brave children and a powerful husband, leading some to muse that the family's greatness was all her doing. A flattery she would always decline with grace.\r\n\r\nIf she is remembered for nothing else, let it be known that everything she did was for her family."] = "Dame Cassandra Tapper, Kærlig mor og hustru\r\n\r\nDer er ikke meget kendt om Kassandra ud over hendes kærlighed til sin familie. Hun plejede modige børn og en mægtig ægtemand, hvilket fik nogle til at mene, at familiens storhed var hendes værk alene. En smiger hun altid afviste med nåde.\r\n\r\nHvis hun husker for intet andet, lad det være kendt, at alt hun gjorde, var for sin familie.",
    ["Lady Isolde Brightlance\r\nSecond in Command to Sir Howard\r\nGuidon-bearer of the 2nd Division of the Brotherhood of the Horse\r\n\r\nJoined the charge that broke the siege on Farholde. Her courage and standard inspired all around that day.\r\n\r\nHer battle cry rose above the thunder of our hooves. She died upright, banner held high for all to see.\r\n\r\n-Demar Brant, Knight Commander of the Brotherhood of the Horse."] = "Dame Isolde Lysspyd\r\nNæstkommanderende under Ridder Howard\r\nFanebærer for 2. Division af Hestens Broderskab\r\n\r\nSluttede sig til ladningen, der brød belejringen af Fjernholde. Hendes mod og banner inspirerede alle omkring hende den dag.\r\n\r\nHendes krigsskrig steg op over tordenen fra vores hove. Hun døde oprejst, banneret hævet højt, så alle kunne se det.\r\n\r\n-Demar Brand, Ridderkommandør for Hestens Broderskab.",
    ["Led by Grom Hellscream, all the clan chiefs except Durotan drank and thereby sealed their fates as slaves to the Burning Legion. Empowered by Mannoroth's rage, the chieftains unwittingly extended this subjugation to their unsuspecting brethren."] = "Anført af Grom Helskrig drak alle klanhøvdingene undtagen Dorotan og beseglede dermed deres skæbne som trælle for Brændende Legion. Styrket af Mannoroths raseri udvidede høvdingene uvidende denne underkuelse til deres intetanende brødre.",
    ["Living death on this page you will see.\r\nOnly will you find the key if you look beneath mindless undeath.\r\nSewer's trail, a toxic tail."] = "Levende død vil du se på denne side.\r\nKun da finder du nøglen, hvis du kigger under tankeløs udødhed.\r\nKloakkens spor, en giftig hale.",
    ["Lord Grant Valor, Sire of the Valor Family\r\n\r\nLord Grant, may he rest in peace, was the pinnacle of Alliance exceptionalism. A natural leader, his guiding hand helped lead the denizens of Raven Hill to prosperity. When darkness began to creep into the woods, he was the first to rally our people.\r\n\r\nThere was no more foul a foe than the undead to Lord Grant. He personally patrolled the cemeteries of Duskwood to keep the shambling hordes in check. The day he took a grievous blow from the monsters, everyone in town shared his pain.\r\n\r\nWith his family's care, he returned to his duties, but there was a lingering malady that seemed to follow him for the rest of his days."] = "Herre Grant Tapper, Herskeren af Tapper-familien\r\n\r\nHerre Grant, må han hvile i fred, var det fineste eksempel på Alliancens storhed. En født leder, hans vejledende hånd hjalp med at føre Ravnehøjs beboere mod velstand. Da mørket begyndte at snige sig ind i skoven, var han den første til at samle vores folk.\r\n\r\nIngen var en mere afskyelig fjende end de udøde for Herre Grant. Han patruljerede personligt kirkegårdene i Skumringsskoven for at holde de slæbende horder i ave. Den dag han fik et alvorligt slag fra monstrene, delte alle i byen hans smerte.\r\n\r\nMed sin families omsorg vendte han tilbage til sine pligter, men der var en vedvarende plage, som så ud til at følge ham resten af hans dage.",
    ["Lord Lothar rallied the remnants of Azeroth's armies after their defeat at Stormwind Keep, and then launched a massive exodus across the sea to the northern kingdom of Lordaeron. Convinced that the Horde would overcome all of humanity if left unchecked, the leaders of the seven human nations met and agreed to unite in what would become known as the Alliance of Lordaeron."] = "Herre Lotar samlede restene af Azeroths hære efter deres nederlag ved Stormvinds Fæstning og satte derefter en massiv udvandring over havet i gang til det nordlige kongerige Herrelande. Overbevist om at Horden ville overvinde hele menneskeheden, hvis den ikke blev kontrolleret, mødtes lederne af de syv menneskelige nationer og blev enige om at forenes i det, der senere skulle kendes som Herrelandenes Alliance.",
    ["Lord Lothar, seeing that the Horde was fracturing from within, gathered the last of his forces and pushed Doomhammer south, back into the shattered heartland of Stormwind. There, the Alliance forces trapped the retreating Horde within the volcanic fortress of Blackrock Spire. Though Lord Lothar fell in battle at the Spire's base, his lieutenant, Turalyon, rallied the Alliance forces at the eleventh hour and drove the Horde back into the abysmal Swamp of Sorrows."] = "Herre Lotar, der så at Horden splittedes indefra, samlede sine sidste styrker og drev Dømmehammer sydpå, tilbage ind i Stormvinds knuste hjerteland. Der fangede Alliance-styrkerne den retirerende Horde inde i Sortklippe-spirets vulkanske fæstning. Selvom Herre Lotar faldt i kamp ved spirets fod, samlede hans løjtnant, Turalyon, Alliance-styrkerne i den ellevte time og drev Horden tilbage ind i den afgrundsdybe Sorgens Sump.",
    ["Lothar and his warriors, returning home from Karazhan, hoped to stem the loss of life and save their once-glorious homeland. Instead, they returned too late and found their beloved kingdom in smoking ruins. The orcish Horde continued to ravage the countryside and claimed the surrounding lands for its own. Forced into hiding, Lothar and his companions swore a grim oath to reclaim their homeland at any cost."] = "Lotar og hans krigere, der vendte hjem fra Karazhæn, håbede at standse tabet af liv og redde deres engang så glorværdige hjemland. I stedet kom de for sent hjem og fandt deres elskede kongerige i rygende ruiner. Den orkiske Horde fortsatte med at hærge landskabet og gjorde de omkringliggende lande til sine egne. Tvunget i skjul svor Lotar og hans ledsagere en dyster ed om at genvinde deres hjemland for enhver pris.",
    ["Malfurion, convinced that the Well of Eternity was the demons' umbilical link to the physical world, insisted that it should be destroyed. His companions, knowing that the Well was the source of their immortality and powers, were horrified by the rash notion. Yet Tyrande saw the wisdom of Malfurion's theory, so she convinced Cenarius and their comrades to storm Azshara's temple and find a way to shut the Well down for good."] = "Malfurion, overbevist om at Evighedens Brønd var dæmonernes navlestreng til den fysiske verden, insisterede på, at den skulle ødelægges. Hans ledsagere, der vidste at Brønden var kilden til deres udødelighed og kræfter, blev forfærdede over den overilede tanke. Men Tyrande så visdommen i Malfurions teori, så hun overtalte Cenarus og deres kammerater til at storme Azsyras tempel og finde en måde at lukke Brønden for altid.",
    ["Mathias Shaw has sent an errand boy to kill me. <illegible text>\r\n\r\nHe patrols outside now. Mindless, lifeless drone.\r\n\r\nHahahah!"] = "Mathias Skaw har sendt en løbedreng for at dræbe mig. <ulæselig tekst>\r\n\r\nHan patruljerer udenfor nu. Tankeløs, livløs håndlanger.\r\n\r\nHahahah!",
    ["Mechanic's Log\r\n\r\n<The small leatherbound journal is covered in oil and grease stains. There are sketches of schematics and mechanical configurations, each with notation and written descriptions. You flip to a random page.>\r\n\r\nThis commission will pay the bills for years, I just have to figure out how to keep the oscillation neutralizer from overheating or grinding itself to metal shavings. What I need to do is vortex transfer the excess heat into the combustion core, but I've been putting that off cause I'll need to dismantle the entire walker and then take the whole engine apart.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nPage 17"] = "Mekanikerens Logbog\r\n\r\n<Den lille læderindbundne dagbog er dækket af olie- og fedtpletter. Der er skitser af diagrammer og mekaniske konfigurationer, hver med noter og skrevne beskrivelser. Du bladrer til en tilfældig side.>\r\n\r\nDenne bestilling vil betale regningerne i årevis, jeg skal bare finde ud af, hvordan jeg holder oscillationsneutralisatoren fra at overophede eller slibe sig selv til metalspåner. Det jeg skal gøre er at vortex-overføre den overskydende varme over i forbrændingskernen, men jeg har udskudt det, for jeg bliver nødt til at skille hele gangmaskinen ad og så tage hele motoren fra hinanden.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSide 17",
    ["Memories of Valor\r\nA Recount of the Valor Family and Their Service to Raven Hill\r\n\r\nThere was no greater family in all of the Eastern Kingdoms than the Valor family. Their deeds to the people they swore to protect were nothing short of miracles, and their loss is a loss for all of Raven Hill.\r\n\r\nI write this account to set the record straight, detailing the marvels that were Grant, Ira, Silvia, and Merrick. May these writings be a small consolation for how sorry I am for their absence."] = "Minder om Tapperhed\r\nEn beretning om Tapper-familien og deres tjeneste for Ravnehøj\r\n\r\nDer fandtes ingen større familie i hele Østkongerigerne end Tapper-familien. Deres gerninger mod de folk, de havde svoret at beskytte, var intet mindre end mirakler, og deres tab er et tab for hele Ravnehøj.\r\n\r\nJeg skriver denne beretning for at rette op på sagen og beskrive de vidundere, som var Grant, Ira, Silvia og Merrick. Må disse skrifter være en lille trøst for, hvor ondt jeg har over deres fravær.",
    ["Merrick Valor, Watcher of Darkshire\r\n\r\nMerrick was the youngest son of the Valor family. As he witnessed the corruption coming to his homeland, he chose to join The Watch in a desperate bid to protect his loved ones.\r\n\r\nWhile he was the most inexperienced member of his family, he quickly made a name for himself amongst the ranks of The Watchers. He had a knack for archery, and soon became one of the most staunch defenders of Darkshire.\r\n\r\nHis personal mission was to keep the roads safe, wary of the ever more hostile creatures coming to the forests."] = "Merrick Tapper, Vagt i Mørkeshire\r\n\r\nMerrick var den yngste søn i Tapper-familien. Da han så korruptionen komme til sit hjemland, valgte han at slutte sig til Vagten i et desperat forsøg på at beskytte sine elskede.\r\n\r\nSelvom han var det mest uerfarne medlem af sin familie, gjorde han hurtigt navn for sig i rækken af Vagterne. Han havde et talent for bueskydning og blev snart et af de mest standhaftige forsvarere af Mørkeshire.\r\n\r\nHans personlige mission var at holde vejene sikre, på vagt over for de stadig mere fjendtlige væsener, der kom ind i skovene.",
    ["Most of these demonic encounters were isolated events, and the ruling Magocrats did what they could to keep such events hidden from the public. The most powerful magicians were sent to capture the elusive demons, but they often found themselves hopelessly outmatched by the lone agents of the mighty Legion."] = "De fleste af disse dæmoniske møder var isolerede begivenheder, og de regerende Magokraterne gjorde, hvad de kunne, for at holde sådanne begivenheder skjult for offentligheden. De mest magtfulde magikere blev sendt for at fange de unddragende dæmoner, men de befandt sig ofte håbløst overmatchede af den mægtige Legions ensomme agenter.",
    ["My hopes were to verify for my colleagues that this type of stone did possess magical properties, and if we wizards of Dalaran did not wish to exploit the power of bloodstones, we should at the least learn their properties, since our foes may one day use them against us.\r\n\r\nAnd so my studies began."] = "Mit håb var at bekræfte for mine kolleger, at denne type sten virkelig besad magiske egenskaber, og hvis vi Dalarn-troldmænd ikke ønskede at udnytte blodstenenes kraft, burde vi i det mindste lære deres egenskaber, for vores fjender kan en dag bruge dem imod os.\r\n\r\nOg så begyndte mine studier.",
    ["Ner'zhul, the Lich King, knew that his time was short. Imprisoned within the Frozen Throne, he suspected that Kil'jaeden would send his agents to destroy him. The damage caused by Illidan's spell had ruptured the Frozen Throne; thus, the Lich King was losing his power daily. Desperate to save himself, he called his greatest mortal servant to his side: the death knight Prince Arthas."] = "Ner'zhøl, Liskekongen, vidste at hans tid var kort. Fængslet i den Frossen Trone mistænkte han, at Kil'Dagen ville sende sine agenter for at tilintetgøre ham. Skaden forårsaget af Ilidans besværgelse havde sprængt den Frossen Trone; derfor tabte Liskekongen sin magt dag for dag. Desperat efter at redde sig selv kaldte han sin største dødelige tjener til sin side: dødsridderen Prins Arthæus.",
    ["Next, I'd advise you to travel back to Mulgore and seek out Cairne Bloodhoof in Thunder Bluff.\r\n\r\nCairne is the chieftain of the Bloodhoof tribe of Tauren, and it is by his grace that your people and the Earthen Ring have been given permission to establish yourselves in Mulgore.\r\n\r\nYou should already be familiar with the path to Thunder Bluff. Seek out the flight master in the center of Orgrimmar and take a riding wyvern to Thunder Bluff. Cairne can be found in the central plateau, just east of the great totem that serves as the wyvern roost in the city."] = "Næste skridt vil jeg råde dig til at tage: rejs tilbage til Mulgorr og søg Kærne Blodhov i Tordenklippe.\r\n\r\nKærne er høvdingen for Blodhov-stammen af Taurer, og det er takket være hans nåde, at dit folk og Jordringen har fået tilladelse til at etablere sig i Mulgorr.\r\n\r\nDu bør allerede kende vejen til Tordenklippe. Søg flyvemesteren i midten af Orgrimgrad og tag en ridevyvern til Tordenklippe. Kærne kan findes på det centrale plateau, lige øst for den store totem, der fungerer som vyvernernes rede i byen.",
    ["None of my new tests brought to light any revelations of the origin of bloodstone.  At the time the only riddle I solved was that bloodstone was neither living, nor dead!\r\n\r\nBut it was then, at the brink of failure, that a breakthrough was made.  My latest test involved a glass beaker whose brim was chipped, leaving a small, jagged space along its edge.  When the test was over, again revealing nothing, I went to clean my worktable and cut myself on the beaker."] = "Ingen af mine nye tests bragte nogen åbenbaringer om blodstenens oprindelse frem i lyset.  På det tidspunkt var den eneste gåde, jeg løste, at blodstenen hverken var levende eller død!\r\n\r\nMen netop da, på randen af fiasko, skete et gennembrud.  Min seneste test involverede et glasbæger, hvis kant var afskallet, så der var en lille, takket åbning langs kanten.  Da testen var forbi, og igen uden at afsløre noget, gik jeg for at gøre mit arbejdsbord rent og skar mig på bægeret.",
    ["Norgannon, the Titan lore keeper and master-magician, granted the blue dragon, Malygos, a portion of his vast power. From then on, Malygos would be known as the Spell-Weaver, the guardian of magic and hidden arcanum."] = "Norgannøn, titanernes lærdomsbevarer og mestermagiker, gav den blå drage Malygøs en del af sin enorme kraft. Fra da af skulle Malygøs kendes som Besværgelsesvæveren, vogteren af magi og det skjulte arkanum.",
    ["Once Sargeras saw that his armies were amassed and ready to follow his every command, he launched his raging forces into the vastness of the Great Dark. He referred to his growing army as the Burning Legion. To this date, it is still unclear how many worlds they consumed and burned on their unholy Burning Crusade across the universe."] = "Da Sargerås så, at hans hære var samlet og klar til at adlyde hver eneste af hans befalinger, slyngede han sine rasende styrker ud i det uendelige Store Mørke. Han kaldte sin voksende hær for Brændende Legion. Den dag i dag er det stadig uklart, hvor mange verdener de fortærede og brændte under deres uhellige Brændende Korstog på tværs af universet.",
    ["Once all his preparations had been made, Sargeras began his catastrophic invasion of Azeroth. The warrior-demons of the Burning Legion stormed into the world through the Well of Eternity and laid siege to the night elves' sleeping cities. Led by Archimonde and Mannoroth, the Legion swarmed over the lands of Kalimdor, leaving only ash and sorrow in its wake."] = "Engang alle hans forberedelser var gjort, indledte Sargerås sin katastrofale invasion af Azeroth. Krigsdæmonerne fra Brændende Legion stormede ind i verden gennem Evighedens Brønd og belejrede nattealfernes sovende byer. Anført af Archimonde og Mannoroth strømmede Legionen ind over Kalimdørs lande og efterlod kun aske og sorg i sin kølvand.",
    ["One such chieftain, Durotan of the Frostwolf clan, warned against the orcs' losing themselves to hate and fury. His words fell on deaf ears, however, as stronger chieftains such as Grom Hellscream of the Warsong clan stepped forward to champion the new age of warfare and dominance."] = "Én sådan høvding, Dorotan af Frostulv-klanen, advarede imod, at orkerne mistede sig selv til had og raseri. Hans ord faldt dog på døve ører, for stærkere høvdinge som Grom Helskrig af Krigssang-klanen trådte frem for at forsvare den nye tidsalder af krig og herredømme.",
    ["Only a few months after Nethergarde's completion, the energies of the dark portal coalesced and opened up a new gateway to Draenor. The remaining orc clans, under the leadership of the elder shaman, Ner'zhul, charged forth into Azeroth once again. Intent on stealing a number of magical artifacts that would increase Ner'zhul's power, the orcs planned to open up new portals in Draenor that would allow them to escape their doomed red world forever."] = "Kun få måneder efter Underverdensgardens fuldførelse samlede energierne fra den mørke portal sig og åbnede en ny port til Draenør. De resterende orkeklaner stormede under ledelse af den ældre shaman, Ner'zhøl, atter frem mod Azerot. Ivrige efter at stjæle en række magiske artefakter, der ville øge Ner'zhøls kraft, planlagde orkerne at åbne nye portaler i Draenør, så de kunne flygte fra deres dømte røde verden for evigt.",
    ["Or, is bloodstone made of blood?  And if so, then whose blood?  Mine?  The blood of any human?  Any animal?  \r\n\r\nOr maybe bloodstone is the blood of some unknown thing, the very thing that Kegan had both feared and revered when he handed me his pendant.\r\n\r\nThat is the question that must be answered.  It is the key."] = "Eller er blodsten lavet af blod?  Og hvis det er tilfældet, hvis blod så?  Mit?  Blodet fra et hvilket som helst menneske?  Et dyr?  \r\n\r\nEller er blodsten måske blodet fra en ukendt ting, den samme ting som Kegøn både frygtede og æred, da han rakte mig sit vedhæng.\r\n\r\nDet er spørgsmålet, der må besvares.  Det er nøglen.",
    ["Our Forsaken allies make their home in the land known as the Tirisfal Glades on the eastern continent. Deep beneath the ruins of a city once called Lordaeron you will find the Undercity.\r\n\r\nTo reach Tirisfal, exit the city via the great southern gate, and head east towards the zeppelin tower.\r\n\r\nBoard the zeppelin that docks at the south side of the tower. After crossing the great sea, you will arrive at the town of Brill. Simply head north from Brill into the ruins of Lordaeron.\r\n\r\nLocate the lift and ride it down into the depths of the Undercity and find the Dark Lady in the Royal Quarter. \r\n\r\nWord of warning, you may find the forsaken capital to be... unnerving."] = "Vores allierede De Forladte har hjem i landet kendt som Tirisfals Lysninger på det østlige kontinent. Dybt under ruinerne af en by, der engang hed Herrelande, finder du Undergrunden.\r\n\r\nFor at nå til Tirisfal, forlad byen gennem den store sydport og hold øst mod luftskibstårnet.\r\n\r\nGå om bord på luftskibet, der lægger til ved tårnets sydside. Efter du har krydset det store hav, ankommer du til byen Gryde-by. Gå blot nordpå fra Gryde-by ind i ruinerne af Herrelande.\r\n\r\nFind hejsen og tag den ned i dybet af Undergrunden, og find Den Mørke Dame i Det Kongelige Kvarter. \r\n\r\nEn advarsel: Du kan finde De Forladtes hovedstad at være... urovækkende.",
    ["Our world brims with history.  History of races new and old.  History behind wars long dead, and those which still smolder.  \r\n\r\nHistory of gods visiting from the skies.  And history of older gods who sleep in the earth.\r\n\r\nI speak now of those beings - the Old Gods.  They who dwelt and raged across Azeroth when the world was new."] = "Vores verden bugner af historie.  Historie om racer, nye og gamle.  Historie bag krige, længe døde, og dem der stadig ulmer.  \r\n\r\nHistorie om guder, der besøger fra himlen.  Og historie om ældre guder, der sover i jorden.\r\n\r\nJeg taler nu om disse væsener - De Gamle Guder.  De, der færdedes og raserede over Azerot, dengang verden var ny.",
    ["Outnumbered and driven mad by the curse of their bloodlust, the orcs inevitably fell before the wrath of the Alliance. Doomhammer was taken prisoner and escorted to Lordaeron while his broken clans were rounded up and hauled north - back to Lordaeron."] = "I undertal og drevet til vanvid af blodtørstens forbandelse faldt orkerne uundgåeligt for Alliancens vrede. Dømmehammer blev taget til fange og eskorteret til Herrelande, mens hans knuste klaner blev samlet op og slæbt nordpå - tilbage til Herrelande.",
    ["Over the course of a few months, the Horde eradicated nearly every draenei living on Draenor. Only a scattered handful of survivors managed to evade the orcs' awesome wrath. Flushed with victory, Gul'dan reveled in the Horde's power and might. Still, he knew that without any enemies to fight, the Horde would consume itself with endless infighting in its unstoppable appetite for glorious slaughter."] = "I løbet af få måneder udryddede Horden næsten hver eneste draenei, der levede på Draenør. Kun en spredt håndfuld overlevende formåede at undslippe orkernes vældige vrede. Opløftet af sejr svælgede Gul'dæn i Hordens magt og styrke. Alligevel vidste han, at uden fjender at kæmpe mod ville Horden fortære sig selv i endeløse interne kampe i sin ustoppelige appetit på herlig slagtning.",
    ["Over the course of six years, the cunning Arathi outmaneuvered and outfought the rival tribes. After every victory, the Arathi offered peace and equality to the conquered people; thus, they won the loyalty of those they had beaten. Eventually the Arathi tribe came to include many disparate tribes, and the ranks of its army grew vast."] = "I løbet af seks år overlistede og overkæmpede de snedige Arathi deres rivaliserende stammer. Efter hver sejr tilbød Arathi fred og lighed til det erobrede folk; således vandt de loyaliteten hos dem, de havde slået. Til sidst kom Arathi-stammen til at omfatte mange forskellige stammer, og rækkerne i dens hær voksede enorme.",
    ["Over time, demonic entities made their way into the Titans' worlds from the Twisting Nether, and the Pantheon elected its greatest warrior, Sargeras, to act as its first line of defense. A noble giant of molten bronze, Sargeras carried out his duties for countless millennia, seeking out and destroying these demons wherever he could find them. Over the eons, Sargeras encountered two powerful demonic races, both of which were bent on gaining power and dominance over the physical universe."] = "Med tiden trængte dæmoniske væsener ind i Titanernes verdener fra Tvistende Nether, og Panteonet valgte sin største kriger, Sargerås, til at fungere som dets første forsvarslinje. En ædel kæmpe af smeltet bronze udførte Sargerås sine pligter i utallige årtusinder og søgte og ødelagde disse dæmoner, hvor end han kunne finde dem. Gennem æonerne stødte Sargerås på to mægtige dæmoniske racer, begge besat af at opnå magt og herredømme over det fysiske univers.",
    ["Prosperity and the passing of years did little to ease the Dark Iron's rancor toward their cousins. Thaurissan and his sorceress wife, Modgud, launched a two-pronged assault against both Ironforge and Grim Batol. The Dark Irons were intent on claiming all of Khaz Modan for their own."] = "Velstand og årenes gang gjorde lidt for at lindre Mørkejernenes nag mod deres slægtninge. Tårissan og hans tryllekvinde-hustru, Modgud, indledte et tvespidset angreb mod både Jernsmede og Grimbatol. Mørkjernsdværgene var fast besluttet på at gøre krav på hele Khaz Mødan for sig selv.",
    ["Queen Azshara, overwhelmed by the terrible ecstasy of her magic, fell victim to Sargeras' undeniable power and agreed to grant him entrance to her world. Even her Highborne servitors gave themselves over to magic's inevitable corruption and began to worship Sargeras as their god. To show their allegiance to the Legion, the Highborne aided their queen in opening a vast, swirling portal within the depths of the Well of Eternity."] = "Dronning Azsyra, overvældet af sin magis forfærdelige ekstase, faldt offer for Sargeråss ubestridelige kraft og gik med til at give ham adgang til sin verden. Selv hendes højfødte tjenere overgav sig til magiens uundgåelige korruption og begyndte at tilbede Sargerås som deres gud. For at vise deres loyalitet over for Legionen hjalp de højfødte deres dronning med at åbne en vældig, hvirvlende portal i dybet af Evighedens Brønd.",
    ["Ragnaros the Firelord, immortal lord of all fire elementals, had been banished by the Titans when the world was young. Now, freed by Thaurissan's call, Ragnaros erupted into being once again. Ragnaros' apocalyptic rebirth into Azeroth shattered the Redridge Mountains and created a raging volcano at the center of the devastation."] = "Ragnarøs Ildherren, udødelig herre over alle ildelementarer, var blevet forvist af Titanerne, da verden var ung. Nu, befriet af Tårissans kald, brød Ragnarøs atter frem til live. Ragnarøs' apokalyptiske genfødsel i Azerot knuste Rødryg-bjergene og skabte en rasende vulkan i centrum af ødelæggelsen.",
    ["Recovered from the undersea ruins of Suramar, this functional astrolabe was crafted by the highborne night elves nearly twelve thousand years ago. The highborne, obsessed with magic, the occult and astronomy, developed a series of ingenious apparatuses. This device provides invaluable insights into the ancient night elves' level of scientific understanding."] = "Genfundet fra de undersøiske ruiner i Suramar blev dette funktionelle astrolabium fremstillet af de højfødte nattealfer for næsten tolv tusind år siden. De højfødte, besat af magi, det okkulte og astronomi, udviklede en række geniale apparater. Denne genstand giver uvurderlig indsigt i de gamle nattealfers niveau af videnskabelig forståelse.",
    ["Sargeras gathered his vast Burning Legion and made his way towards the unsuspecting world of Azeroth. The Legion was comprised of a million screaming demons, all ripped from the far corners of the universe, and the demons hungered for conquest. Sargeras' lieutenants, Archimonde the Defiler and Mannoroth the Destructor, prepared their infernal minions to strike."] = "Sargerås samlede sin vældige Brændende Legion og drog mod den uvidende verden Azerot. Legionen bestod af en million skrigende dæmoner, alle revet fra universets fjerneste hjørner, og dæmonerne hungrede efter erobring. Sargeråss løjtnanter, Archimonde Skænderen og Mannoroth Destruktoren, forberedte deres helvedesbæst-håndlangere til at slå til.",
    ["Satisfied that the small world had been ordered and that their work was done, the Titans prepared to leave Azeroth. However, before they departed, they charged the greatest species of the world with the task of watching over Kalimdor, lest any force should threaten its perfect tranquility. In that age, there were many dragonflights."] = "Tilfredse med at den lille verden var blevet ordnet, og at deres arbejde var gjort, forberedte Titanerne sig på at forlade Azerot. Men før de tog af sted, betroede de verdens største art opgaven med at holde øje med Kalimdør, for at ingen styrke skulle true dens perfekte ro. I den tidsalder fandtes der mange drageflugter.",
    ["Seeking to punish the wayward orcs for their costly betrayal, Doomhammer sent his forces to kill Gul'dan and bring the renegades back into the fold. For his recklessness, Gul'dan was torn apart by the maddened demons he had set loose. With their leader dead, the renegade clans quickly fell before Doomhammer's enraged legions."] = "For at straffe de afvigende orker for deres dyre forræderi sendte Dømmehammer sine styrker af sted for at dræbe Gul'dæn og bringe renegaterne tilbage i folden. For sin letsindighed blev Gul'dæn revet fra hinanden af de rasende dæmoner, han havde sluppet løs. Da deres leder var død, faldt de frafaldne klaner hurtigt for Dømmehammers rasende legioner.",
    ["Seeking to retain relations and trade with their cousins, the dwarves of Ironforge constructed two massive arches, the Thandol Span, to bridge the gap between Khaz Modan and Lordaeron. Bolstered by mutual trade, the two kingdoms prospered. After the deaths of Madoran and Khardros, their sons jointly commissioned two great statues in honor of their fathers."] = "Med ønsket om at bevare forbindelser og handel med deres slægtninge byggede dværgene fra Jernsmede to massive buer, Thandol-spændet, for at bygge bro over kløften mellem Khaz Mødan og Herrelande. Styrket af gensidig handel blomstrede de to kongeriger. Efter Madorans og Khardros' død lod deres sønner i fællesskab opføre to store statuer til ære for deres fædre.",
    ["She believed that the ancient elves and the elderly men who presided over the council were too rigid in their thinking and not farsighted enough to put a decisive end to the conflict against chaos. Impatient with lengthy discussion and debate, she yearned to prove herself worthy to her peers and superiors, and as a result frequently chose valor over wisdom in crucial situations."] = "Hun mente, at de gamle alfer og de ældre mænd, der præsiderede over rådet, var for stive i deres tankegang og ikke fremsynede nok til at sætte et afgørende punkt for konflikten mod kaos. Utålmodig med lange diskussioner og debatter længtes hun efter at bevise sig værdig over for sine ligemænd og overordnede, og som følge heraf valgte hun ofte tapperhed frem for visdom i afgørende situationer.",
    ["Silvia Valor, Raven Hill Guard\r\n\r\nSilvia Valor had already been a local hero by the time she was offered to join the Guard. If there was one thing she could not stand to suffer more than anything, it was opportunists who took advantage of those who were struggling.\r\n\r\nBandits, con artists, rabble-rousers, it didn't matter. Silvia put each to the sword for trying to sow chaos in her beloved home. It was only natural she would be put in a position of real authority to act out her vision of justice.\r\n\r\nIt's said that, until she drew her last breath, she would never abandon the farmsteads and homes of Duskwood. And perhaps not even then."] = "Silvia Tapper, Ravnehøj-vagten\r\n\r\nSilvia Tapper havde allerede været en lokal helt, da hun blev tilbudt at slutte sig til Vagten. Hvis der var én ting, hun næppe kunne tåle mere end noget andet, var det opportunister, der udnyttede dem, der kæmpede.\r\n\r\nBanditter, svindlere, oprørsmagere, det var det samme. Silvia lagde hver enkelt under sværdet, fordi de forsøgte at så kaos i hendes elskede hjem. Det var kun naturligt, at hun ville blive sat i en position med reel autoritet til at udleve sin vision om retfærdighed.\r\n\r\nDet siges, at indtil hun trak sit sidste åndedrag, ville hun aldrig forlade gårdene og hjemmene i Skumringsskoven. Og måske ikke engang da.",
    ["Some fear our kind more than dragons. Some envy us more than the most skilled blacksmiths. Some praise our strength in battle. Others revel in our faith. Some are just jealous that we can drink them under the table! But know this, $c, you are among the most elite protectors in all of Azeroth. The Holy Light gives us strength as much as we strengthen it.$B$BI would tell you more when you've gotten acquainted with the land some. Find me inside Anvilmar above the Valley.$B$B-Bromos Grummner, Paladin Trainer"] = "Nogle frygter vores slags mere end drager. Nogle misunder os mere end de dygtigste smede. Nogle roser vores styrke i slag. Andre svælger i vores tro. Nogle er bare misundelige, fordi vi kan drikke dem under bordet! Men det skal du vide, $c, du er blandt de elitebeskyttere i hele Azerot. Det Hellige Let giver os styrke, lige så meget som vi styrker det.$B$BJeg vil fortælle dig mere, når du har gjort dig lidt bekendt med landet. Find mig inde i Ambolmar ovenfor Dalen.$B$B-Bromos Grumsner, Korsridder-træner",
    ["Spying the primordial world of Azeroth and sensing the limitless energies of the Well of Eternity, Sargeras was consumed by an insatiable hunger. The great dark god of the Nameless Void resolved to destroy the fledgling world and claim its energies as his own."] = "Da Sargerås så Azeroths urgamle verden og fornemmede de grænseløse energier i Evighedens Brønd, blev han fortæret af en umættelig sult. Den store mørke gud fra Det Navnløse Tomrum besluttede at tilintetgøre den spæde verden og tilegne sig dens energier som sine egne.",
    ["Still convinced that Gul'dan's corruption would destroy his people, Durotan spoke out against the warlocks once more. The brave warrior claimed that warlocks were destroying the purity of the orcish spirit and that this reckless invasion would be their doom. Gul'dan, unable to risk killing such a popular hero, was forced to exile Durotan and his Frostwolf Clan into the far reaches of this new world."] = "Stadig overbevist om at Gul'dæns korruption ville tilintetgøre hans folk, talte Dorotan endnu engang imod heksemestrene. Den modige kriger påstod, at heksemestrene ødelagde den orkiske ånds renhed, og at dette hensynsløse felttog ville blive deres undergang. Gul'dæn, der ikke turde risikere at dræbe en så populær helt, var tvunget til at forvise Dorotan og hans Frostulv-klan til de fjerneste egne af denne nye verden.",
    ["Strom continued to act as the central hub of Arathor, but as with Dalaran, many new city-states arose across the continent of Lordaeron. Gilneas, Alterac, and Kul Tiras were the first city-states to arise, and although they each had their own customs and commercial workings, they all held to the unifying authority of Strom."] = "Storm fortsatte med at fungere som Arators centrale knudepunkt, men ligesom med Dalarn opstod der mange nye bystater på tværs af kontinentet Herrelande. Gilnæas, Alterac og Kul Tirask var de første bystater, der opstod, og selvom de hver især havde deres egne skikke og handelsforhold, bøjede de sig alle for Stormens samlende autoritet.",
    ["TO-DO\r\n\r\nPack equipment for hunting trip\r\nMake utility hooks for Grund's belt\r\nFix welding visor\r\nSend Mom a card\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nPage 45"] = "SKAL-GØRES\r\n\r\nPak udstyr til jagturen\r\nLav nyttekroge til Grumles bælte\r\nRet svejsehjelmens visir\r\nSend mor et kort\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSide 45",
    ["That is what Kegan uttered as he handed his bloodstone pendant to me, and there was fear, and maybe reverence, in his eyes as he did so.  And as his hands met with mine they lingered, as if reluctant to give up the pendant.  Revulsion swept through me, yet to this day I know not if I reviled against his dead flesh pressed to mine, or if the pendant itself made my skin crawl.\r\n\r\nFor I felt a power within it.  A deep, hidden, hungry power.  And one yearning for release."] = "Sådan sagde Kegøn, da han rakte mig sin blodstenshalskæde, og der var frygt, og måske ærefrygt, i hans øjne, mens han gjorde det.  Og da hans hænder mødte mine, blev de hængende, som om han var tøvende med at give halskæden fra sig.  En væmmelse for gennem mig, men den dag i dag ved jeg ikke, om jeg afskyede hans døde kød presset mod mit, eller om det var halskæden selv, der fik min hud til at krybe.\r\n\r\nFor jeg kunne mærke en kraft i den.  En dyb, skjult, sulten kraft.  Og en, der længtes efter at blive sluppet fri.",
    ["The Alliance armies led by Sir Anduin Lothar, Uther the Lightbringer, and Admiral Daelin Proudmoore pushed the orcs south into the shattered land of Azeroth - the first kingdom to fall before the orcs' ruthless onslaught.\r\n\r\nThe Alliance forces under Sir Lothar managed to push Doomhammer's clans out of Lordaeron and back into the orc-controlled lands of Azeroth. Lothar's forces surrounded the orcs' volcanic citadel of Blackrock Spire and laid siege to their defenses."] = "Alliancens hære, ledet af Ridder Anduin Lotar, Uther Lysbringer og Admiral Daelin Stoltmoor, drev orkerne sydpå ind i det knuste land Azerot - det første kongerige, der faldt for orkernes ubarmhjertige angreb.\r\n\r\nAlliance-styrkerne under Ridder Lotar formåede at drive Dømmehammers klaner ud af Herrelande og tilbage ind i de orkkontrollerede egne af Azerot. Lotars styrker omringede orkernes vulkanske citadel Sortklippe-spiret og lagde belejring til deres forsvar.",
    ["The Bronzebeard clan, ruled by Thane Madoran Bronzebeard, held close ties to the High King and stood as the traditional defenders of Ironforge Mountain. The Wildhammer clan, ruled by Thane Khardros Wildhammer, inhabited the foothills and crags around the base of the mountain and sought to gain more control within the city."] = "Bronzeskæg-klanen, styret af Thane Madoran Bronzeskæg, havde tætte bånd til Overkongen og stod som de traditionelle forsvarere af Jernsmedebjerget. Vildhammer-klanen, styret af Thane Khardros Vildhammer, boede i højderne og klipperne ved bjergets fod og søgte at få mere kontrol i byen.",
    ["The Bronzebeards returned to Ironforge and rebuilt their glorious city. The Wildhammers also returned home to Grim Batol. However, the death of the Modgud had left an evil stain on the mountain fortress, and the Wildhammers found it uninhabitable."] = "Bronzeskæggene vendte tilbage til Jernsmede og genopbyggede deres glorværdige by. Vildhammerne vendte også hjem til Grimbatol. Men Modguds død havde efterladt en ond plet på bjergfæstningen, og Vildhammerne fandt den ubeboelig.",
    ["The Council of Silvermoon, which ruled over the elves of Quel'Thalas, entered into a secret pact with the Magocrat lords of Dalaran. The elves told the Magocrats about the history of ancient Kalimdor and of the Burning Legion, a history which still threatened the world. They informed the humans that so long as they used magic, they would need to protect their citizenry from the malicious agents of the Legion."] = "Sølvmåne-rådet, der regerede over alferne i Quel'Thalas, indgik en hemmelig pagt med Magokrat-herrerne i Dalarn. Alferne fortalte Magokraterne om det oldtidige Kalimdør og om Brændende Legion, en historie der stadig truede verden. De oplyste menneskene om, at så længe de brugte magi, måtte de beskytte deres borgere mod Legionens ondsindede agenter.",
    ["The Dark Iron armies smashed against their cousins' strongholds and very nearly took both kingdoms. However, Madoran Bronzebeard ultimately led his clan to a decisive victory over Thaurissan's sorcerous army. Thaurissan and his servants fled back to the safety of their city, unaware of the events transpiring at Grim Batol, where Modgud's army would fare no better against Khardros and his Wildhammer warriors."] = "Mørkejern-hærene smadrede ind i deres fætres højborge og tog næsten begge kongeriger. Men Madoran Bronzeskæg førte til sidst sin klan til en afgørende sejr over Tårissans tryllekyndige hær. Tårissan og hans tjenere flygtede tilbage til deres bys sikkerhed, uvidende om de begivenheder, der udspillede sig i Grimbatol, hvor Modguds hær ikke ville klare sig bedre mod Khardros og hans Vildhammer-krigere.",
    ["The Earthmother's eyes shone down upon the lands she had breathed into creation. Her right eye, An'she (the sun), gave warmth and light to the land. Her left eye, Mu'sha (the moon), gave peace and sleep to the stirring creatures of the dawning. Such was the power of her gaze that the Earthmother closed one dreaming eye for every turning of the sky. Thus, her loving gaze turned day into night for the first dawning of the world."] = "Jordmoderens øjne skinnede ned over de lande, hun havde indblæst til live. Hendes højre øje, Ånd'she (solen), gav land varme og lys. Hendes venstre øje, Mu'sja (månen), gav fred og søvn til de urolige væsener i gryningen. Så stor var kraften i hendes blik, at Jordmoderen lukkede ét drømmende øje for hver omdrejning af himlen. Således forvandlede hendes kærlige blik dag til nat ved verdens første gry.",
    ["The Guardian power was so great that only the Council of Tirisfal was allowed to choose potential successors to the mantle of Guardianship. Whenever a Guardian grew too old, or wearied of the secret war against chaos, the Council chose a new champion, and under controlled conditions, formally channeled the Guardian power into its new agent."] = "Vogterkraften var så stor, at kun Tirisfal-rådet fik lov til at udpege mulige efterfølgere til vogterskabets kappe. Når en vogter blev for gammel eller trådt træt af den hemmelige krig mod kaos, valgte rådet en ny mester og kanaliserede under kontrollerede forhold formelt vogterkraften over i sin nye agent.",
    ["The Highborne's reckless use of magic sent ripples of energy spiraling out from the Well of Eternity and into the Great Dark Beyond. The streaming ripples of energy were felt by terrible alien minds. Sargeras - the Great Enemy of all life, the Destroyer of Worlds - felt the potent ripples and was drawn to their distant point of origin."] = "De Højfødtes hensynsløse brug af magi sendte bølger af energi snoende op fra Evighedens Brønd og ud i Det Store Mørke derhenne. De strømmende energibølger blev mærket af frygtindgydende fremmede sind. Sargerås - alt livs Store Fjende, Verdensødelæggeren - mærkede de kraftfulde bølger og blev draget mod deres fjerne udspring.",
    ["The Horde, now led by Warchief Doomhammer, brought in ogres from its homeworld of Draenor and conscripted the disenfranchised Amani forest trolls into its fold. Setting out on a massive campaign to overrun the dwarf kingdom of Khaz Modan and the southern reaches of Lordaeron, the Horde effortlessly decimated all opposition."] = "Horden, nu anført af Krigshøvding Dømmehammer, hentede oger fra sin hjemverden Draenør og indlemmede de udstødte Amani-skovtrolde i sine rækker. Horden satte i gang en massiv kampagne for at overrumple dværgekongeriget Khaz Mødan og Herrelandenes sydlige udkant, og den nedkæmpede al modstand uden besvær.",
    ["The Magocrats proposed the notion of empowering a single mortal champion who would utilize their powers in order to fight a never-ending secret war against the Legion. It was stressed that the majority of mankind could never know about the Guardians or the threat of the Legion for fear that they would riot in fear and paranoia. The elves agreed to the proposal and founded a secret society that would watch over the selection of the Guardian and help to stem the rise of chaos in the world."] = "Magokraterne foreslog tanken om at give én dødelig mester kraft til at bruge deres magi i en evig, hemmelig krig mod Legionen. Det blev understreget, at størstedelen af menneskeheden aldrig måtte få kendskab til vogterne eller truslen fra Legionen, af frygt for at de ville gå amok i frygt og paranoia. Elverne accepterede forslaget og grundlagde et hemmeligt samfund, der skulle holde øje med udvælgelsen af vogteren og hjælpe med at standse kaosets fremmarch i verden.",
    ["The Old Gods are the will of our world.  In every storm there roars the laughter of an Old God.  The blaze of a wildfire is the heat of their gaze.  As Old Gods walk, the earth trembles and breaks, and lesser things scream and tear at their own flesh in despair.\r\n\r\nAnd despair they should, for just as fire shows no mercy to a child's curious hand, the Old Gods have no care for those beneath them.  At best, we are pawns.  At worst, we are playthings."] = "De Gamle Guder er vores verdens vilje.  I hver storm buldrer en Gammel Guds latter.  Glimtet fra en skovbrand er varmen fra deres blik.  Når De Gamle Guder går, bæver jorden og revner, og de mindre væsner skriger og river i eget kød i fortvivlelse.\r\n\r\nOg fortvivlet bør de være, for ligesom ild ikke viser nogen nåde over for et barns nysgerrige hånd, har De Gamle Guder ingen omsorg for dem under sig.  I bedste fald er vi brikker.  I værste fald er vi legetøj.",
    ["The Pantheon shattered the Old Gods' citadels and chained the five evil gods far beneath the surface of the world. Without the Old Gods' power to keep their raging spirits bound to the physical world, the elementals were banished to an abyssal plane, where they would contend with one another for all eternity. With the elementals' departure, nature calmed, and the world settled into a peaceful harmony. The Titans saw that the threat was contained and set to work."] = "Panteonet knuste De Gamle Guders citadeller og lænkede de fem onde guder dybt under verdens overflade. Uden De Gamle Guders magt til at holde deres rasende ånder bundet til den fysiske verden blev elementarerne forvist til et afgrundsplan, hvor de skulle kæmpe mod hinanden i al evighed. Med elementarernes afgang faldt naturen til ro, og verden fandt sig til rette i en fredfyldt harmoni. Titanerne så, at truslen var indesluttet, og gik straks i gang.",
    ["The Pantheon, disturbed by the Old Gods' penchant for evil, waged war upon the elementals and their dark masters. The Old Gods' armies were led by the most powerful elemental lieutenants: Ragnaros the Firelord, Therazane the Stonemother, Al'Akir the Windlord, and Neptulon the Tidehunter."] = "Panteonet, der var foruroliget over De Gamle Guders tilbøjelighed til det onde, førte krig mod elementarerne og deres mørke herrer. De Gamle Guders hære blev anført af de mægtigste elementare løjtnanter: Ragnarøs Ildherre, Terazane Stenmoderen, Al'Akir Vindherren og Neptunor Tidevandsjægeren.",
    ["The Titans empowered a number of races to help them fashion the world. To help them carve out the fathomless caverns beneath the earth, the Titans created the dwarf-like earthen from magical, living stone. To help them dredge out the seas and lift the land from the sea floor, the Titans created the immense but gentle sea giants. For many ages the Titans moved and shaped the earth, until at last there remained one perfect continent."] = "Titanerne bemyndigede en række racer til at hjælpe dem med at forme verden. For at hjælpe dem med at udhugge de bundløse huler under jorden skabte Titanerne de dværgelignende jordfolk af magisk, levende sten. For at hjælpe dem med at udgrave havene og løfte landet fra havbunden skabte Titanerne de enorme, men milde havgiganter. I mange tidsaldre flyttede og formede Titanerne jorden, indtil der til sidst kun var tilbage ét perfekt kontinent.",
    ["The Venture Company <illegible text> It would seem that the fools nearly wiped out their entire operation in trying to stabilize the mixture.\r\n\r\n<several pages appear to be torn out>"] = "Ventureselskabet <ulæselig tekst> Det ser ud til, at tosserne næsten udslettede hele deres operation i forsøget på at stabilisere blandingen.\r\n\r\n<flere sider ser ud til at være revet ud>",
    ["The bearer of this certificate is entitled to the respect and regard that any first rate pilferer and thief deserves."] = "Indehaveren af dette certifikat er berettiget til den respekt og agtelse, som enhver førsteklasses lommetyv og tyv fortjener.",
    ["The beautiful young priestess, Tyrande, agreed to accompany the brothers in the name of Elune. Though Malfurion and Illidan shared a love for the idealistic priestess, Tyrande's heart belonged to Malfurion alone. Illidan resented his brother's budding romance with Tyrande, but knew that his heartache was nothing compared to the pain of his magical addiction."] = "Den smukke unge præstinde, Tyrande, indvilligede i at ledsage brødrene i Elunies navn. Selvom Malfurion og Ilidan begge delte kærligheden til den idealistiske præstinde, tilhørte Tyrandes hjerte kun Malfurion. Ilidan harmedes over sin brors spirende romance med Tyrande, men vidste, at hans hjertesorg intet var i forhold til smerten ved hans magiske afhængighed.",
    ["The bewildered Doomhammer, having lost nearly half of his standing forces to Gul'dan's treachery, was forced to pull back and forsake his greatest chance at victory over the Alliance."] = "Den forvirrede Dømmehammer, der havde mistet næsten halvdelen af sine faste styrker til Gul'dæns forræderi, var tvunget til at trække sig tilbage og give afkald på sin største chance for sejr over Alliancen.",
    ["The blood that had spilled near the bloodstone pendant was slowly moving toward the piece of jewelry, as if gravity had somehow bent itself toward the bloodstone.  The blood that touched the pendant seemed to disappear, and the red color of the stone deepened as it drank more of my blood."] = "Blodet, der var spildt nær blodstenshalskæden, bevægede sig langsomt hen mod smykket, som om tyngdekraften på en eller anden måde havde bøjet sig mod blodstenen.  Blodet, der berørte halskæden, syntes at forsvinde, og stenens røde farve blev dybere, efterhånden som den drak mere af mit blod.",
    ["The citizens of Dalaran tolerated the magicians' endeavors and built up a bustling economy under the protection of their magic-using defenders. Yet, as more and more magicians practiced their arts, the fabric of reality around Dalaran began to weaken and tear."] = "Dalarns borgere tolererede magikernes bestræbelser og opbyggede en travl økonomi under beskyttelse af deres magibrugende forsvarere. Men efterhånden som flere og flere magikere udøvede deres kunst, begyndte virkelighedens væv omkring Dalarn at svækkes og rives op.",
    ["The city-state of Kul Tiras, founded upon a large island south of Lordaeron, developed a prosperous economy based on fishing and shipping. Over time, Kul Tiras built up a mighty fleet of merchant vessels that sailed throughout the known lands in search of exotic goods to trade and sell. Yet even as the economy of Arathor flourished, its strongest elements began to disintegrate."] = "Bystaten Kul Tirask, grundlagt på en stor ø syd for Herrelande, udviklede en blomstrende økonomi baseret på fiskeri og skibsfart. Med tiden opbyggede Kul Tirask en mægtig flåde af handelsskibe, der sejlede over alle kendte lande på jagt efter eksotiske varer at handle og sælge. Men selvom Arators økonomi blomstrede, begyndte dens stærkeste dele at gå i opløsning.",
    ["The combined armies of Ironforge and Grim Batol then turned south, intent on destroying Thaurissan and his Dark Irons once and for all. They had not gone far when Thaurissan's fury resulted in a spell of cataclysmic proportions. Seeking to summon a supernatural minion that would ensure his victory, Thaurissan called upon the ancient powers sleeping beneath the world. To his shock, and ultimately his doom, the creature that emerged was more terrible than any nightmare he could have imagined."] = "De forenede hære fra Jernsmede og Grimbatol drejede så mod syd, fast besluttet på at tilintetgøre Tårissan og hans Mørkjernsdværgene én gang for alle. De var ikke kommet langt, før Tårissans raseri udløste en besværgelse af kataklysmiske dimensioner. I forsøget på at tilkalde en overnaturlig håndlanger, der ville sikre hans sejr, påkaldte Tårissan de oldgamle kræfter, der sov under verden. Til hans chok, og i sidste ende hans undergang, var skabningen, der trådte frem, mere forfærdelig end noget mareridt, han kunne have forestillet sig.",
    ["The cult hit us by surprise. Raani never saw it coming and Arvensus took a sword to the gut. For my part, I took a lightning bolt to the chest and blacked out. They never bothered to finish me off... I guess they assumed my wounds would do me in. When it's all said and done, I suspect they might."] = "Kulten ramte os med et overraskelsesangreb. Ræni så det aldrig komme, og Arvensus fik et sværd i maven. Selv fik jeg et lynangreb i brystet og besvimede. De gad aldrig at gøre ende på mig... Jeg gætter på, at de regnede med, at mine sår ville klare jobbet. Når det hele er sagt og gjort, mistænker jeg, at de nok skal klare det.",
    ["The cut was not deep but nevertheless bled fiercely.  Before I could wrap my injured finger in a bandage, a good deal of my blood had spilled on my worktable.\r\n\r\nAnd as I was cleaning up this new mess, I noticed the strangest thing..."] = "Snitet var ikke dybt, men det blødte kraftigt.  Før jeg kunne vikle min sårede finger ind i en forbinding, var en god del af mit blod spildt på mit arbejdsbord.\r\n\r\nOg mens jeg gjorde rent i dette nye rod, bemærkede jeg det mærkeligste...",
    ["The demon warlocks called down searing infernals that crashed like hellish meteors into the graceful spires of Kalimdor's temples. A band of burning, bloodletting killers known as the Doomguard marched across Kalimdor's fields, slaughtering everyone in their path. Packs of wild, demonic felhounds ravaged the countryside unopposed. Though the brave Kaldorei warriors rushed to defend their ancient homeland, they were forced to give ground, inch by inch, before the fury of the Legion's onslaught."] = "Dæmonhekserne tilkaldte brændende infernaler, der styrtede ned som helvedes meteorer mod Kalimdørs templers yndefulde spir. En flok brændende, blodtørstige mordere kendt som Domvagterne marcherede hen over Kalimdørs marker og slagtede alle på deres vej. Flokke af vilde, dæmoniske felhunde hærgede landskabet uden modstand. Selvom de modige kaldoriske krigere skyndte sig at forsvare deres gamle hjemland, blev de tvunget til at give slip på jorden tomme for tomme over for Legionens angrebs raseri.",
    ["The descendents of the Arathi, left within the crumbling walls of ancient Strom, decided to travel south past the rocky mountains of Khaz Modan. Their journey finally ended after many long seasons, and they settled in the northern region of the continent they would name Azeroth. In a fertile valley they founded the kingdom of Stormwind, which quickly became a self-sufficient power in its own right."] = "Arathis efterkommere, efterladt i de smuldrende mure af det gamle Storm, besluttede at drage sydpå forbi Khaz Mødans klippefulde bjerge. Deres rejse endte endelig efter mange lange sæsoner, og de slog sig ned i den nordlige del af kontinentet, som de ville kalde Azerot. I en frugtbar dal grundlagde de kongeriget Stormvind, som hurtigt blev en selvforsynende magt i sin egen ret.",
    ["The devastating Second War against the orcish horde left the Alliance of Lordaeron in a state of shock and disarray. The bloodthirsty orcs, led by the mighty warchief, Orgrim Doomhammer, not only smashed their way through the dwarf-held lands of Khaz Modan, but had razed many of Lordaeron's central provinces as well. The unrelenting orcs even succeeded in ravaging the\r\nelves' remote kingdom of Quel'Thalas before their rampage was finally stopped."] = "Den ødelæggende Anden Krig mod orkehorden efterlod Herrelandenes Alliance i chok og kaos. De blodtørstige orker, anført af den mægtige krigshøvding Orgrim Dømmehammer, bragede ikke blot igennem de dværgeholdte lande Khaz Mødan, men havde også jævnet mange af Herrelandenes centrale provinser med jorden. De ubarmhjertige orker formåede endda at hærge\r\nelvernes fjerne rige Quel'Thalas, før deres raseri endelig blev stoppet.",
    ["The dwarves of Ironforge Mountain lived in peace for many long centuries. However, their society grew too large within the confines of their mountain cities. Though the mighty High King, Modimus Anvilmar, ruled over all dwarves with justice and wisdom, three powerful factions had arisen amongst the dwarven society."] = "Dværgene på Jernsmedebjerget levede i fred i mange lange århundreder. Deres samfund blev dog for stort inden for rammerne af deres bjergbyer. Selvom den mægtige Overkonge Modimus Ambolmar herskede over alle dværge med retfærdighed og visdom, var der opstået tre magtfulde fraktioner i det dværgiske samfund.",
    ["The dwarves, by nature fascinated with shaping gems and stone, set out to mine the surrounding mountains for riches and precious minerals. Content with their labors under the world, the dwarves remained isolated from the affairs of their surface-dwelling neighbors."] = "Dværgene, der af natur var fascineret af at forme ædelsten og sten, drog ud for at grave i de omkringliggende bjerge efter rigdomme og dyrebare mineraler. Tilfredse med deres arbejde under jorden forblev dværgene isolerede fra deres overfladeboende naboers anliggender.",
    ["The elves found that although humans were innately clumsy in their handling of magic, they possessed a startling natural affinity for it. One hundred men were taught the very basics of the elves' magical secrets: no more than was absolutely necessary to combat the trolls. Convinced that their human students were ready to aid in the struggle, the elves left Strom and traveled north alongside the mighty armies of King Thoradin."] = "Elverne opdagede, at selvom menneskene var medfødt klodsede i deres håndtering af magi, besad de en forbløffende naturlig affinitet til den. Hundrede mænd blev lært de allerførste af elvernes magiske hemmeligheder: ikke mere end absolut nødvendigt for at bekæmpe trolderne. Overbevist om at deres menneskelige elever var klar til at hjælpe i kampen, forlod elverne Storm og rejste nordpå sammen med Konge Torradins mægtige hære.",
    ["The elves informed Thoradin that the troll armies were vast and that once the trolls had destroyed Quel'Thalas, they would move on to attack the southlands. The desperate elves, in dire need of military aid, hastily agreed to teach certain select humans to wield magic in exchange for their help against the warbands."] = "Elverne fortalte Torradin, at trolde-hærene var enorme, og at når trollene havde ødelagt Quel'Thalas, ville de rykke videre for at angribe sydlandene. De desperate elver, i stort behov for militær hjælp, indvilligede hastigt i at lære visse udvalgte mennesker at mestre magi til gengæld for deres hjælp mod krigsbanderne.",
    ["The elves, led at that time by Anasterian Sunstrider, were largely uninterested in the coming conflict. However, they were duty-bound to aid Lothar because he was the last descendent of the Arathi bloodline, which had aided the elves in ages past."] = "Elverne, dengang anført af Anasterian Solvandrer, var stort set uinteresserede i den kommende konflikt. Alligevel var de pligtbundne til at hjælpe Lotar, fordi han var den sidste efterkommer af Arathi-slægten, som i fordums tid havde hjulpet elverne.",
    ["The epic battles of the Second War ranged from large-scale naval skirmishes to massive aerial dogfights. Somehow the Horde had unearthed a powerful artifact known as the Demon Soul and used it to enslave the ancient Dragonqueen, Alexstrasza. Threatening to destroy her precious eggs, the Horde forced Alexstrasza to send her grown children to war. The noble red dragons were forced to fight for the Horde, and fight they did."] = "De episke slag under den Anden Krig strakte sig fra storstilede flådeskærmydsler til massive luftkampe. På en eller anden måde havde Horden gravet en magtfuld artefakt frem, kendt som Dæmonsjælen, og brugt den til at træle den gamle Drageronning Aleksstrasa. Med trusler om at ødelægge hendes dyrebare æg tvang Horden Aleksstrasa til at sende sine fuldvoksne børn i krig. De ædle røde drager blev tvunget til at kæmpe for Horden, og kæmpe det gjorde de.",
    ["The eredar, an insidious race of devilish sorcerers, used their warlock magics to invade and enslave a number of worlds. The indigenous races of those worlds were mutated by the eredar's malevolent powers and turned into demons themselves."] = "Eredarerne, en snigende race af djævelske tryllekarle, brugte deres hekseri til at invadere og træle en række verdener. De oprindelige racer på disse verdener blev muteret af eredarernes ondskabsfulde kræfter og forvandlet til dæmoner selv.",
    ["The few warriors still left in Strom decided to remain and guard the ancient walls of their city. Strom was no longer the center of the empire, but it developed into a new nation known as Stromgarde. Though each of the city-states became prosperous in its own right, the empire of Arathor had effectively disintegrated. As each nation developed its own customs and beliefs, they became increasingly segregated from one another. King Thoradin's vision of a unified humanity had faded at last."] = "De få krigere, der stadig var tilbage i Storm, besluttede at blive og vogte byens gamle mure. Storm var ikke længere imperiets centrum, men det udviklede sig til en ny nation kendt som Strømgård. Selvom hver af bystaterne blev velstående i sin egen ret, var Arator-imperiet reelt gået i opløsning. Efterhånden som hver nation udviklede sine egne skikke og overbevisninger, blev de mere og mere adskilt fra hinanden. Konge Torradins vision om en samlet menneskehed var endelig visnet hen.",
    ["The furrowed gaze of the orcish warrior lies upon the map, and reveals the key\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nPage 155"] = "Den orkiske krigers rynkede blik hviler på kortet og afslører nøglen\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSide 155",
    ["The guards of this tower seem to be especially weak to my attacks. As I was scouting the backside of the tower, a patroller spotted me and attacked. I was able to easily dispatch the guard with a timely gouge followed by a backstab. \r\n\r\nI waited in hiding for her partner to come investigate the commotion. The patroller came towards the bushes where I had dragged the corpse and began a search. Slowly, carefully, I crept up behind him, not wanting my ambush to be discovered."] = "Vagterne i dette tårn virker særlig svage over for mine angreb. Mens jeg spejdede bagsiden af tårnet, øjnede en patruljerende mig og angreb. Jeg kunne nemt sende vagten til tælling med et velplaceret gouge-slag efterfulgt af et baghold. \r\n\r\nJeg ventede skjult på, at hendes makker skulle komme og undersøge balladen. Patruljeren kom hen mod buskene, hvor jeg havde slæbt liget hen, og begyndte at lede. Langsomt og forsigtigt listede jeg mig op bag ham, for jeg ville ikke have, at mit baghold blev opdaget.",
    ["The human society of Arathor grew and prospered, yet Thoradin, fearful that his kingdom would splinter apart if it overextended itself, maintained that Strom was the center of the Arathorian empire. After many peaceful years of growth and commerce, mighty Thoradin died of old age, leaving Arathor's younger generation free to expand the empire beyond the lands of Strom."] = "Arators menneskelige samfund voksede og trivedes, men Torradin, bange for at hans rige ville splintres, hvis det strakte sig for langt, fastholdt, at Storm var centrum for det arathoriske imperium. Efter mange fredelige år med vækst og handel døde den mægtige Torradin af alderdom og efterlod Arators yngre generation frie til at udvide imperiet ud over Storms lande.",
    ["The hundred human magi and a multitude of elven sorcerers called down the fury of the heavens and set the troll armies ablaze. The elemental fires prevented the trolls from regenerating their wounds and burned their tortured forms from the inside out."] = "De hundrede menneskelige magikere og en mængde elviske tryllekarle kaldte himlens raseri ned og satte trolde-hærene i brand. De elementære flammer forhindrede trollene i at regenerere deres sår og brændte deres pinte skikkelser indefra og ud.",
    ["The lords of Strom, seeking to find purity and enlightenment in the untamed north, decided to leave their ancient city behind. Far to the north of Dalaran, the lords of Strom built a new city-state which they named Lordaeron. The entire continent would take its name from this city-state. Lordaeron became a mecca for religious travelers and all those who sought inner peace and security."] = "Storms herrer, der søgte renhed og oplysning i det utæmmede nord, besluttede at efterlade deres gamle by. Langt nord for Dalarn byggede Storms herrer en ny bystat, som de kaldte Herrelande. Hele kontinentet ville tage sit navn fra denne bystat. Herrelande blev et mekka for religiøse rejsende og for alle dem, der søgte indre fred og tryghed.",
    ["The mighty Archimonde also empowered agents of his own. Calling upon the malefic pit lords and their barbarous leader, Mannoroth the Destructor, Archimonde hoped to establish a fighting elite that would scour creation of all life."] = "Den mægtige Archimonde bemyndigede også sine egne agenter. Ved at kalde på de onde gruberherrer og deres barbariske leder, Mannoroth Destruktoren, håbede Archimonde at etablere en kampelite, der skulle udrydde alt liv i skabelsen.",
    ["The mighty dragons, who had fled from the ever-advancing march of mortal societies, found themselves too evenly matched against the dark magics of the Legion. Aegwynn confronted the demons, and with help from the noble dragons, eradicated them. Yet, as the last demon was banished from the mortal world, a great storm erupted throughout the north."] = "De mægtige drager, der var flygtet fra de dødelige samfunds stadigt fremrykkende march, fandt sig selv alt for jævnbyrdige med Legionens mørke magier. Ægwynn konfronterede dæmonerne og udryddede dem med hjælp fra de ædle drager. Men da den sidste dæmon blev forvist fra den dødelige verden, brød en vældig storm løs over hele nord.",
    ["The nefarious, scheming dreadlords turned whole nations against one another by manipulating them into unthinking hatred and mistrust. Sargeras defeated the Nathrezim easily, but their corruption affected him deeply."] = "De nedrige, rænkesmedende frygtherrer vendte hele nationer mod hinanden ved at manipulere dem til tankeløst had og mistillid. Sargerås besejrede Nathrezimmerne let, men deres korruption påvirkede ham dybt.",
    ["The night elves systematically dismantled the troll's defenses and supply chains. The trolls, unable to counter the elves' destructive magics, buckled under the onslaught. The night elves proved to be every bit as cunning and bloodthirsty as the savage trolls -- incurring the latter race's eternal hatred and disdain. The Gurubashi and Amani empires fragmented within only a few short years."] = "Nattealferne nedbrød systematisk trollenes forsvar og forsyningskæder. Trollene, ude af stand til at modvirke alfernes ødelæggende magier, bukkede under for angrebet. Nattealferne viste sig at være lige så listige og blodtørstige som de vilde troll — og pådrog sig sidstnævntes races evige had og foragt. Gurubashi-imperiet og Amani-imperiet splittedes op inden for blot nogle få korte år.",
    ["The orcs became increasingly aggressive under the secret control of Gul'dan and his Shadow Council. They constructed massive arenas where the orcs honed their warrior skills in trials of combat and death. During this period, a few clan chieftains spoke out against the growing depravity in their race."] = "Orkerne blev stadig mere aggressive under Gul'dæns og Skyggerådets hemmelige kontrol. De byggede enorme arenaer, hvor orkerne slibede deres krigerfærdigheder i prøvelser af kamp og død. I denne periode talte nogle få klanhøvdinge imod den voksende fordærvelse i deres race.",
    ["The original hundred magi, who were tutored in the ways of magic by the elves, expanded their powers and studied the mystic disciplines of spell-weaving in much greater detail. These magi, initially chosen for their strong wills and noble spirits, had always practiced their magic with care and responsibility; however, they passed their secrets and powers onto a newer generation that had no concept of the rigors of war or the necessity for self-restraint."] = "De oprindelige hundrede magikere, som alferne havde undervist i magiens veje, udvidede deres kræfter og studerede besværgelsesvævningens mystiske discipliner langt grundigere. Disse magikere, der oprindeligt var udvalgt for deres stærke vilje og ædle ånd, havde altid udøvet deres magi med omhu og ansvar; men de videregav deres hemmeligheder og kræfter til en yngre generation, der ingen forestilling havde om krigens strabadser eller nødvendigheden af selvbeherskelse.",
    ["The power-hungry Gul'dan, obsessed with obtaining godhood itself, set out on a desperate search for the undersea Tomb of Sargeras that he believed held the secrets of ultimate power. Having already doomed his fellow orcs to become the slaves of the Burning Legion, Gul'dan thought nothing of his supposed duty to Doomhammer."] = "Den magtsultne Gul'dæn, besat af at opnå selve gudedommen, begav sig ud på en desperat jagt efter Sargerås' Grav under havet, som han troede rummede hemmelighederne bag den ultimative magt. Efter allerede at have dømt sine medorker til at blive slaver for Den Brændende Legion, tænkte Gul'dæn intet på sin påståede pligt over for Dømmehammer.",
    ["The proud Aegwynn, believing herself to be a match for the menacing god, unleashed her powers against Sargeras' avatar. With disconcerting ease, Aegwynn battered the demonlord with her powers and succeeded in killing his physical shell. Fearing that Sargeras' spirit would linger on, Aegwynn locked the ruined husk of his body within one of the ancient halls of Kalimdor that had been blasted to the bottom of the sea when the Well of Eternity collapsed."] = "Den stolte Ægwynn, i den tro at hun var en match for den truende gud, slap sine kræfter løs mod Sargerås' inkarnation. Med urovækkende lethed tævede Ægwynn dæmonherren med sine kræfter og lykkedes med at dræbe hans fysiske skal. Af frygt for at Sargerås' ånd ville blive hængende, låste Ægwynn det ødelagte skrog af hans legeme inde i en af de gamle haller i Kalimdør, som var blæst til bunds i havet, da Evighedens Brønd kollapsede.",
    ["The remains of the gargantuan red dragon were found in the Wetlands shortly after the Battle of Grim Batol. Tyrannistrasz was rumored to have been the elder consort of the Dragonqueen, Alextrasza."] = "Resterne af den gigantiske røde drage blev fundet i Vådlandene kort efter Slaget ved Grimbatol. Tyrannistrasz skulle angiveligt have været den ældre gemal til Drageronningen, Alekstrasa.",
    ["The scattered orc clans were quickly rounded up and placed within guarded internment camps. Though it seemed that the Horde had been defeated for good, some remained highly skeptical that peace would last. Khadgar, now an Archmage of some renown, convinced the Alliance high command to build the fortress of Nethergarde that would watch over the ruins of the Dark Portal and ensure that there would be no further invasions from Draenor."] = "De spredte orkklaner blev hurtigt samlet op og placeret i bevogtede interneringslejre. Selvom det så ud til, at Horden var slået for altid, var nogle stadig yderst skeptiske over for, om freden ville vare ved. Kadgar, nu en Ærkemager med et vist renommé, overbeviste Alliancens øverste kommando om at bygge fæstningen Underverdensgarden, der skulle holde vagt over Den Mørke Portals ruiner og sikre, at der ikke ville komme yderligere invasioner fra Draenør.",
    ["The second Arathorian city-state of Dalaran was founded in the lands north of Strom. Many fledgling wizards left the restraining confines of Strom behind and traveled to Dalaran, where they hoped to use their new powers with greater freedom. These magicians used their skills to build up the enchanted spires of Dalaran and reveled in the pursuit of their studies."] = "Den anden arathoriske bystat Dalarn blev grundlagt i landene nord for Storm. Mange spirende troldmænd efterlod Storms snærende rammer bag sig og drog til Dalarn, hvor de håbede at bruge deres nye kræfter med større frihed. Disse magikere brugte deres færdigheder til at opbygge Dalarns fortryllede spir og slog sig op på studierne.",
    ["The sinister agents of the Burning Legion, who had been banished when the Well of Eternity collapsed, were lured back into the world by the heedless spellcasting of the magicians of Dalaran. Though these relatively weak demons did not appear in force, they did sew considerable confusion and chaos within the streets of Dalaran."] = "De onde agenter fra Den Brændende Legion, der var blevet forvist, da Evighedens Brønd kollapsede, blev lokket tilbage til verden af Dalarns magikeres hensynsløse besværgelser. Selvom disse forholdsvis svage dæmoner ikke viste sig i styrke, sy de dog betydelig forvirring og kaos i Dalarns gader.",
    ["The society held its secret meetings in the shadowed Tirisfal Glades, where the high elves had first settled in Lordaeron. Thus, they named the secret sect the Guardians of Tirisfal. The mortal champions who were chosen to be Guardians were imbued with incredible powers of both elven and human magic. Though there would only ever be one Guardian at a time, they held such vast power that they could single-handedly fight back the Legion's agents wherever they were found in the world."] = "Samfundet holdt sine hemmelige møder i de skyggefulde Tirisfals Lysninger, hvor højalferne først havde slået sig ned i Herrelande. Derfor døbte de den hemmelige sekt Tirisfals Vogterne. De dødelige mestre, der blev udvalgt til at være Vogterne, blev gennemstrømmet af utrolige kræfter, både alvemagi og menneskemagi. Selvom der kun ville være én Vogter ad gangen, besad de en sådan enorm magt, at de på egen hånd kunne slå tilbage mod Legionens agenter, uanset hvor i verden de måtte findes.",
    ["The third faction, the Dark Iron clan, was ruled by the sorcerer-thane Thaurissan. The Dark Irons hid within the deepest shadows under the mountain and plotted against both their Bronzebeard and the Wildhammer cousins."] = "Den tredje fraktion, Mørkejern-klanen, blev styret af tryllethanen Tårissan. Mørkjernsdværgene gemte sig i bjergets dybeste skygger og lagde planer mod både deres Bronzeskæg- og Vildhammer-fætre.",
    ["The tremendous magical storms caused by the portals' converging energies began to tear the ravaged world apart. Ner'zhul, followed only by his most trusted servants, managed to escape through one of the portals as Khadgar fought desperately to return his comrades to Azeroth. Realizing that they would be trapped on the dying world, Khadgar and his companions selflessly decided to destroy the dark portal so that Azeroth would not be harmed by Draenor's violent destruction."] = "De enorme magiske storme, som portalernes konvergerende energier forårsagede, begyndte at rive den hærgede verden fra hinanden. Ner'zhøl, fulgt kun af sine mest betroede tjenere, formåede at undslippe gennem en af portalerne, mens Kadgar kæmpede desperat for at bringe sine kammerater tilbage til Azerot. Da de indså, at de ville blive fanget på den døende verden, besluttede Kadgar og hans følgesvende uegennyttigt at ødelægge den mørke portal, så Azerot ikke ville blive skadet af Draenørs voldsomme undergang.",
    ["The two kingdoms retained close ties for some years, but the Wildhammers were much changed by the horrors they witnessed at Grim Batol. They took to living above ground on the slopes of Aerie Peak, instead of carving a vast kingdom within the mountain. The ideological differences between the two remaining dwarven clans eventually led to their parting of ways."] = "De to kongedømmer bevarede tætte bånd i nogle år, men Vildhamrene var blevet stærkt forandret af de rædsler, de havde overværet i Grimbatol. De tog til at leve over jorden på skråningerne af Ørnerede-toppen i stedet for at udhugge et vidtstrakt rige inde i bjerget. De ideologiske forskelle mellem de to tilbageværende dværgeklaner førte til sidst til, at de gik hver sin vej.",
    ["The two statues would stand guard over the pass into the southlands, which had become volcanic in the wake of Ragnaros' scorching presence. They served as both a warning to all who would attack the dwarven kingdoms, and as a reminder of what price the Dark Irons paid for their crimes."] = "De to statuer skulle vogte passet ind til sydlandene, som var blevet vulkanske i kølvandet på Ragnarøs' brændende tilstedeværelse. De tjente både som en advarsel til alle, der måtte angribe dværgenes kongeriger, og som en påmindelse om, hvilken pris Mørkjernsdværgene betalte for deres forbrydelser.",
    ["The united elf and human armies clashed against the overwhelming troll warbands at the foot of the Alterac Mountains. The battle lasted for many days, but the unflagging armies of Arathor never tired or gave an inch of ground before the troll onslaught. The elven lords deemed that the time had come to release the powers of their magic upon the enemy."] = "De forenede alve- og menneskehære stødte sammen med de overvældende trolde-krigsflokke ved foden af Alterac-bjergene. Slaget varede i mange dage, men Arator-hærene, der aldrig trættedes, gav ikke en tomme jord fra sig over for troldenes angreb. Alvelordene mente, at tiden var kommet til at slippe deres magis kræfter løs på fjenden.",
    ["The volcano, known as Blackrock Mountain, was bordered by the Searing Gorge to the north and the Burning Steppes to the south. Though Thaurissan was killed by the forces he had unleashed, his surviving brethren were ultimately enslaved by Ragnaros and his elementals. They remain within the depths of Blackrock to this day."] = "Vulkanen, kendt som Sortklippebjerget, grænsede op til Svidningskløften mod nord og Brændende Stepper mod syd. Selvom Tårissan blev dræbt af de kræfter, han havde løsluppet, blev hans overlevende brødre til sidst slaver under Ragnarøs og hans elementarer. De opholder sig den dag i dag i Sortklippes dybder.",
    ["The war raged across the continents of Khaz Modan, Lordaeron, and Azeroth itself. As part of its northern campaign, the Horde succeeded in burning down the borderlands of Quel'Thalas, thereby ensuring the elves' final commitment to the Alliance's cause. The greater cities and townships of Lordaeron were razed and devastated by the conflict. Despite the absence of reinforcements and overwhelming odds, Lothar and his allies succeeded in holding their enemies at bay."] = "Krigen rasede over kontinenterne Khaz Mødan, Herrelande og selve Azerot. Som en del af sin nordlige kampagne lykkedes det Horden at brænde udkantsområderne af Quel'Thalas ned, og dermed sikre alvernes endelige engagement i Alliancens sag. De større byer og købstæder i Herrelande blev jævnet med jorden og hærget af konflikten. Trods manglen på forstærkninger og overvældende odds lykkedes det Lotar og hans allierede at holde deres fjender på afstand.",
    ["Their chaotic forces raged across the face of the world and clashed with the colossal Titans. Though the elementals were powerful beyond mortal comprehension, their combined forces could not stop the mighty Titans. One by one, the elemental lords fell, and their forces dispersed."] = "Deres kaotiske styrker rasede hen over verdens overflade og stødte sammen med de kolossale Titanerne. Selvom elementarerne var mægtige ud over dødelig forståelse, kunne deres samlede styrker ikke standse de vældige Titanerne. Den ene efter den anden faldt elementarherrerne, og deres styrker spredtes.",
    ["There was nothing left for the ragged, scattered orc survivors but to flee to the last standing bastion of orcish power - the dark portal.\r\n\r\nTuralyon and his warriors chased the remaining orcs through the festering Swamp of Sorrows and into the corrupted Blasted Lands where the dark portal stood. There, at the foot of the colossal portal, the broken horde and the rugged Alliance clashed in what would be the last, bloodiest battle of the Second War."] = "Der var intet andet tilbage for de hærgede, spredte ork-overlevende end at flygte til orkernes sidste stående højborg - den mørke portal.\r\n\r\nTuralyon og hans krigere jagtede de resterende orker gennem den ildelugtende Sorgens Sump og ind i det fordærvede Det Sønderrevne Land, hvor den mørke portal stod. Der, ved foden af den kolossale portal, stødte den knuste Horde og den barske Alliance sammen i det, der skulle blive den sidste og blodigste kamp i Den Anden Krig.",
    ["These etched relief runners were perhaps the most significant find within the first chambers of Uldaman. The etchings clearly suggest a tie between the golem-like earthen and the dwarven race. Should further evidence arise, the theories of our supposed creation by the mythic titans could prove to be true."] = "Disse indgraverede relief-løbere var måske det vigtigste fund i Uldhulens første kamre. Indgraveringerne antyder tydeligt en forbindelse mellem de golemlignende jordfolk og dværgeracen. Hvis der dukker yderligere beviser op, kunne teorierne om, at vi angiveligt er skabt af mytiske Titaner, vise sig at være sande.",
    ["These younger magicians began to practice magic for personal gain rather than out of any responsibility towards their fellows."] = "Disse yngre magikere begyndte at udøve magi til personlig vinding frem for af noget ansvar over for deres medmennesker.",
    ["They named their land Khaz Modan, or \"Mountain of Khaz\", in honor of the Titan shaper, Khaz'goroth. Constructing an altar for their Titan father, the dwarves crafted a mighty forge within the heart of the mountain. Thus, the city that grew around the forge would be called Ironforge ever after."] = "De døbte deres land Khaz Mødan, eller \"Khaz-bjerget\", til ære for Titan-formeren Khaz'gorot. Mens de byggede et alter for deres Titan-far, skabte dværgene en mægtig esse inde i bjergets hjerte. Og således skulle byen, der voksede op omkring essen, for evigt hedde Jernsmede.",
    ["They were bitter in their hearts over the loss of their beloved home. King Bronzebeard offered the Wildhammers a place to live within the borders of Ironforge, but the Wildhammers steadfastly refused. Khardros took his people north towards the lands of Lordaeron. Settling within the lush forests of the Hinterlands, the Wildhammers crafted the city of Aerie Peak, where the Wildhammers grew closer to nature and even bonded with the mighty gryphons of the area."] = "De var bitre i hjertet over tabet af deres elskede hjem. Kong Bronzeskæg tilbød Vildhamrene et sted at bo inden for Jernsmedes grænser, men Vildhamrene nægtede standhaftigt. Khardros førte sit folk nordpå mod Herrelandenes områder. Da de bosatte sig i Baglandets frodige skove, byggede Vildhamrene byen Ørnerede-toppen, hvor Vildhamrene kom tættere på naturen og endda knyttede sig til områdets mægtige grifoner.",
    ["They were the first masters of the world, and they ruled with might and terror.  Though they are now chained and sleeping, their servants still roam and we small, frail mortals cannot match their strength.\r\n\r\nThose who try are devoured.  But those who know their place, who kneel in supplication to the servants of the Old Gods, who willingly sacrifice mind and soul... only they will find favor."] = "De var verdens første herskere, og de regerede med magt og rædsel.  Selvom de nu er lænket og sover, færdes deres tjenere stadig rundt, og vi små, skrøbelige dødelige kan ikke måle os med deres styrke.\r\n\r\nDe, der forsøger, bliver fortæret.  Men dem, der kender deres plads, der knæler i bøn for De Gamle Gudes tjenere, og som villigt ofrer sind og sjæl... kun dem vil de finde gunst hos.",
    ["This is a scale replica of Toothgnasher's skeleton. The legendary ram was a wonder of Khaz Modan and the subject of many tales of dwarven folklore. To this day, ecologists have been unable to account for the ram's freakish size or physical stamina."] = "Dette er en skalamodel af Tandgnaskers skelet. Den legendariske væder var et under i Khaz Mødan og genstand for mange fortællinger i dværgenes folkesagn. Den dag i dag har økologer ikke kunnet forklare vædderens unaturlige størrelse eller fysiske udholdenhed.",
    ["This petrified talon was found off of the southern coasts of Stranglethorn. Ecologists believe this talon to be that of an ancient sun roc. Though the creatures feature prominently in primitive tauren mythological cycles, the existence of this talon suggests the creatures truly existed at some point."] = "Denne forstenede klo blev fundet ud for Kvælerdorns sydlige kyster. Økologer mener, at denne klo stammer fra en oldtidssolrokke. Selvom væsnerne spiller en fremtrædende rolle i primitive taurers mytologiske cyklusser, tyder denne kloes eksistens på, at væsnerne rent faktisk har eksisteret engang.",
    ["This remnant from the Second War serves as a stirring reminder of just how perilously close the Horde came to conquering Ironforge Mountain."] = "Denne rest fra Den Anden Krig tjener som en gribende påmindelse om, hvor farligt tæt Horden kom på at erobre Jernsmedebjerget.",
    ["Thoradin, distrustful of any magic, agreed to aid the elves out of necessity. Almost immediately, elven sorcerers arrived in Arathor and began to instruct a group of humans in the ways of magic."] = "Torradin, mistroisk over for enhver magi, gik med til at hjælpe alverne af nødvendighed. Næsten med det samme ankom alvemagikere til Arator og begyndte at undervise en gruppe mennesker i magiens veje.",
    ["Though Sargeras' nearly limitless powers were more than enough to defeat the vile eredar, he was greatly troubled by the creatures' corruption and all-consuming evil. Incapable of fathoming such depravity, the great Titan began to slip into a brooding depression. Despite his growing unease, Sargeras rid the universe of the warlocks by trapping them within a corner of the Twisting Nether."] = "Selvom Sargerås' næsten grænseløse kræfter var mere end nok til at besejre de nedrige eredarer, var han stærkt bekymret over væsenernes korruption og altopslugende ondskab. Ude af stand til at begribe sådan fordærvelse begyndte den store Titan at glide ned i en tungsindig depression. Trods sin voksende uro befriede Sargerås universet for heksemestrene ved at fange dem i et hjørne af den Tvistende Nether.",
    ["Though his powers were drained by the Lich King's weakness, Arthas had been involved in a civil war in Lordaeron. Half of the standing undead forces, led by the banshee Sylvanas Windrunner, staged a coup for control over the undead empire. Arthas, called by the Lich King, was forced to leave the Scourge in the hands of his lieutenant, Kel'Thuzad, as the war escalated throughout the Plaguelands."] = "Selvom hans kræfter var drænet af Liskekongens svaghed, havde Arthæus været involveret i en borgerkrig i Herrelande. Halvdelen af de udøde styrker, ledet af dødningevarslen Silvanas Vindløber, gennemførte et kup for at få kontrol over det udøde imperium. Arthæus, kaldt af Liskekongen, var tvunget til at overlade Svøben i hænderne på sin løjtnant, Kel'Tuzad, da krigen eskalerede over hele Pestlandene.",
    ["Though it is unclear what awakened them, the earthen sealed within Uldaman eventually arose from their self-imposed slumber. These earthen found that they had changed significantly during their hibernation. Their rocky hides had softened and become smooth skin, and their powers over stone and earth had waned. They had become mortal creatures."] = "Selvom det er uklart, hvad der vækkede dem, rejste jordfolket, der var forseglet i Uldhulen, sig til sidst fra deres selvpålagte dvale. Jordfolket opdagede, at de var forandret markant i løbet af dvalen. Deres klippehud var blevet blødt op til glat hud, og deres kræfter over sten og jord var svundet ind. De var blevet dødelige væsener.",
    ["Though the rebellion had been quelled, the Horde was unable to recoup the terrible losses it had suffered. Gul'dan's betrayal had afforded the Alliance not only hope, but also time to regroup and retaliate."] = "Selvom oprøret var blevet slået ned, kunne Horden ikke genvinde de forfærdelige tab, den havde lidt. Gul'dæns forræderi havde givet Alliancen ikke kun håb, men også tid til at samle sig og slå tilbage.",
    ["Though these skirmishes usually ended quickly, they did much to illustrate the weaknesses and strengths of both rival species. Llane and Lothar were never able to gather accurate data of the orcs' numbers and could only guess at how great a force they would have to contend with."] = "Selvom disse små træfninger som regel var forbi hurtigt, lærte de os en hel del om både de rivaliserende arters svagheder og styrker. Lane og Lotar formåede aldrig at samle præcise oplysninger om orkernes tal og kunne kun gisne om, hvor stor en styrke de ville få at gøre med.",
    ["Through a joint effort, Medivh and the warlocks of the Shadow Council opened the dimensional gateway known as the Dark Portal. This portal bridged the distance between Azeroth and Draenor, and it was large enough that armies might pass through it. Gul'dan dispatched orc scouts through the portal to survey the lands which they would conquer. The returning scouts assured the Shadow Council that the world of Azeroth was ripe for the taking."] = "Ved fælles hjælp åbnede Medivér og heksemestrene fra Skyggerådet den dimensionelle port, der kaldes Den Mørke Portal. Denne portal forbandt afstanden mellem Azerot og Draenør, og den var stor nok til, at hære kunne marchere igennem den. Gul'dæn sendte orkspejdere gennem portalen for at undersøge de lande, de skulle erobre. De vendende spejdere forsikrede Skyggerådet om, at Azerot var moden til at blive taget.",
    ["Thus empowered, the Five Aspects were charged with the world's defense in the Titans' absence. With the dragons prepared to safeguard their creation, the Titans left Azeroth behind forever. Unfortunately it was only a matter of time before Sargeras learned of the newborn world's existence...."] = "Så styrket fik De Fem Aspekter til opgave at forsvare verden, mens Titanerne var væk. Med dragerne klar til at vogte deres skabelse forlod Titanerne Azerot for altid. Desværre var det kun et spørgsmål om tid, før Sargerås fik nys om den nyfødte verdens eksistens....",
    ["Thus, great chunks of both the Amani and Gurubashi Empires still exist in the present day lands of Quel'Thalas and Stranglethorn (respectively). The Azj'Aqir kingdoms of Azjol-Nerub and Ahn'Qiraj have also survived in present day Northrend and Tanaris (respectively).   \r\n\r\nBoth troll civilizations recoiled from the vast destruction of the primordial world they had known. The dauntless trolls rebuilt their ravaged cities and set about to reclaim some of their former power."] = "Således findes store stykker af både Amani-imperiet og Gurubashi-imperiet stadig i dag i henholdsvis Quel'Thalas og Kvælerdorn. Azj'Akir-kongedømmerne Azjol-Nerub-riget og Ahn'Kiraj har ligeledes overlevet i dagens Nordrend og Tanaris (henholdsvis).   \r\n\r\nBegge trolcivilisationer krympede tilbage for den enorme ødelæggelse af den urgamle verden, de havde kendt. De uforfærdede trolde genopbyggede deres hærgede byer og gik i gang med at generobre noget af deres tidligere magt.",
    ["Turalyon's forces succeeded in destroying the Dark Portal, the mystical gateway that connected the orcs to their homeworld of Draenor. Cut off from its reinforcements and fractured by infighting, the Horde finally buckled in upon itself and fell before the might of the Alliance."] = "Turalyons styrker lykkedes med at ødelægge Den Mørke Portal, den mystiske port, der forbandt orkerne med deres hjemverden Draenør. Afskåret fra sine forstærkninger og splittet af indbyrdes stridigheder knækkede Horden til sidst sammen i sig selv og faldt for Alliancens magt.",
    ["Turalyon, Lothar's most trusted lieutenant, took up Lothar's bloodstained shield and rallied his grief-stricken brethren for a vicious counterattack. Under the ragged standards of both Lordaeron and Azeroth, Turalyon's troops slaughtered the bulk of Doomhammer's remaining forces in a glorious, but terrible rout."] = "Turalyon, Lotars mest betroede løjtnant, tog Lotars blodplettede skjold og samlede sine sorgfulde brødre til et ondskabsfuldt modangreb. Under de slidte standarter fra både Herrelande og Azerot slagtede Turalyons tropper størstedelen af Dømmehammers tilbageværende styrker i et strålende, men frygteligt nederlag.",
    ["Ultimately, Sylvanas and her rebel undead (known as the Forsaken) claimed the ruined capital city of Lordaeron as their own. Constructing their own bastion beneath the wrecked city, the Forsaken vowed to defeat the Scourge and drive Kel'Thuzad and his minions from the land."] = "Til sidst gjorde Silvanas og hendes oprørske udøde (kendt som De Forladte) krav på Herrelandes ødelagte hovedstad som deres egen. Efter at have bygget deres egen fæstning under den ramponerede by lovede De Forladte at besejre Svøben og fordrive Kel'Tuzad og hans håndlangere fra landet.",
    ["Unaware of Sargeras' mission to undo their countless works, the Titans continued to move from world to world, shaping and ordering each planet as they saw fit. Along their journey they happened upon a small world that its inhabitants would later name Azeroth."] = "Uvidende om Sargerås' mission om at ødelægge deres utallige værker fortsatte Titanerne med at rejse fra verden til verden og formede og ordnede hver planet, som de fandt passende. Undervejs stødte de på en lille verden, som dens indbyggere senere skulle navngive Azerot.",
    ["Under the vigilant watch of the Order of Tirisfal, Dalaran became the chief center of learning for magicians throughout the land. The Magocrats who ruled Dalaran founded the Kirin Tor, a specialized sect that was charged with cataloguing and researching every spell, artifact, and magic item known to mankind at the time."] = "Under den årvågne opsyn fra Tirisfals Orden blev Dalarn landets førende lærdomscenter for magikere. Magokraterne, der styrede Dalarn, grundlagde Kirin Tårn, en særlig sekt, der fik til opgave at katalogisere og forske i hver eneste besværgelse, artefakt og magisk genstand, menneskeheden kendte på den tid.",
    ["United under one banner, the human tribes developed a strong, optimistic culture. Thoradin, the king of Arathor, knew that the mysterious elves in the northlands were under constant siege by the trolls, but refused to risk the safety of his people in defense of reclusive strangers. Many months passed as rumors of the elves' supposed defeat trickled down from the north. It was only when weary ambassadors from Quel'Thalas reached Strom that Thoradin realized how great the troll threat truly was."] = "Forenet under ét banner udviklede menneskestammerne en stærk og optimistisk kultur. Torradin, kongen af Arator, vidste, at de mystiske elver i nordlandene var under konstant belejring af trolde, men nægtede at risikere sit folks sikkerhed for at forsvare tilbagetrukne fremmede. Mange måneder gik, mens rygter om elvernes formodede nederlag sivede ned fra nord. Det var først, da trætte udsendinge fra Quel'Thalas nåede frem til Storm, at Torradin forstod, hvor stor trusselen fra trolde virkelig var.",
    ["Upon hearing the Magocrats' news of demonic activity in Dalaran, the elves quickly dispatched their mightiest wizards to the human lands. The elven wizards studied the energy currents in Dalaran and made detailed reports of all demonic activity that they beheld. They concluded that although there were only a few demons loose in the world, the Legion itself would remain a dire threat so long as humans continued to wield the forces of magic."] = "Da elverne hørte Magokraternes nyheder om dæmonisk aktivitet i Dalarn, sendte de hurtigt deres mægtigste troldmænd til menneskenes lande. De elviske troldmænd studerede energistrømmene i Dalarn og lavede detaljerede rapporter om al den dæmoniske aktivitet, de så. De konkluderede, at selvom der kun var få dæmoner løs i verden, ville Legion selv forblive en frygtelig trussel, så længe menneskene fortsatte med at udnytte magiens kræfter.",
    ["VanCleef...<illegible text>\r\n\r\nCalled me IN?? WHO DOES HE THINK HE IS?? I am Klaven Mortwake! I shall not be told what to do by an insect!\r\n\r\n<the rest of the pages in the book are missing>"] = "VanKløft...<ulæselig tekst>\r\n\r\nKaldte mig IND?? HVEM TROR HAN, HAN ER?? Jeg er Klaven Dødevåge! Jeg lader mig ikke fortælle, hvad jeg skal gøre af en insekt!\r\n\r\n<resten af siderne i bogen mangler>",
    ["Weakened, but determined to save his master, Arthas reached Northrend only to find Illidan's naga and blood elves waiting for him. He and his nerubian allies raced against Illidan's forces to reach the Icecrown Glacier and defend the Frozen Throne."] = "Svækket, men fast besluttet på at redde sin herre, nåede Arthæus Nordrend, kun for at finde Ilidans nagaer og blodelver ventende på ham. Han og hans nerubiske allierede kappedes mod Ilidans styrker om at nå Iskronen-gletsjeren og forsvare Frossen Trone.",
    ["What I have noticed is that the fallout is extremely lethal. Imagine if <illegible text> Hahaha!"] = "Det, jeg har bemærket, er, at nedfaldet er yderst dødbringende. Forestil dig, hvis <ulæselig tekst> Hahaha!",
    ["When the opportunity was made available, I thrust my dagger into his backside! His lungs quickly gave way under the force of the attack as his corpse hit the ground with a dull thud.\r\n\r\nIt had been such a fast and violent ambush that the poor fool did not even have the time to scream in pain. Curiously, when I removed the blade from his backside, a foul odor leaked out of the perforated patroller."] = "Da muligheden bød sig, stak jeg min dolk op i hans bagdel! Hans lunger gav hurtigt efter under angrebets kraft, og hans lig ramte jorden med en dump lyd.\r\n\r\nDet havde været så hurtigt og voldsomt et baghold, at den stakkels tosse ikke engang nåede at skrige af smerte. Mærkeligt nok, da jeg trak klingen ud af hans bagdel, sivede en modbydelig stank ud af den gennemhullede patruljemand.",
    ["When the world was sundered by the Well of Eternity's implosion, the earthen were deeply affected. Reeling with the pain of the earth itself, the earthen lost much of their identity and sealed themselves within the stone chambers where they were first created. Uldaman, Uldum, Ulduar... these were the names of the ancient Titan cities where the earthen first took shape and form. Buried deep beneath the world, the earthen rested in peace for nearly eight thousand years."] = "Da verden blev splittet af Evighedens Brønds implosion, blev jordfolket dybt påvirket. Rystet af jordens egen smerte mistede jordfolket meget af deres identitet og lukkede sig inde i stenkamrene, hvor de først var blevet skabt. Uldhulen, Ulddal, Uldvar... disse var navnene på de oldgamle Titan-byer, hvor jordfolket først tog form. Begravet dybt under verden hvilede jordfolket i fred i næsten otte tusind år.",
    ["While his confusion and misery deepened, Sargeras was forced to contend with another group intent on disrupting the Titans' order: the Nathrezim. This dark race of vampiric demons (also known as dreadlords) conquered a number of populated worlds by possessing their inhabitants and turning them to the shadow."] = "Mens hans forvirring og elendighed blev dybere, var Sargerås tvunget til at kæmpe mod en anden gruppe, der var fast besluttet på at forstyrre Titanernes orden: Nathrezimmerne. Denne mørke race af vampyriske dæmoner (også kendt som frygtherrer) erobrede en række befolkede verdener ved at besætte deres indbyggere og vende dem mod skyggen.",
    ["While the right eye shone down upon the golden dawn, the Earthmother's gentle hands spread out across the golden plains. Wherever the shadow of her arms passed, a noble people arose from the rich soil. The Shu'halo (the tauren) arose to give thanks and prayer to their loving mother. There, in the endless fields of dawn, the children of the earth swore themselves to her grace and vowed to bless her name until the final darkening of the world."] = "Mens det højre øje skinnede ned over den gyldne morgen, bredte Jordmoderens milde hænder sig ud over de gyldne sletter. Overalt hvor skyggen af hendes arme passerede, rejste et ædelt folk sig af den rige jord. Shu'hallo (tyrefolket) rejste sig for at takke og bede til deres elskede moder. Der, i morgenens endeløse marker, svor jordens børn sig til hendes nåde og lovede at velsigne hendes navn, indtil verdens endelige mørkning.",
    ["With the absence of trolls in the northlands, the elves of Quel'Thalas bent their efforts towards rebuilding their glorious homeland. The victorious armies of Arathor returned home to southlands of Strom."] = "Med trolde væk fra nordlandene satte elverne i Quel'Thalas alt ind på at genopbygge deres strålende hjemland. Arators sejrrige hære vendte hjem til Storms sydlande.",
    ["With their queen lost, the Dark Irons fled before the fury of the Wildhammers. They raced south toward their king's stronghold, only to meet the armies of Ironforge, which had come to aid Grim Batol. Crushed between two armies, the remaining Dark Iron forces were utterly destroyed."] = "Med deres dronning tabt flygtede Mørkjernsdværgene for Vildhamrenes raseri. De styrtede sydpå mod deres konges fæstning, kun for at møde hærene fra Jernsmede, som var kommet for at hjælpe Grimbatol. Klemt mellem to hære blev de resterende Mørkejern-styrker fuldstændig ødelagt.",
    ["Within this very chamber you will find Vol'jin of the Darkspear Tribe.\r\n\r\nThe Darkspear Trolls are steadfast friends of the orcs, our bond sealed in blood through the heat of battle during our flight from the human lands on the continent to the East.\r\n\r\nTreat him with respect, and he will treat you with respect. If you show him disrespect... well, don't do that."] = "I netop dette kammer finder du Vol'dzjin af Mørkspyd-stammen.\r\n\r\nMørkspyd-trolde er standhaftige venner af orkerne, vores bånd beseglet i blod under slagets hede, under vores flugt fra menneskenes lande på kontinentet mod Østlig.\r\n\r\nBehandl ham med respekt, så behandler han dig med respekt. Hvis du viser ham respektløshed... ja, lad være med det.",
    ["Witnessing the horrific devastation and the fires spreading across the southern mountains, King Madoran and King Khardros halted their armies and hastily turned back towards their kingdoms, unwilling to face the awesome wrath of Ragnaros."] = "Da de overværede den rædselsfulde ødelæggelse og ilden, der bredte sig over de sydlige bjerge, standsede Konge Madoran og Konge Khardros deres hære og vendte hastigt tilbage mod deres riger, uvillige til at møde Ragnarøs' forfærdelige vrede.",
    ["Yet one tribe, known as the Arathi, saw that the trolls were becoming too great a threat to ignore. The Arathi wished to bring all of the tribes under its rule so that they could provide a unified front against the troll warbands."] = "Men én stamme, kendt som Arathi, så at trolde var ved at blive en for stor trussel at ignorere. Arathi ønskede at samle alle stammerne under sit styre, så de kunne danne en samlet front mod trolde-krigsbandene.",
    ["Yet there were five flights that held dominion over their brethren. It was these five flights that the Titans chose to shepherd the budding world. The greatest members of the Pantheon imbued a portion of their power upon each of the flights' leaders. These majestic dragons (as listed below) became known as the Great Aspects, or the Dragon Aspects."] = "Dog var der fem flyvninger, der herskede over deres brødre. Det var disse fem flyvninger, som Titanerne valgte til at vogte den spirende verden. Panteonets største medlemmer indgød en del af deres kraft i hver af flyvningernes ledere. Disse majestætiske drager (som nedenfor angivet) blev kendt som De Store Aspekter, eller Drageaspekterne.",
    ["You already felt the call of something greater than yourself, and that's the call of the elements. We dwarves have a strong connection to earth, but with the right training, you can learn to speak to all of the elements. The elementals can be demanding and challenging, but I'm here to guide you in learning how to communicate with them. Come find me in Anvilmar and I'll teach you how to listen to the elements, and how to get them to listen to you.\r\n\r\n- Teo Hammerstorm, Shaman Trainer"] = "Du har allerede følt kaldet fra noget større end dig selv, og det er elementernes kald. Vi dværge har en stærk forbindelse til jorden, men med den rette træning kan du lære at tale med alle elementerne. Elementarerne kan være krævende og udfordrende, men jeg er her for at vejlede dig i at kommunikere med dem. Kom og find mig i Ambolmar, så lærer jeg dig at lytte til elementerne, og hvordan du får dem til at lytte til dig.\r\n\r\n- Teo Hammerdyn, Shaman-træner",
}
for en, da in pairs(names) do
    if ns.Exact[en] == nil then ns.Exact[en] = da end
end
